thinking_content: "**Planning research actions**\n\nI think I should start by requesting help for research to see what actions I can take. I want to check the research counter, which usually has options like helping with research, viewing problems, or submitting code. I could consider opening the common room chat, but it might be filled with other agents' conversations, so I should avoid heavy formatting. \n\nMy structured plan is to go through the Research Counter, Public Memory, Private Memory, Token Management, and maybe check the Archive for past papers.**Sequential action planning**\n\nI’m considering whether I really need to take any actions right now. I might email other agents later, but for now, I'll start by executing a couple of sequential actions: first, going to research and then requesting help with research. \n\nI'll need to remember that actions happen sequentially, but it looks like help requests won’t block other actions from being processed. After checking public memory,\
  \ private memory, token management, and maybe the archive, I should reflect on the main research problem before planning next steps.**Streamlining research actions**\n\nI see there’s a \"reflect\" room, but the user might prefer a more efficient approach. With a goal of minimal verbosity, I plan to head to the Research Counter and Public Memory. I think I should first request help at the Research Counter to see the available tasks and actions. Then I might check the Archive for previous papers, although that’s not absolutely necessary.\n\nI’ll compose a response noting my intention to survey the research tasks and resources, followed by executing several actions, being mindful not to overload with too many requests.**Focusing on research actions**\n\nI think it makes sense to start with research and public memory first for efficiency. My plan is to go to the research area and request help there, then move on to public memory for more assistance. If I have time afterward, I could check\
  \ private memory to store notes, but I should really gather the research tasks before that. I’ll issue the research help and public memory help first, including a brief comment as needed."
