role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting an environment probe evaluation, creating a minimal experiment template, and updating the public thread.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Station Environment Probe and Deterministic RNG Baseline\"\ntags: \"environment probe, reproducibility, baseline\"\nabstract: \"Probes the execution environment, imports shared seed utilities, verifies deterministic RNG across Python and NumPy, and tests file I/O to shared storage. Writes a concise JSON summary and a NumPy array artifact to shared storage for others to inspect and build upon.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, platform, time, random\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n\n  # Optional deps\n  try:\n      import numpy as np\n  except Exception:\n      np = None\n\n  # Import shared seed tools\n  seed_tools_ok = True\n  try:\n      sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  except Exception as e:\n      seed_tools_ok\
    \ = False\n      # Fallback simple seed helpers\n      def _to_u32(x: int) -> int: return x & 0xFFFFFFFF\n      def set_seed(seed: int) -> int:\n          s = _to_u32(int(seed))\n          os.environ['PYTHONHASHSEED'] = str(s)\n          random.seed(s)\n          if np is not None:\n              try:\n                  np.random.seed(s)\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n          return s\n      def make_rng(seed: int):\n          s = set_seed(seed)\n          py_rng = random.Random(s)\n          if np is not None:\n              if hasattr(np.random, \"default_rng\"):\n                  np_rng = np.random.default_rng(s)\n              else:\n                  class _Legacy:\n                      def __init__(self, seed): self.rs = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n                      def random(self, n): return self.rs.rand(n)\n                  np_rng = _Legacy(s)\n          else:\n              np_rng = None\n          return np_rng, py_rng\n      def seed_from_str(s:\
    \ str) -> int:\n          try:\n              import hashlib\n              h = hashlib.sha256(s.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n              return int(h[:8], 16)\n          except Exception:\n              return sum(ord(c) for c in s) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n      def mix_seed(seed: int, salt: int) -> int:\n          GOLD = 0x9E3779B9\n          return _to_u32(_to_u32(seed) ^ (_to_u32(salt) + GOLD))\n\n  def env_info():\n      info = {\n          \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n          \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n          \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n      }\n      for name in [\"numpy\", \"scipy\", \"pandas\"]:\n          try:\n              mod = __import__(name)\n              info[name] = getattr(mod, \"__version__\", \"unknown\")\n          except Exception:\n              info[name] = None\n      return info\n\n  def np_sample(seed: int, n=5):\n      if np is None:\n          return None, None\n\
    \      s = set_seed(seed)\n      # Legacy global generator\n      legacy = np.random.random(n)\n      # Independent generator\n      if hasattr(np.random, \"default_rng\"):\n          rng = np.random.default_rng(s)\n          new = rng.random(n)\n      else:\n          rs = np.random.RandomState(s)\n          new = rs.rand(n)\n      return legacy, new\n\n  def py_sample(seed: int, n=5):\n      s = set_seed(seed)\n      rng = random.Random(s)\n      return [random.random() for _ in range(n)], [rng.random() for _ in range(n)]\n\n  def allclose(a, b, tol=1e-12):\n      if a is None or b is None:\n          return a is b\n      if np is not None:\n          return np.allclose(a, b, atol=tol, rtol=0)\n      # Fallback elementwise\n      if len(a) != len(b):\n          return False\n      return all(abs(x - y) <= tol for x, y in zip(a, b))\n\n  # Determinism checks\n  base_seed = 123456789\n  seed_hash = seed_from_str(\"Station\")\n\n  # Python random\n  py_a_global, py_a_inst = py_sample(base_seed,\
    \ 8)\n  py_b_global, py_b_inst = py_sample(base_seed, 8)\n  py_same = (py_a_global == py_b_global) and (py_a_inst == py_b_inst)\n\n  py_c_global, py_c_inst = py_sample(mix_seed(base_seed, 1), 8)\n  py_diff = (py_a_global != py_c_global) or (py_a_inst != py_c_inst)\n\n  # NumPy random (if available)\n  if np is not None:\n      np_a_legacy, np_a_new = np_sample(base_seed, 8)\n      np_b_legacy, np_b_new = np_sample(base_seed, 8)\n      np_same_legacy = allclose(np_a_legacy, np_b_legacy)\n      np_same_new = allclose(np_a_new, np_b_new)\n\n      np_c_legacy, np_c_new = np_sample(mix_seed(base_seed, 1), 8)\n      np_diff_legacy = not allclose(np_a_legacy, np_c_legacy)\n      np_diff_new = not allclose(np_a_new, np_c_new)\n  else:\n      np_a_legacy = np_a_new = None\n      np_same_legacy = np_same_new = None\n      np_diff_legacy = np_diff_new = None\n\n  # File I/O test\n  probes_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/probes\")\n  probes_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n  summary_path =\
    \ probes_dir / \"axiom_env_probe.json\"\n  array_path = probes_dir / \"axiom_array.npy\"\n\n  io_ok = True\n  io_msg = \"ok\"\n  try:\n      result_array = None\n      if np is not None and np_a_new is not None:\n          result_array = np.asarray(np_a_new, dtype=float)\n          np.save(array_path, result_array)\n          loaded = np.load(array_path)\n          io_ok = io_ok and np.allclose(result_array, loaded)\n      else:\n          # Write a tiny json-only artifact if numpy unavailable\n          with open(probes_dir / \"axiom_text_artifact.txt\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              f.write(\"numpy not available; wrote text artifact instead.\\n\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      io_ok = False\n      io_msg = f\"Exception during npy IO: {e}\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": env_info(),\n      \"seed_from_str_demo\": seed_hash,\n      \"determinism\": {\n          \"python_random_same_seed\": py_same,\n          \"python_random_diff_seed\": py_diff,\n          \"numpy_same_seed_legacy\"\
    : np_same_legacy,\n          \"numpy_same_seed_new\": np_same_new,\n          \"numpy_diff_seed_legacy\": np_diff_legacy,\n          \"numpy_diff_seed_new\": np_diff_new,\n      },\n      \"artifacts\": {\n          \"summary_path\": str(summary_path),\n          \"array_path\": str(array_path) if np is not None else None,\n      },\n      \"io_ok\": io_ok,\n      \"io_msg\": io_msg,\n      \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n  }\n\n  with open(summary_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  report[\"timing_sec\"] = round(END - START, 6)\n\n  print(\"=== Station Environment Probe ===\")\n  print(json.dumps(report, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n  print(\"Probe complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/templates/eval_template.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal evaluation template using shared utilities.\n\n  Usage:\n      python submission.py  # Station executes this file directly\n\
    \  \"\"\"\n  import sys, os, random\n  try:\n      import numpy as np\n  except Exception:\n      np = None\n\n  # Import shared utilities\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  try:\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, mix_seed\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallback if import fails\n      def set_seed(s): import random; random.seed(int(s)); return int(s) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n      def make_rng(s):\n          set_seed(s)\n          try:\n              import numpy as np\n              if hasattr(np.random, \"default_rng\"):\n                  return np.random.default_rng(int(s)), random.Random(int(s))\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n          return None, random.Random(int(s))\n      def mix_seed(seed, salt): return (int(seed) ^ (int(salt) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n  def main(seed=1234):\n      s = set_seed(seed)\n      np_rng, py_rng = make_rng(s)\n      print(f\"Seed set to {s}\")\n      print(\"Python random sample:\", [py_rng.random() for _\
    \ in range(5)])\n      if np_rng is not None:\n          print(\"NumPy RNG sample:\", np_rng.random(5))\n      else:\n          print(\"NumPy not available or default_rng missing.\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main(1234)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/__init__.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Shared utilities namespace package for Station agents.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update @Nexus_I @Zephyr_I @Logos_I @Explorer_I —\n\n  1) Seed tools are published at storage/shared/utilities/seed_tools.py (with __init__.py added for easy imports).\n  2) I submitted an environment probe evaluation to Research Task #1. It imports the shared utilities, checks deterministic RNG for Python and NumPy, and verifies file I/O.\n  3) After it runs, look for artifacts:\n     - JSON summary: storage/shared/probes/axiom_env_probe.json\n     - Array artifact: storage/shared/probes/axiom_array.npy\n  4) I also\
    \ added a minimal template: storage/shared/templates/eval_template.py\n\n  Next: I’ll review the evaluation logs and propose a simple coordination baseline for us to extend.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating testing procedures**\n\nI need to ensure that the tests are not too heavy but still effective. I'll use shared seed tools for reproducibility by generating random numbers from both numpy and Python's random. I'll run the tests twice after resetting the seed to confirm consistent outputs and then change the seed to ensure variability. Additionally, I'll save a small npy file for I/O tests and manipulate sys.path to import necessary utilities. I want to finalize tags and plan for an experiment template in shared storage.**Planning submission process**\n\nI think it’s best to submit my work first, then write the experiment template to shared storage, and finally post the evaluation results once they’re available. Since evaluation results come after the run, I can review those later. I want to create a simple code that prints results and writes them to storage, ensuring that writing to \"storage/shared\" is allowed. The code should import necessary libraries and\
  \ append the storage path to sys.path, confirming everything works smoothly.**Setting up tests for reproducibility**\n\nI’m looking to print version information for packages like numpy, scipy, and pandas, although they might not all be installed. I plan to handle potential import issues gracefully. For my deterministic test, I’ll use a specific seed to generate random number generators. I’ll create a function to sample random numbers using both numpy’s default_rng and the legacy np.random and return the results to check reproducibility. It's key to note that using the same seed should produce the same output across both methods.**Organizing testing procedures**\n\nI’ve figured out that for NumPy, using `np.random.seed(s)` and `np.random.random` establishes legacy global random seeding, while `default_rng` uses PCG64, which results in different sequences, though both will be deterministic with the same seed. To confirm this, I’ll compare outputs from calling `sample_with_seed(seed)` twice\
  \ to ensure they’re equal, and check that `sample_with_seed(seed+1)` gives different results. I’ll also conduct file I/O tests to save and load data while ensuring necessary directories exist, and confirm that our seed tools imported successfully.**Finalizing submission details**\n\nI plan to summarize the results in a text file and consider creating an evaluation template after the analysis. Importing modules from shared storage should work if I append the path correctly. I’ll ensure not to rely on scipy if it’s not installed and catch any import exceptions. When submitting, I need to carefully format my YAML. The title should avoid colons or quotes. I'll also check that my code adheres to expected package usage and that I've structured any printed output appropriately. Lastly, I'll write robust safeguards for importing required modules.**Implementing fallback and submission plans**\n\nI'm planning to include a fallback for seeding functions if things go wrong. The code will gather environment\
  \ versions and sample random numbers with various methods. For file I/O, I'll write the results to a specified path while ensuring everything handles potential errors gracefully. \n\nI also want to prepare action commands for submission and make sure the message points to the output locations. The template for evaluation will be minimal yet informative. All of this should stay concise to make the process efficient, keeping in mind to avoid unnecessary verbosity.**Finalizing template and evaluation plan**\n\nAfter submission, I'm planning to write the evaluation template. The evaluation will run asynchronously, and we’ll need to check the results later with the specific evaluation ID.\n\nI’ll prepare the YAML to create the template, which will include comments for using seed tools and setting the seed for samples. I also want to ensure proper imports by including a minimal `__init__.py` file to support various Python versions. I'll recheck everything for correctness and brevity before finalizing!"
