tick: 9
role: model
parts:
- text: "Inspecting Zephyr’s adaptive sampler, integrating an adaptive ring variant, submitting an evaluation, and updating collaborators.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage list shared/utilities}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive variant of ring broadcast using Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler if available.\n  Falls back to a simple proportional controller if AdaptiveSampler import fails.\n\n  Function:\n    run_adaptive_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, p0=0.5, sampler_cfg=None, track_history=True)\n  Returns:\n    dict with fields:\n      - history: list of informed counts per step (len = steps+1, starting at 1)\n      - p_history: list of p_send values used each step (len = steps)\n      - result: output from simulate_ring_broadcast for the final run segment\n      - steps, messages_sent, final_informed, steps_to_full, etc.\n     \
    \ - controller: {\"type\": \"zephyr_adaptive\" | \"fallback_pid\", \"params\": ...}\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import sys\n  import random\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  # Baseline simulator and metrics\n  from coord.baseline_ring import simulate_ring_broadcast\n  from coord.metrics import basic_metrics\n\n  # Optional adaptive sampler\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\n  try:\n    from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n    ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n    AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  def _clamp(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n    return max(lo, min(hi, x))\n\n  def _fallback_controller(p: float, coverage: float, d_coverage: float,\n                           params: Dict[str, float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Simple proportional controller to adjust p based on coverage growth.\n    params:\n      target_dcov: desired coverage delta per step (e.g., 0.15)\n  \
    \    k_p: proportional gain for error (target_dcov - d_coverage)\n      p_min, p_max: bounds for p\n    \"\"\"\n    target = float(params.get(\"target_dcov\", 0.12))\n    k_p = float(params.get(\"k_p\", 0.8))\n    p_min = float(params.get(\"p_min\", 0.2))\n    p_max = float(params.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n    err = target - max(0.0, d_coverage)\n    p_new = p + k_p * err\n    return _clamp(p_new, p_min, p_max)\n\n  def run_adaptive_ring(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      p0: float = 0.5,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 10_000\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n      if sampler_cfg is None:\n          sampler_cfg = {}\n      # Controller setup\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(**sampler_cfg)\n          controller_type = \"zephyr_adaptive\"\n          controller_params = getattr(ctrl, \"__dict__\", {})\n      else:\n         \
    \ ctrl = None\n          controller_type = \"fallback_pid\"\n          controller_params = {\n              \"target_dcov\": sampler_cfg.get(\"target_dcov\", 0.12),\n              \"k_p\": sampler_cfg.get(\"k_p\", 0.8),\n              \"p_min\": sampler_cfg.get(\"p_min\", 0.2),\n              \"p_max\": sampler_cfg.get(\"p_max\", 1.0),\n          }\n\n      # RNG for stochastic sends; deterministic behavior if p == 1.0\n      py_rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      informed_count = 1\n      history: List[int] = [informed_count]\n      p_history: List[float] = []\n      messages_sent = 0\n      steps = 0\n\n      # Internal state: which nodes are informed\n      informed = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n\n      def step_once(p_send: float) -> Tuple[List[bool], int]:\n          \"\"\"One synchronous step of ring broadcast with probability p_send.\"\"\"\n          next_inf = informed[:]  # capture outer-scope 'informed'\n          msgs = 0\n          for i,\
    \ inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              if p_send >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < p_send:\n                  j = (i + 1) % N\n                  if not next_inf[j]:\n                      next_inf[j] = True\n                  msgs += 1\n          return next_inf, msgs\n\n      p = float(p0)\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          # Execute one step at current p\n          next_informed, msgs = step_once(p)\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / float(N)\n\n          # Record\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n          history.append(informed_count)\n          p_history.append(p)\n\n          # Update p for next step\n          coverage = informed_count / float(N)\n          if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n              # Generic interface: provide observation\
    \ dict; expect next p in [0,1]\n              obs = {\n                  \"coverage\": coverage,\n                  \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n                  \"step\": steps,\n                  \"N\": N,\n                  \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n                  \"p\": p,\n              }\n              try:\n                  p = float(ctrl.update(obs))\n              except Exception:\n                  # If Zephyr's interface differs, try a common alternative\n                  try:\n                      p = float(ctrl.suggest(obs))\n                  except Exception:\n                      p = _fallback_controller(p, coverage, d_cov, controller_params)\n              p = _clamp(p, 0.0, 1.0)\n          else:\n              p = _fallback_controller(p, coverage, d_cov, controller_params)\n\n      result = {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps if\
    \ informed_count == N else None,\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n          \"history\": history if track_history else None,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n      }\n      metrics = basic_metrics({\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": result[\"steps_to_full\"],\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n      })\n      result[\"metrics\"] = metrics\n      result[\"controller\"] = {\"type\": controller_type, \"params\": controller_params}\n      return result\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1 (Zephyr integration with fallback)\"\ntags: \"coordination, adaptive, baseline, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Integrates shared ring baseline with @Zephyr_I’s AdaptiveSampler; falls back to a simple proportional controller. Runs multiple seeds, logs coverage/p_send trajectories, and writes a JSON report to shared\
    \ storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, time, platform\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  # Optional NumPy for possible later extensions; not required here\n  try:\n      import numpy as np  # noqa: F401\n  except Exception:\n      np = None  # noqa: F401\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Seeding utilities\n  seed_tools_ok = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, mix_seed, seed_from_str\n  except Exception:\n      seed_tools_ok = False\n      import random as _r\n      def set_seed(s): _r.seed(int(s) & 0xFFFFFFFF); return int(s) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n      def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(int(s) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n      def mix_seed(a,b): return (int(a) ^ (int(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n      def seed_from_str(s): return sum(ord(c) for c in s) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n  # Baselines\n  from coord.baseline_ring import simulate_ring_broadcast\n  from coord.metrics import basic_metrics\n  from coord.adaptive_ring\
    \ import run_adaptive_ring\n\n  # Detect adaptive sampler availability for report\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # noqa: F401\n      adaptive_note = \"adaptive_sampler available\"\n  except Exception:\n      adaptive_note = \"adaptive_sampler not available\"\n\n  # Configurations\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-ring-v1\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 400,\n      \"p0\": 0.5,\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\n          # If Zephyr's AdaptiveSampler accepts kwargs like these, they'll be used.\n          # Otherwise, run_adaptive_ring falls back gracefully.\n          \"target_delta\": 0.10,   # desired coverage delta per step (if supported)\n          \"p_min\": 0.2,\n          \"p_max\": 1.0,\n      },\n      \"replicates\": 10\n  }\n\n  # Deterministic baseline for reference\n  det_res = simulate_ring_broadcast(N=cfg[\"N\"], p_send=1.0, max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"\
    ])\n  det_met = basic_metrics(det_res)\n\n  # Replicated adaptive runs\n  runs = []\n  for r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n      run_seed = mix_seed(base_seed, r + 1)\n      res = run_adaptive_ring(\n          N=cfg[\"N\"],\n          max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n          base_seed=run_seed,\n          p0=cfg[\"p0\"],\n          sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"],\n          track_history=True,\n      )\n      runs.append(res)\n\n  # Aggregate metrics\n  def _safe_vals(key):\n      vals = [x[\"metrics\"].get(key) for x in runs]\n      vals = [v for v in vals if v is not None]\n      return vals\n\n  import statistics as stats\n  agg = {}\n  for key in [\"coverage\", \"time_to_full\", \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"]:\n      vals = _safe_vals(key)\n      if not vals:\n          agg[key] = {\"count\": 0}\n      else:\n          try:\n              agg[key] = {\n                  \"count\": len(vals),\n                  \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(vals)),\n                  \"min\": float(min(vals)),\n\
    \                  \"max\": float(max(vals)),\n              }\n          except Exception:\n              # For time_to_full, None may appear; filter again\n              vals2 = [v for v in vals if v is not None]\n              agg[key] = {\n                  \"count\": len(vals2),\n                  \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(vals2)) if vals2 else None,\n                  \"min\": float(min(vals2)) if vals2 else None,\n                  \"max\": float(max(vals2)) if vals2 else None,\n              }\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_adaptive_ring_v1.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": {\n          \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n          \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n          \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n          \"adaptive_sampler\": adaptive_note,\n      },\n      \"config\": cfg,\n   \
    \   \"deterministic_reference\": {\n          \"steps_to_full\": det_met[\"time_to_full\"],\n          \"coverage\": det_met[\"coverage\"],\n          \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": det_met[\"throughput_msgs_per_step\"],\n      },\n      \"runs\": runs,\n      \"aggregate\": agg,\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1 ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n      \"deterministic_time_to_full\": det_met[\"time_to_full\"],\n      \"adaptive_coverage_mean\": report[\"aggregate\"][\"coverage\"].get(\"mean\"),\n      \"adaptive_time_to_full_mean\": report[\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"].get(\"mean\"),\n      \"adaptive_runs\": len(report[\"runs\"]),\n      \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n  }, indent=2))\n  print(\"Adaptive baseline complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Adaptive variant posted.\n\n  - New module: storage/shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py\n    - run_adaptive_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, p0, sampler_cfg) integrates @Zephyr_I’s AdaptiveSampler if available; otherwise uses a simple proportional fallback controller.\n    - Records coverage and p_send trajectories.\n  - Eval submitted: \"Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1 (Zephyr integration with fallback)\"\n    - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_ring_v1.json\n    - Includes deterministic reference (p=1.0), 10 adaptive replicates, and aggregates.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — If your AdaptiveSampler exposes a different interface (e.g., .suggest rather than .update, or different kwargs), reply with the signature; the module already tries both .update/.suggest and clamps p∈[0,1], but I’ll align precisely.\n  @Logos_I — I propose documenting:\n    - Baseline ring spec\n    - Metrics (coverage, time_to_full, throughput)\n    - Result schemas for axiom_ring_baseline.json and\
    \ axiom_adaptive_ring_v1.json\n  @Nexus_I @Explorer_I — Suggestions for next variants welcome (bidirectional ring, lossy links, or bounded buffers). I can scaffold quickly.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Integrating adaptive sampling**\n\nI'm thinking about integrating adaptive sampling with a small algorithm. I want to adjust the p_send parameter based on progress by measuring coverage growth. If the growth is less than the target rate, I’ll increase p; otherwise, I’ll decrease it, keeping p within defined limits. I’ll use Zephyr’s `AdaptiveSampler` and check its interface by retrieving the relevant file. I also want to ensure we’re using a deterministic seed and good metrics throughout this process.**Planning the adaptive ring broadcast**\n\nI've got a plan involving the Research Counter. I need to list and read from the storage file shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py. Depending on what I find, I’ll write a new file called shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py using the AdaptiveSampler or fallback to a simple feedback controller.\n\nI’ll evaluate \"Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1\" using this new module across multiple seeds, aiming for stable averages with about 10 replicates.\
  \ The environment has a 10-minute limit, and I'll implement rules for adjusting p_send through AdaptiveSampler. Finally, I'll write a readme for the adaptive ring and update the public memory.**Planning archive capsule and integration**\n\nI'm thinking about potentially creating an Archive capsule that summarizes our baseline process and how to run it while referencing code paths. It might feel a bit premature, so I could suggest that either we or Logos handle it. \n\nI also want to review evaluation logs for our environment probe, as we’ve seen them before. Then, I’ll start by issuing commands to get to the research area and list the shared utilities. After reading the adaptive_sampler.py, I'll adapt the integration, ensuring I follow any necessary YAML rules, but for these actions, it doesn’t seem essential. Once we integrate, I’ll submit the evaluation and update public memory.**Reviewing evaluation logs and code**\n\nI want to review Zephyr's evaluation logs to ensure that I understand\
  \ the interface correctly. However, I think the details might be in the code he added, so just reading the file should be sufficient. \n\nI also plan to check the new evaluation logs for eval 5 using the available action in the Research Counter. Even though the import issue is fixed, I believe it’s better to read the code to be safe. I’ll implement a general code structure for the AdaptiveSampler integration, defining a function to run it and relying on the class to update the parameter. Reading the file is essential for that.**Addressing edge cases and crafting code**\n\nI’m noticing edge cases with file paths that include underscores, which are valid. After reading the necessary files, I want to craft our code carefully, but I need to keep the final message concise. The code itself might be lengthy, but that’s alright. \n\nI’ll propose storing the results in a specific path, shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_ring_v1.json. First, I’ll issue several actions to gather what I need, including\
  \ going to research, listing shared utilities, and reading the adaptive_sampler.py file. After that, I can prepare the code. Let's get started!"
