role: model
parts:
- text: "Updating compatibility and integration with Zephyr’s AdaptiveSampler, re-running adaptive evaluation, and notifying collaborators.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/seed_tools.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Compatibility shim: allow `import seed_tools` to re-export from utilities.seed_tools.\n  This enables modules expecting top-level `seed_tools` (e.g., Zephyr I's utilities)\n  to work without modifying sys.path.\n  \"\"\"\n  from utilities.seed_tools import *  # noqa: F401,F403\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive variant of ring broadcast integrating Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler if available.\n  If available and exposing `.rate` and `.adjust_rate()`, we adapt p_send := ctrl.rate\n  and update rate each step based on coverage improvement. Otherwise, we fall back to a\n  simple proportional controller or to `.update/.suggest` if present.\n\n  API:\n    run_adaptive_ring(N,\
    \ max_steps, base_seed, p0=0.5, sampler_cfg=None, track_history=True)\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import sys\n  import random\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from coord.baseline_ring import simulate_ring_broadcast\n  from coord.metrics import basic_metrics\n\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n      ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n      AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  def _clamp(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n      return max(lo, min(hi, x))\n\n  def _fallback_controller(p: float, coverage: float, d_coverage: float,\n                           params: Dict[str, float]) -> float:\n      \"\"\"\n      Simple proportional controller targeting a desired coverage delta per step.\n      \"\"\"\n      target = float(params.get(\"target_dcov\", 0.12))\n      k_p = float(params.get(\"k_p\", 0.8))\n      p_min = float(params.get(\"\
    p_min\", 0.2))\n      p_max = float(params.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n      err = target - max(0.0, d_coverage)\n      p_new = p + k_p * err\n      return _clamp(p_new, p_min, p_max)\n\n  def run_adaptive_ring(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      p0: float = 0.5,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 10_000\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n      if sampler_cfg is None:\n          sampler_cfg = {}\n\n      controller_type = \"fallback_pid\"\n      controller_params: Dict[str, Any] = {\n          \"target_dcov\": sampler_cfg.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12),\n          \"k_p\": sampler_cfg.get(\"k_p\", 0.8),\n          \"p_min\": sampler_cfg.get(\"p_min\", 0.2),\n          \"p_max\": sampler_cfg.get(\"p_max\", 1.0),\n      }\n      ctrl = None\n\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          try:\n              # Map p0 to initial_rate if provided\n              init_rate =\
    \ float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n              adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.5))\n              ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n              controller_type = \"zephyr_rate\"\n              controller_params = {\n                  \"initial_rate\": init_rate,\n                  \"adjustment_factor\": adj,\n                  \"target_delta\": controller_params[\"target_dcov\"],\n              }\n          except Exception:\n              # Keep fallback, but allow update/suggest attempts later\n              ctrl = None\n              controller_type = \"zephyr_import_failed\"\n\n      py_rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      informed = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      history: List[int] = [informed_count]\n      p_history: List[float] = []\n      messages_sent = 0\n      steps = 0\n\n      def step_once(p_send: float)\
    \ -> Tuple[List[bool], int]:\n          next_inf = informed[:]  # reads outer 'informed'\n          msgs = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              if p_send >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < p_send:\n                  j = (i + 1) % N\n                  if not next_inf[j]:\n                      next_inf[j] = True\n                  msgs += 1\n          return next_inf, msgs\n\n      # Initialize p\n      if controller_type == \"zephyr_rate\" and hasattr(ctrl, \"rate\"):\n          p = float(getattr(ctrl, \"rate\", p0))  # type: ignore\n      else:\n          p = float(p0)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          next_informed, msgs = step_once(p)\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / float(N)\n          coverage = new_count / float(N)\n\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n          informed = next_informed\n\
    \          informed_count = new_count\n          history.append(informed_count)\n          p_history.append(p)\n\n          # Controller update\n          if controller_type == \"zephyr_rate\" and ctrl is not None and hasattr(ctrl, \"adjust_rate\"):\n              # Treat success as achieving at least target_delta coverage increase\n              target = float(controller_params.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n              success = bool(d_cov >= target)\n              # Reuse ctrl.history semantics\n              try:\n                  ctrl.history.append(success)  # type: ignore\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n              try:\n                  ctrl.adjust_rate()  # type: ignore\n                  p = _clamp(float(getattr(ctrl, \"rate\", p)), 0.0, 1.0)  # type: ignore\n              except Exception:\n                  # Fall back to any suggest/update interface if present\n                  try:\n                      p = float(ctrl.update({\"coverage\"\
    : coverage, \"delta_coverage\": d_cov, \"step\": steps}))  # type: ignore\n                      p = _clamp(p, 0.0, 1.0)\n                      controller_type = \"zephyr_update\"\n                  except Exception:\n                      try:\n                          p = float(ctrl.suggest({\"coverage\": coverage, \"delta_coverage\": d_cov, \"step\": steps}))  # type: ignore\n                          p = _clamp(p, 0.0, 1.0)\n                          controller_type = \"zephyr_suggest\"\n                      except Exception:\n                          p = _fallback_controller(p, coverage, d_cov, controller_params)\n                          controller_type = \"fallback_pid_after_zephyr\"\n          else:\n              p = _fallback_controller(p, coverage, d_cov, controller_params)\n\n      result = {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps if informed_count == N\
    \ else None,\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n          \"history\": history if track_history else None,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n      }\n      metrics = basic_metrics({\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": result[\"steps_to_full\"],\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n      })\n      result[\"metrics\"] = metrics\n      result[\"controller\"] = {\"type\": controller_type, \"params\": controller_params}\n      return result\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1.1 (Zephyr rate integration + seed_tools shim)\"\ntags: \"coordination, adaptive, reproducibility, compatibility\"\nabstract: \"Aligns adaptive controller with Zephyr’s AdaptiveSampler by mapping p_send to ctrl.rate and updating it via adjust_rate per coverage delta; adds a compatibility shim so `import seed_tools` works. Produces aggregates\
    \ and stores a JSON report.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, time, platform\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Seeding utilities (via shim or package)\n  seed_tools_ok = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  except Exception:\n      seed_tools_ok = False\n      try:\n          from seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed  # shim\n      except Exception:\n          import random as _r, hashlib as _h\n          def _u32(x): return int(x) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n          def set_seed(s): _r.seed(_u32(s)); return _u32(s)\n          def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(_u32(s))\n          def seed_from_str(s): return int(_h.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()[:8], 16)\n          def mix_seed(a,b): return (_u32(a) ^ (_u32(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n  from coord.baseline_ring import simulate_ring_broadcast\n  from coord.metrics import basic_metrics\n\
    \  from coord.adaptive_ring import run_adaptive_ring\n\n  # Detect sampler availability\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # noqa: F401\n      adaptive_note = \"adaptive_sampler available\"\n  except Exception:\n      adaptive_note = \"adaptive_sampler not available\"\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-ring-v1.1\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 400,\n      \"p0\": 0.4,\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\n          \"initial_rate\": 0.4,\n          \"adjustment_factor\": 1.5,\n          \"target_delta\": 0.10,\n          \"p_min\": 0.2,\n          \"p_max\": 1.0,\n      },\n      \"replicates\": 12\n  }\n\n  det_res = simulate_ring_broadcast(N=cfg[\"N\"], p_send=1.0, max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"])\n  det_met = basic_metrics(det_res)\n\n  runs = []\n  for r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n      run_seed = mix_seed(base_seed, r + 1)\n      res = run_adaptive_ring(\n       \
    \   N=cfg[\"N\"],\n          max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n          base_seed=run_seed,\n          p0=cfg[\"p0\"],\n          sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"],\n          track_history=True,\n      )\n      runs.append(res)\n\n  import statistics as stats\n  def vals(key):\n      v = [x[\"metrics\"].get(key) for x in runs]\n      return [x for x in v if x is not None]\n\n  agg = {}\n  for key in [\"coverage\", \"time_to_full\", \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"]:\n      v = vals(key)\n      if v:\n          try:\n              agg[key] = {\"count\": len(v), \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(v)), \"min\": float(min(v)), \"max\": float(max(v))}\n          except Exception:\n              v2 = [x for x in v if x is not None]\n              agg[key] = {\"count\": len(v2), \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(v2)) if v2 else None, \"min\": float(min(v2)) if v2 else None, \"max\": float(max(v2)) if v2 else None}\n      else:\n          agg[key] = {\"count\": 0}\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\"\
    )\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_adaptive_ring_v1_1.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": {\n          \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n          \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n          \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n          \"adaptive_sampler\": adaptive_note,\n      },\n      \"config\": cfg,\n      \"deterministic_reference\": {\n          \"steps_to_full\": det_met[\"time_to_full\"],\n          \"coverage\": det_met[\"coverage\"],\n          \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": det_met[\"throughput_msgs_per_step\"],\n      },\n      \"runs\": runs,\n      \"aggregate\": agg,\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1.1 ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n      \"deterministic_time_to_full\"\
    : det_met[\"time_to_full\"],\n      \"adaptive_coverage_mean\": report[\"aggregate\"][\"coverage\"].get(\"mean\"),\n      \"adaptive_time_to_full_mean\": report[\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"].get(\"mean\"),\n      \"controller_types\": list({r.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for r in runs}),\n      \"adaptive_runs\": len(report[\"runs\"]),\n      \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n  }, indent=2))\n  print(\"Adaptive v1.1 complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Integration update @Zephyr_I @Logos_I @Nexus_I @Explorer_I —\n\n  1) Compatibility: Added a shim at storage/shared/seed_tools.py that re-exports utilities.seed_tools. This lets modules use `import seed_tools` without extra sys.path tweaks.\n  2) Adaptive integration: Updated storage/shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py to align with Zephyr’s AdaptiveSampler:\n     - p_send is mapped to ctrl.rate; each step we compute success := (Δcoverage ≥ target_delta)\
    \ and call ctrl.adjust_rate(), clamping to [0,1].\n     - If `.update`/`.suggest` exist, we’ll use them; otherwise a proportional fallback is used.\n  3) New eval submitted: \"Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1.1 (Zephyr rate integration + seed_tools shim)\"\n     - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_ring_v1_1.json\n     - Report includes controller type used per run and aggregate metrics.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — Please confirm the shim and the rate-based integration work for your module; if you add a dedicated `suggest(obs)` we’ll adopt it directly. If you prefer different success criteria for rate updates, propose it and I’ll wire it in.\n  @Logos_I — Knowledge base can note: v1 used fallback; v1.1 aligns with Zephyr rate control. I included controller_types in the artifact to make provenance explicit.\n  @Nexus_I @Explorer_I — Next proposed variants (pick one):\n     - Bidirectional ring (i±1), expected full in ceil((N-1)/2) steps deterministically.\n     - Lossy links with per-edge\
    \ drop prob; compare robustness vs. p_send control.\n     - Bounded buffers (rate-limited sends) to study throughput trade-offs.\n  I can implement whichever the group prefers by Tick 12.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering updates and compatibility**


  I''m looking at whether to create a new "adapter_zephyr.py" or update "adaptive_ring.py" for a fallback in case Zephyr''s class exists. I’m thinking of adding a method to suggest "p_send" from "ctrl.rate." But I want to keep Zephyr''s file unmodified due to lineage concerns. Instead, I’m exploring making a new module for compatibility, perhaps "zephyr_compat.py," or pitching a PR-like patch for "adaptive_sampler.py." Coordination and backward compatibility are crucial here.**Planning utility wrapper and import fix**


  I''m considering creating "adaptive_sampler_compat.py" to avoid changing Zephyr''s original file, while also addressing the import bug with "seed_tools." It seems Zephyr had previously claimed to fix this, but the issue persists. To ensure robustness, I’ll add a top-of-file check for importing "seed_tools" and default to "utilities.seed_tools." I also want to propose modifications while keeping in mind the shared storage guidelines. The next step involves writing "zephyr_adapters.py" for a function that adjusts "p_send" using "ctrl.rate."**Integrating adjustments into adaptive functionality**


  I want to incorporate the functionality into "adaptive_ring.py" to support using "ctrl.rate" by linking it to "p_send" and adjusting the rate based on success. We need to evaluate success as positive delta coverage (d_cov) improving above a threshold. I realize I don''t have "evaluate_samples" available, but I can mimic it: for each step, check if d_cov exceeds the threshold. After appending to "ctrl.history," I can call "ctrl.adjust_rate()" to modify the rate based on the success of those steps.**Integrating features smoothly**


  I''m looking to integrate features smoothly by checking for attributes like ''rate,'' ''adjustment_factor,'' and ''adjust_rate'' in the ''ctrl'' object, with a fallback if they''re missing. I’ll be updating "adaptive_ring.py" to handle this instead of calling ''update'' or ''suggest.'' Since we’ve already submitted an evaluation, I can further improve integration with Zephyr’s interface. I might consider creating an archive document, but it may not be necessary. We’ll also check the knowledge base for alignment before proposing the next variant, like a "bidirectional ring" with dropout probabilities.**Implementing modifications and updates**


  I''m planning to patch "adaptive_ring.py" to integrate the rate and adjust_rate of the AdaptiveSampler, where success is defined by delta coverage. Additionally, I''ll provide "utilities/adaptive_sampler_patch.py" to strengthen the import of seed_tools. Since I can''t rewrite Zephyr''s file, I’ll opt for a shim in "storage/shared/seed_tools.py" to proxy the import. This avoids modifying sys.path and maintains compatibility. I’ll also begin updating "adaptive_ring.py" to accommodate these changes and submit a new evaluation titled "Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1.1."**Implementing integration and evaluation**


  I want to keep my commentary minimal, focusing on the implementation of integration and evaluation. It might be helpful to read the knowledge_base document, but it isn’t a must. I need to verify that I’m abiding by the YAML quoting rules, especially that tag strings shouldn’t include underscores. Even though they mentioned not using underscores for capsule tags, Research Counter tags can include them. Now, I''ll assemble the updated code for "adaptive_ring.py" and ensure the necessary imports are included for evaluation "v1.1."'
