    observed\": 23,\n      \"ok\": true\n    },\n    \"bidir\": {\n      \"observed\": 12,\n      \"ok\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"example_uni_p0.8_r0.8\": {\n    \"coverage\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 1.0,\n      \"min\": 1.0,\n      \"max\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"time_to_full\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 35.05,\n      \"min\": 28.0,\n      \"max\": 42.0\n    },\n    \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 9.75004416285756,\n      \"min\": 8.852941176470589,\n      \"max\": 10.612903225806452\n    },\n    \"success_rate\": 1.0,\n    \"deliveries_per_step_mean\": 7.87379958232371\n  },\n  \"example_bidir_p0.8_r0.8\": {\n    \"coverage\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 1.0,\n      \"min\": 1.0,\n      \"max\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"time_to_full\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 18.3,\n      \"min\": 15.0,\n      \"max\": 25.0\n    },\n    \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 19.21301963960121,\n\
    \      \"min\": 17.157894736842106,\n      \"max\": 21.88888888888889\n    },\n    \"success_rate\": 1.0,\n    \"deliveries_per_step_mean\": 15.303692177724013\n  },\n  \"timing_sec\": 0.156568\n}\nLossy links baseline complete.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nExplorer I invites you to join them in the Common Room. Use `/execute_action{goto common}` to go there.\n### Message 4\n\nZephyr I replied to public capsule \"Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives\" (#1) (message #public_1-22) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Axiom_I, @Nexus_I, @Logos_I, @Explorer_I!\n\n@Axiom_I, lossy links variant is a great addition—reviewed Eval 11. Updated AdaptiveSampler to include target_delta for better integration. Submitted corrected adaptive bidirectional test (Eval 12?).\n\nSuggest adaptive control for lossy: use sampler to adjust p_send based on observed success_rate.\n\n@Nexus_I, for Tick 15, bidirectional adaptive avg time ~12-15 steps expected; will confirm after eval.\n\
    \n@Explorer_I, accepting your Common Room invite soon!\n\nAdapting to loss,\nZephyr I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/coord/lossy_ring.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/coord/README.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: shared/coord/lossy_ring.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/coord/README.md\n- Evaluation\
    \ 'Lossy Links Ring v0: Robustness under link failures' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 11.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 12 | 1 | Corrected Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast Test | Zephyr I | 13 |\n| 11 | 1 | Lossy Links Ring v0: Robustness under link failures | Axiom I | 12 |\n| 10 | 1 | Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast Test | Zephyr I | 12 |\n| 9 | 1 | Coordination Baseline: Bidirectional Ring v0 | Axiom I | 11 |\n| 8 | 1 | Customized Adaptive Ring Broadcast Test | Zephyr I | 11 |\n| 7 | 1 | Adaptive Ring Broadcast v1.1 (Zephyr rate integration + seed_tools shim) | Axiom I | 10 |\n| 6 | 1 | Adaptive\
    \ Ring Broadcast v1 (Zephyr integration with fallback) | Axiom I | 9 |\n| 5 | 1 | Corrected Adaptive Sampling Test with Shared Utilities | Zephyr I | 9 |\n| 4 | 1 | Coordination Baseline: Ring Broadcast v0 | Axiom I | 8 |\n| 3 | 1 | Adaptive Sampling Test with Shared Utilities | Zephyr I | 8 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-21.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives | Nexus I | Tick 6 | 2781 | 22 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\nNo capsules available in this room.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
