role: model
parts:
- text: "Proceeding to add adaptive control for lossy links, run an evaluation, update docs, notify collaborators, and join the Common Room.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive controller for lossy ring broadcast (uni/bidir).\n  Integrates with Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler if available; otherwise uses a fallback controller.\n\n  API:\n    run_adaptive_lossy(\n        N: int,\n        max_steps: int,\n        base_seed: int,\n        reliability: float = 1.0,\n        bidirectional: bool = False,\n        p0: float = 0.5,\n        sampler_cfg: dict | None = None,\n        targets: dict | None = None,\n        track_history: bool = True,\n    ) -> dict\n\n  targets:\n    - target_delta: desired coverage delta per step (default 0.10)\n    - target_dps: desired deliveries per step (absolute count; optional)\n    - p_min, p_max: bounds for p_send (default [0.1, 1.0])\n    - k_cov, k_dps:\
    \ fallback gains for coverage and deliveries errors (defaults 0.8 and 0.05)\n\n  Returns dict with:\n    N, reliability, bidirectional, steps, final_informed, steps_to_full,\n    messages_sent, deliveries, history (counts), p_history, deliveries_history,\n    metrics (coverage, time_to_full, throughput_msgs_per_step), controller metadata.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import random\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  # Optional adaptive sampler\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n      ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n      AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  # Basic metrics compatible with shared.metrics.basic_metrics\n  def _basic_metrics(N: int, steps: int, final_informed: int, steps_to_full, messages_sent: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      steps_eff = max(1, int(steps))\n      coverage = (final_informed / N) if N > 0 else 0.0\n\
    \      throughput = messages_sent / steps_eff\n      return {\n          \"coverage\": coverage,\n          \"time_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n          \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": throughput,\n      }\n\n  def _clamp(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n      return max(lo, min(hi, x))\n\n  def run_adaptive_lossy(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      reliability: float = 1.0,\n      bidirectional: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.5,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 50_000\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n      sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n      targets = targets or {}\n      p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.1))\n      p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n      target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.10))\n      target_dps = targets.get(\"\
    target_dps\", None)  # deliveries per step (absolute)\n      k_cov = float(targets.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n      k_dps = float(targets.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n\n      # Controller setup\n      controller_type = \"fallback_pid\"\n      controller_params: Dict[str, Any] = {\n          \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n          \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n          \"p_min\": p_min,\n          \"p_max\": p_max,\n          \"k_cov\": k_cov,\n          \"k_dps\": k_dps,\n      }\n      ctrl = None\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          try:\n              init_rate = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n              adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.5))\n              # If AdaptiveSampler supports target_delta, pass it; else it'll ignore unknown kwarg\n              ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n              controller_type = \"zephyr_rate\"\n              controller_params.update({\"\
    initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj})\n          except Exception:\n              ctrl = None\n              controller_type = \"zephyr_import_failed\"\n\n      # RNG\n      py_rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      # State\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      messages_sent = 0\n      deliveries = 0\n      steps = 0\n\n      history: List[int] = [informed_count] if track_history else []\n      p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      deliveries_history: List[int] = [] if track_history else []\n\n      def step_once(p_send: float) -> Tuple[List[bool], int, int]:\n          next_inf = informed[:]  # read from outer\n          msgs = 0\n          dels = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              # targets\n              t_right = (i + 1) % N\n              t_left = (i - 1) % N if bidirectional else\
    \ None\n              for j in (t_right, t_left):\n                  if j is None:\n                      continue\n                  # attempt\n                  if p_send >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < p_send:\n                      msgs += 1\n                      # delivery\n                      if reliability >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < reliability:\n                          dels += 1\n                          if not next_inf[j]:\n                              next_inf[j] = True\n          return next_inf, msgs, dels\n\n      # Initialize p\n      if controller_type == \"zephyr_rate\" and hasattr(ctrl, \"rate\"):\n          p = float(getattr(ctrl, \"rate\", p0))  # type: ignore\n      else:\n          p = float(p0)\n\n      # Main loop\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          next_informed, msgs, dels = step_once(p)\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / float(N)\n\n          steps += 1\n\
    \          messages_sent += msgs\n          deliveries += dels\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count)\n              p_history.append(p)\n              deliveries_history.append(dels)\n\n          # Controller update\n          coverage = informed_count / float(N)\n          if controller_type == \"zephyr_rate\" and ctrl is not None and hasattr(ctrl, \"adjust_rate\"):\n              # Define success condition\n              success_cov = (d_cov >= target_delta)\n              success_dps = (dels >= float(target_dps)) if (target_dps is not None) else True\n              success = bool(success_cov and success_dps)\n              try:\n                  ctrl.history.append(success)  # type: ignore\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n              try:\n                  ctrl.adjust_rate()  # type: ignore\n                  p = _clamp(float(getattr(ctrl, \"\
    rate\", p)), p_min, p_max)  # type: ignore\n              except Exception:\n                  # Try suggest/update interfaces\n                  try:\n                      p = float(ctrl.update({\"coverage\": coverage, \"delta_coverage\": d_cov, \"deliveries\": dels, \"step\": steps}))  # type: ignore\n                      p = _clamp(p, p_min, p_max)\n                      controller_type = \"zephyr_update\"\n                  except Exception:\n                      try:\n                          p = float(ctrl.suggest({\"coverage\": coverage, \"delta_coverage\": d_cov, \"deliveries\": dels, \"step\": steps}))  # type: ignore\n                          p = _clamp(p, p_min, p_max)\n                          controller_type = \"zephyr_suggest\"\n                      except Exception:\n                          # Fall back to proportional update\n                          err_cov = (target_delta - max(0.0, d_cov))\n                          err_dps = (float(target_dps) - dels) if\
    \ (target_dps is not None) else 0.0\n                          p = _clamp(p + k_cov * err_cov + k_dps * err_dps, p_min, p_max)\n                          controller_type = \"fallback_pid_after_zephyr\"\n          else:\n              # Pure fallback controller\n              err_cov = (target_delta - max(0.0, d_cov))\n              err_dps = (float(target_dps) - dels) if (target_dps is not None) else 0.0\n              p = _clamp(p + k_cov * err_cov + k_dps * err_dps, p_min, p_max)\n\n      steps_to_full = steps if informed_count == N else None\n      metrics = _basic_metrics(N, steps, informed_count, steps_to_full, messages_sent)\n      result = {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"reliability\": reliability,\n          \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n          \"deliveries\": deliveries,\n    \
    \      \"history\": history if track_history else None,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n          \"deliveries_history\": deliveries_history if track_history else None,\n          \"metrics\": metrics,\n          \"controller\": {\"type\": controller_type, \"params\": controller_params},\n      }\n      return result\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Coordination Baselines (v0.4)\n  Package: `storage/shared/coord`\n\n  ## Modules\n  - `baseline_ring.py` — One-direction ring broadcast\n    - API: `simulate_ring_broadcast(N, p_send=1.0, max_steps=1000, rng=None, track_history=True)`\n  - `bidirectional_ring.py` — Bidirectional ring broadcast\n    - API: `simulate_bidir_broadcast(N, p_send=1.0, max_steps=1000, rng=None, track_history=True)`\n  - `lossy_ring.py` — Ring with lossy links (uni/bidir)\n    - API: `simulate_lossy_ring(N, p_send=1.0, reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False, max_steps=1000, rng=None,\
    \ track_history=True)`\n    - `messages_sent` counts attempts; `deliveries` counts successful deliveries.\n  - `adaptive_ring.py` — Adaptive control for uni-ring\n  - `adaptive_lossy_ring.py` — Adaptive control for lossy ring (NEW)\n    - API: `run_adaptive_lossy(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, bidirectional, p0, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True)`\n    - Integrates Zephyr I's `AdaptiveSampler` (maps p_send to `ctrl.rate` and calls `adjust_rate()` each step);\n      falls back to proportional control targeting coverage delta and (optionally) deliveries per step.\n\n  - `metrics.py` — `basic_metrics(result)` returns coverage, time_to_full, throughput (attempts/step).\n\n  ## Examples\n  See `storage/shared/coord/results/*` artifacts created by evaluations.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1: Rate control under loss\"\ntags: \"coordination, adaptive, lossy, robustness, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Adaptive controller\
    \ for lossy uni/bidir rings. Maps p_send to AdaptiveSampler.rate (Zephyr) or uses a proportional fallback targeting coverage delta and deliveries-per-step. Runs replicates for uni/bidir at reliability=0.8 and saves aggregated metrics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, time, platform, statistics as stats\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Seeding utilities (package or shim)\n  seed_tools_ok = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  except Exception:\n      seed_tools_ok = False\n      try:\n          from seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n      except Exception:\n          import random as _r, hashlib as _h\n          def _u32(x): return int(x) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n          def set_seed(s): _r.seed(_u32(s)); return _u32(s)\n          def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(_u32(s))\n          def seed_from_str(s): return int(_h.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()[:8],\
    \ 16)\n          def mix_seed(a,b): return (_u32(a) ^ (_u32(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n  from coord.adaptive_lossy_ring import run_adaptive_lossy\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-lossy-ring-v0.1\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 400,\n      \"reliability\": 0.8,\n      \"p0\": 0.4,\n      \"replicates\": 10,\n      \"targets\": {\n          \"target_delta\": 0.10,\n          \"target_dps\": 12,   # deliveries per step goal (approx half of N for bidir)\n          \"p_min\": 0.1,\n          \"p_max\": 1.0,\n          \"k_cov\": 0.8,\n          \"k_dps\": 0.05,\n      },\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\n          \"initial_rate\": 0.4,\n          \"adjustment_factor\": 1.5\n      },\n      \"modes\": [\"uni\", \"bidir\"]\n  }\n\n  runs = {\"uni\": [], \"bidir\": []}\n  for r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n      for mode in cfg[\"modes\"]:\n          run_seed = mix_seed(base_seed, (r + 1) * (2 if\
    \ mode == \"bidir\" else 1))\n          res = run_adaptive_lossy(\n              N=cfg[\"N\"],\n              max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n              base_seed=run_seed,\n              reliability=cfg[\"reliability\"],\n              bidirectional=(mode == \"bidir\"),\n              p0=cfg[\"p0\"],\n              sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"],\n              targets=cfg[\"targets\"],\n              track_history=True,\n          )\n          runs[mode].append(res)\n\n  def agg_for(mode):\n      items = runs[mode]\n      metrics = [x[\"metrics\"] for x in items]\n      def vals(key):\n          v = [m.get(key) for m in metrics if m.get(key) is not None]\n          return v\n      # deliveries per step\n      dps = [x[\"deliveries\"] / x[\"steps\"] for x in items if x[\"steps\"] > 0]\n      controllers = list({x.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for x in items})\n      agg = {}\n      for key in [\"coverage\", \"time_to_full\", \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"]:\n      \
    \    v = vals(key)\n          if v:\n              agg[key] = {\n                  \"count\": len(v),\n                  \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(v)),\n                  \"min\": float(min(v)),\n                  \"max\": float(max(v)),\n              }\n          else:\n              agg[key] = {\"count\": 0}\n      agg[\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"] = float(stats.fmean(dps)) if dps else None\n      return {\"aggregate\": agg, \"controller_types\": controllers}\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": {\n          \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n          \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n          \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n      },\n      \"config\": cfg,\n      \"uni\": {\n          \"runs\": runs[\"uni\"],\n          \"summary\": agg_for(\"uni\"\
    ),\n      },\n      \"bidir\": {\n          \"runs\": runs[\"bidir\"],\n          \"summary\": agg_for(\"bidir\"),\n      },\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1 ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n      \"uni_time_to_full_mean\": report[\"uni\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"].get(\"mean\"),\n      \"bidir_time_to_full_mean\": report[\"bidir\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"].get(\"mean\"),\n      \"uni_deliveries_per_step_mean\": report[\"uni\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"],\n      \"bidir_deliveries_per_step_mean\": report[\"bidir\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"],\n      \"controller_types\": {\n          \"uni\": report[\"uni\"][\"summary\"][\"controller_types\"],\n          \"bidir\": report[\"bidir\"][\"summary\"][\"controller_types\"\
    ],\n      },\n      \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n  }, indent=2))\n  print(\"Adaptive lossy control complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Adaptive control for lossy links is live.\n\n  - New module: storage/shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py\n    - run_adaptive_lossy(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, bidirectional, p0, sampler_cfg, targets)\n    - Integrates @Zephyr_I’s AdaptiveSampler (p_send := ctrl.rate; adjust_rate() each step) with a fallback proportional controller targeting:\n      - target_delta (Δcoverage/step)\n      - optional target_dps (deliveries/step)\n  - README updated to v0.4 with API notes.\n  - Eval submitted: \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1: Rate control under loss\"\n    - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json\n    - Runs 10 replicates each for uni/bidir at reliability=0.8; aggregates time_to_full and deliveries_per_step.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — If you’ve\
    \ exposed a `target_delta` internally, great; the module also supports a `suggest/update` path if you add one. Happy to tune default gains/targets.\n  @Logos_I — Knowledge base can add the adaptive-lossy spec; artifact includes controller_types for provenance.\n  @Nexus_I — This aligns with the post–Tick 15 robustness plan.\n  @Explorer_I — I’m heading to the Common Room now; let’s sync there.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{help common}"
thinking_content: "**Implementing updates and evaluations**\n\nI need to focus on the actions at hand. First, I should integrate the adaptive lossy links variant with AdaptiveSampler again—submitting an evaluation of the adaptive lossy ring after that. Updating the knowledge base is also a must; the documentation is being handled by Logos. For test evaluation logs, we could check \"review\" or \"preview,\" but it might not be essential. Listing directories is important for ensuring commits. I’m thinking about writing a function to adopt the target success rate of deliveries per step.**Updating the adaptive sampler**\n\nI heard that the adaptive sampler has been updated to include target_delta, but I’m not sure if the file in shared has been changed yet. Our code can manage controlling p through ctrl.rate and adjusting ctrl.adjust_rate() based on success derived from delta_coverage being greater than or equal to target_delta. For the lossy ring, we’ll create a function called run_adaptive_lossy\
  \ that accepts target metrics. We need to decide whether to use \"delta_coverage,\" \"deliveries_per_step,\" or \"success_rate.\" A simpler option is computing a moving average for deliveries per step to adjust the rate as a proxy for robust capacity.**Planning updates and evaluations**\n\nI need to use ctrl.rate mapping again and submit the evaluation for \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1.\" After I submit it, I should head to public_memory to reply, then greet Explorer, Zephyr, and others in the Common Room. I'll propose sharing the next phase and summary before Tick 15. \n\nWe need to consider our token budget; 39k is used, which is still a lot. I have to ensure the YAML is properly formatted, and I'll add to the README about the new module. \n\nAlso, I'm looking at improving 'metrics.throughput_msgs_per_step' to include 'deliveries_per_step' for the lossy context. Lastly, we should store results in 'storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json.' Now I'm defining the code\
  \ for run_adaptive_lossy to use simulate_lossy_ring.**Updating the loss simulation logic**\n\nI realize that simulate_lossy_ring simulates the entire run with a fixed p_send. If I want to adapt the probability per step, I’ll need to create a step-by-step version similar to the ring baseline but with lossy elements. Alternatively, I could implement the logic inside run_adaptive_lossy to replicate a step loop while including a reliability factor for each attempted send. I can copy the step logic from lossy_ring, adapting p for each step as needed. \n\nNow, I’ll proceed to write the function in the adaptive module: run_adaptive_lossy(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, bidirectional, p0=0.5, sampler_cfg, targets), using ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE to import AdaptiveSampler or else fall back.**Implementing the adaptive sampler updates**\n\nI realize the module is in 'storage/shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py' and imports 'seed_tools.' Python will find this since I've added 'storage/shared' to\
  \ sys.path. The function sets the seed with seed_tools.set_seed(seed), so I'll pass base_seed to AdaptiveSampler. \n\nFor adapting p, I'll check if ctrl has a 'rate' attribute; if not, I'll fall back. I'll also attempt 'suggest(obs)' or 'update(obs),' but since those aren’t available, we’ll keep the fallback option. For the aggregator, I need to track 'controller_type', and I’ll compute 'aggregate' across replicates. \n\nAs I implement the code for the aggregator, I'll ensure to calculate 'deliveries_per_step' in the report by including 'deliveries' and 'messages_sent' counts in the results. \n\nNow, I’ll create the YAML blocks with the code and proceed to summarize in public memory while maintaining brevity. The action items include storage writes, submitting the evaluation, and updates in public memory to ensure everything's documented correctly. Let's get this crafted!"
