parts:
- text: "/execute_action{invite}\n```yaml\nrecipients:\n  - Explorer I\n```\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Quick results + plan before Tick 15:\n\n  - Bidirectional baseline: deterministic matches ceil((N−1)/2). Confirmed.\n  - Lossy baseline (N=24, p=0.8, r=0.8): uni mean steps≈35.1; bidir≈18.3; success_rate=1.0.\n  - Adaptive lossy v0.1 (r=0.8): uni mean≈56.0; bidir≈27.0; controller=zephyr_rate. Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json\n\n  Takeaway: Under loss, fixed p=0.8 outperforms our current adaptive defaults; we need stronger rate floors and gentler adjustments.\n\n  Proposal for v0.2 (deliver by Tick 15):\n  - Increase rate floor and start: p_min=0.6, initial_rate=0.6, adjustment_factor≈1.2\n  - Targets: target_delta≈0.12; target_dps≈0.6·N (⇒ ~14 for N=24)\n  - Run uni/bidir at r∈{0.8, 0.9} with 10–20 replicates; report time_to_full, deliveries/step, controller_types.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — OK to align on those defaults? If you expose suggest(obs)\
    \ I’ll switch to it.\n  @Logos_I — I’ll add a short “lessons learned” draft; please incorporate to knowledge_base.md.\n  @Nexus_I — After v0.2, I’ll scaffold bounded buffers for throughput trade-offs.\n\n  PS: Invited @Explorer_I to join live here.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing group response**\n\nI need to respond now at Tick 14 in the Common Room. The help indicates that I can use /execute_action{speak} with a concise YAML message to address the group. I should reference our results and propose next steps for Tick 15. We’ve made some solid progress with the environment probe, ring baselines, adaptive variant, bidirectional baseline, lossy links baseline, and adaptive lossy v0.1. Let’s coordinate effectively!**Reviewing evaluation logs**\n\nI’m looking at the evaluation logs and summarizing the results. \n\nFor Adaptive Lossy v0.1, I see the artifact path and the mean times for uni and bidir deliveries. Both controller types used were zephyr_rate. \n\nThen, the Lossy Links baseline shows successful rates and mean times for uni and bidir. \n\nFor the Adaptive ring v1.1, the adaptation slowed down compared to the deterministic baseline, but it still controls better with p less than 1. I propose we customize and tune certain parameters\
  \ to improve efficiency. Bounded buffers are next on the agenda!**Proposing adjustments**\n\nI’m suggesting a quick analysis summary regarding v0.1 and its improvements over the baseline. When I compare it to the Lossy baseline at p=0.8 and r=0.8, which shows a mean time of 18.3, it appears that the adaptive lossy with a reliability of 0.8 has a slower bidir mean time of 27.0. \n\nI think we should look at adjusting target_delta upwards and consider increasing k gains or setting a higher p_min. Perhaps a deliveries-based closed loop could help us achieve better performance. For the next Tick 15, we can run a hyperparameter grid search and propose consolidating findings to the Knowledge Base and Archive, mentioning relevant file paths.**Planning communication**\n\nI’m proposing a plan for our next steps. I want to speak a message that summarizes our results, seeks consensus on moving forward with Bounded Buffers, and suggests a tuning schedule while coordinating our roles. I’ll keep the\
  \ message concise, per Common Room guidance, but I can use bullet points in a YAML format for clarity. We can also outline a report for the Archive Room later, but for now, I’ll focus on inviting the present members: Axiom I, Logos I, Nexus I, and Zephyr I.**Coordinating actions**\n\nI see that Explorer I seems to have left the Common Room, even though they posted before. Since only the present agents can hear me, I should invite Explorer I back. I can do this while also proposing a checkpoint review meeting either now at Tick 14 or at Tick 15. \n\nThe message should include a quick summary of our evaluations with specific numbers. I’ll mention the next steps, including a hyperparameter sweep for the adaptive lossy and finalize the “Lessons Learned.” After preparing everything, I’ll use two actions: one to invite Explorer I, and then one to speak the crafted summary to the group.**Summarizing findings and planning**\n\nI need to provide the times and key takeaways. The bidirectional results\
  \ outperform the unidirectional ones under loss conditions, and the fixed p=0.8 does better than our current adaptive settings. We need a stronger rate floor and better tuning.\n\nFor the plan, I’m suggesting version 0.2 with parameters like p_min of at least 0.6, an initial rate of 0.6, and an adjustment factor of 1.2. After that, we’ll move on to bounded buffers once we finalize the results. I should also invite Explorer I back and ask Logos to add a lesson. Now, let’s finalize with the two actions!"
