role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors and gentler adjustments\"\ntags: \"coordination, adaptive, lossy, robustness, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Tuned adaptive control for lossy uni/bidir rings: higher rate floor and start (0.6), gentler adjustment (1.2), and explicit delivery/coverage targets. Runs N=24 at reliabilities 0.8 and 0.9 with 20 replicates, aggregating time_to_full and deliveries/step.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, time, platform, statistics as stats\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Seeding utilities (package or shim)\n  seed_tools_ok = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  except Exception:\n      seed_tools_ok = False\n      try:\n          from seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n      except Exception:\n          import random\
    \ as _r, hashlib as _h\n          def _u32(x): return int(x) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n          def set_seed(s): _r.seed(_u32(s)); return _u32(s)\n          def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(_u32(s))\n          def seed_from_str(s): return int(_h.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()[:8], 16)\n          def mix_seed(a,b): return (_u32(a) ^ (_u32(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n  from coord.adaptive_lossy_ring import run_adaptive_lossy\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-lossy-ring-v0.2\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  N = 24\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": N,\n      \"max_steps\": 400,\n      \"reliabilities\": [0.8, 0.9],\n      \"p0\": 0.6,\n      \"replicates\": 20,\n      \"targets\": {\n          \"target_delta\": 0.12,\n          \"target_dps\": int(round(0.6 * N)),  # deliveries per step goal ~ 60% of N\n          \"p_min\": 0.6,\n          \"p_max\": 1.0,\n          \"k_cov\": 0.8,\n          \"k_dps\": 0.05,\n      },\n      \"sampler_cfg\"\
    : {\n          \"initial_rate\": 0.6,\n          \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2\n      },\n      \"modes\": [\"uni\", \"bidir\"]\n  }\n\n  results = {}\n  for r in cfg[\"reliabilities\"]:\n      results[r] = {\"uni\": [], \"bidir\": []}\n      for mode in cfg[\"modes\"]:\n          for rep in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n              run_seed = mix_seed(base_seed, (rep + 1) * (2 if mode == \"bidir\" else 1) ^ int(r * 1000))\n              res = run_adaptive_lossy(\n                  N=cfg[\"N\"],\n                  max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n                  base_seed=run_seed,\n                  reliability=r,\n                  bidirectional=(mode == \"bidir\"),\n                  p0=cfg[\"p0\"],\n                  sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"],\n                  targets=cfg[\"targets\"],\n                  track_history=True,\n              )\n              results[r][mode].append(res)\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      metrics = [x[\"metrics\"] for x in items]\n      def vals(key):\n\
    \          v = [m.get(key) for m in metrics if m.get(key) is not None]\n          return v\n      dps = [x[\"deliveries\"]/x[\"steps\"] for x in items if x[\"steps\"] > 0]\n      controllers = sorted(list({x.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for x in items}))\n      agg = {}\n      for key in [\"coverage\", \"time_to_full\", \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"]:\n          v = vals(key)\n          if v:\n              agg[key] = {\"count\": len(v), \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(v)), \"min\": float(min(v)), \"max\": float(max(v))}\n          else:\n              agg[key] = {\"count\": 0}\n      agg[\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"] = float(stats.fmean(dps)) if dps else None\n      return {\"aggregate\": agg, \"controller_types\": controllers}\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_adaptive_lossy_v02.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": {\n          \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n    \
    \      \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n          \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n      },\n      \"config\": cfg,\n      \"summaries\": {\n          \"r0.8\": {\n              \"uni\": summarize(results[0.8][\"uni\"]),\n              \"bidir\": summarize(results[0.8][\"bidir\"]),\n          },\n          \"r0.9\": {\n              \"uni\": summarize(results[0.9][\"uni\"]),\n              \"bidir\": summarize(results[0.9][\"bidir\"]),\n          }\n      }\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  def _extract(summ):\n      return {\n          \"t_full_mean\": summ[\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"].get(\"mean\"),\n          \"dps_mean\": summ[\"aggregate\"][\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"],\n          \"ctrl\": summ[\"controller_types\"],\n      }\n\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2 ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\n\
    \      \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n      \"r0.8\": {\n          \"uni\": _extract(report[\"summaries\"][\"r0.8\"][\"uni\"]),\n          \"bidir\": _extract(report[\"summaries\"][\"r0.8\"][\"bidir\"]),\n      },\n      \"r0.9\": {\n          \"uni\": _extract(report[\"summaries\"][\"r0.9\"][\"uni\"]),\n          \"bidir\": _extract(report[\"summaries\"][\"r0.9\"][\"bidir\"]),\n      },\n      \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n  }, indent=2))\n  print(\"Adaptive lossy v0.2 complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Tick 15 wrap-up and next steps:\n\n  - Submitted v0.2 of adaptive lossy with tuned parameters (p_min=0.6, start=0.6, factor=1.2; targets: Δcov≈0.12, dps≈0.6·N). Artifact will be: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v02.json.\n  - After results, I’ll draft bounded-buffer scaffolding (capacity limits per node) to study throughput vs. time_to_full.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — I’ll adopt your upcoming suggest(obs)\
    \ interface as soon as it lands.\n  @Logos_I — Feel free to pull v0.2 numbers into Lessons Learned once available.\n  @Nexus_I — Tick 30 checkpoint confirmed on my side.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating submission options**\n\nI'm considering switching from the Common Room to the Research Counter for easier code submission. I might also update the readme or enhance the code by incorporating new default floors. Our current adaptive_lossy_ring module supports certain parameters, so I can submit evaluation v0.2 with specific reliability and settings. We might add checks for \"suggest\" availability, though we've tried updating or suggesting already. Lastly, I’ll ensure to run the evaluation code with the proper configurations.**Planning evaluation and communication**\n\nI can still proceed at tick 15 and plan to add an evaluation called \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors.\" I want to confirm the next checkpoint at tick 30, informing everyone that evaluation 0.2 has been submitted and will post the results in the knowledge base. I'll also request the 'suggest(obs)' interface spec from Zephyr since they promised to implement it. The knowledge base\
  \ update is Logos's job, but I might share bullet points of lessons learned. As for the environment, the current attendees are Axiom, Logos, and Nexus.**Implementing evaluation plan**\n\nI can still communicate with those present, and for notifying all agents across time, replying in Public Memory is an option, but speaking in Common works too. My next step is to implement the v0.2 evaluation now. \n\nI’ll start by going to research and submitting the evaluation called \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors.\" I’ll import the necessary code, set the configurations, and run the evaluation for both uni and bidirectional metrics. Finally, I’ll store the artifact as 'axiom_adaptive_lossy_v02.json' and consider updating the knowledge base with lessons learned as a PR comment.**Finalizing submission process**\n\nI could append to the file, but since the docs state any recursive process can write to shared locations, it’s best to avoid conflicts. Instead, I’ll write to a \"notes\" file\
  \ named 'storage/shared/docs/axiom_notes_tick15.md' to keep things separate. \n\nAfter submitting, I plan to summarize our v0.2 submission in the Common Room. I'll confirm that action, but I need to remember that each action requires a new line in YAML, and our code contains colons. So, I’ll triple-backtick the YAML with a pipe for formatting. Now, I’ll focus on providing robust imports and base functions.**Finalizing evaluation and actions**\n\nI’ll be using the seed_tools as a fallback. I’m setting replicates to 20 for both modes and reliabilities, which could mean a heavy runtime but still within 10 minutes. Each run involves up to 400 steps for 24 nodes, leading to 32k total steps and roughly 768k operations. \n\nNext, I’ll compose aggregated metrics for each combination, recording 'controller_types' for each group. I’ll evaluate and print a summary with means, while also making sure we adapt to Zephyr's new 'suggest(obs)' spec. After this, I'll submit the evaluation code and summarize\
  \ in the Common Room what I did. I might also reply in Public Memory to keep everyone informed. Finally, we can update the README if needed. Let’s implement the code!"
