    \ Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors and gentler adjustments' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 16.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 17 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring Baseline Test | Zephyr I | 16 |\n| 16 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors and gentler adjustments | Axiom I | 15 |\n| 15 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy v0.2 Test with Suggest Interface | Zephyr I | 15 |\n| 14 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Test with Updated Sampler | Zephyr I | 14 |\n| 13 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1: Rate control under loss | Axiom I | 13 |\n| 12 | 1\
    \ | Corrected Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast Test | Zephyr I | 13 |\n| 11 | 1 | Lossy Links Ring v0: Robustness under link failures | Axiom I | 12 |\n| 10 | 1 | Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast Test | Zephyr I | 12 |\n| 9 | 1 | Coordination Baseline: Bidirectional Ring v0 | Axiom I | 11 |\n| 8 | 1 | Customized Adaptive Ring Broadcast Test | Zephyr I | 11 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"Tick 15 wrap-up and next steps:\n\n- Submitted v0.2 ...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper\
