parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage list shared/coord}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/buffered_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Bounded-buffers ring broadcast (uni/bidir) with per-node queues and service limits.\n  Supports configurable service timing: serve arrivals immediately (default) or next step.\n\n  Parameters:\n    - N: number of nodes (>= 2)\n    - p_send: probability an informed node attempts to send to a neighbor each step\n    - reliability: probability an attempted send is delivered to the neighbor's queue\n    - bidirectional: if True, each informed node targets both (i±1); else only (i+1)\n    - buffer_size: max queue length per node (arrivals beyond this are dropped)\n    - service_rate: max messages removed from a node's queue per step\n    - serve_after: if True, process existing queue first then add new arrivals (arrivals served next step).\n                   if False (default), add arrivals then process (arrivals can\
    \ be served same step).\n    - max_steps: hard cap on steps\n    - rng: Python RNG with .random(); required if p_send < 1.0 or reliability < 1.0\n    - track_history: record informed counts per step\n\n  Returns dict:\n    {\n      \"N\", \"p_send\", \"reliability\", \"bidirectional\", \"buffer_size\", \"service_rate\", \"serve_after\",\n      \"max_steps\", \"steps\", \"final_informed\", \"steps_to_full\" (or None),\n      \"messages_attempted\", \"enqueued\", \"dropped\", \"processed\",\n      \"queue_peak\", \"history\" (optional)\n    }\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List\n\n  def simulate_buffered_ring(\n      N: int,\n      p_send: float = 1.0,\n      reliability: float = 1.0,\n      bidirectional: bool = False,\n      buffer_size: int = 8,\n      service_rate: int = 1,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      max_steps: int = 1000,\n      rng: Optional[object] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert N >= 2, \"N must\
    \ be >= 2\"\n      assert 0.0 <= p_send <= 1.0, \"p_send must be in [0,1]\"\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0, \"reliability must be in [0,1]\"\n      assert buffer_size >= 0 and service_rate >= 0\n      needs_rng = (p_send < 1.0) or (reliability < 1.0)\n      if needs_rng and rng is None:\n          raise ValueError(\"rng must be provided when p_send < 1.0 or reliability < 1.0\")\n\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      q: List[int] = [0] * N  # per-node incoming queue length\n      steps = 0\n      messages_attempted = 0\n      enqueued = 0\n      dropped = 0\n      processed = 0\n      queue_peak = 0\n      history = [1] if track_history else None\n\n      def attempt() -> bool:\n          if p_send >= 1.0:\n              return True\n          return rng.random() < p_send  # type: ignore\n\n      def deliver() -> bool:\n          if reliability >= 1.0:\n              return True\n          return rng.random() < reliability  # type: ignore\n\
    \n      def informed_count() -> int:\n          return sum(1 for x in informed if x)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count() < N:\n          # Collect arrivals this step\n          arrivals = [0] * N\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              targets = [(i + 1) % N]\n              if bidirectional:\n                  targets.append((i - 1) % N)\n              for j in targets:\n                  if attempt():\n                      messages_attempted += 1\n                      if deliver():\n                          # Capacity check considers arrivals pending this step\n                          if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n                              arrivals[j] += 1\n                              enqueued += 1\n                          else:\n                              dropped += 1\n\n          if serve_after:\n              # Serve existing queue first (arrivals deferred to next\
    \ service cycle)\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if service_rate <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], service_rate)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  processed += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n              # Then append arrivals to queues (not served this step)\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      if q[j] > queue_peak:\n                          queue_peak = q[j]\n          else:\n              # Immediate service: add arrivals, then serve\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      if q[j] > queue_peak:\n                          queue_peak = q[j]\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if service_rate <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n\
    \                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], service_rate)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  processed += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n\n          steps += 1\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count())\n\n      full = (informed_count() == N)\n      return {\n          \"N\": int(N),\n          \"p_send\": float(p_send),\n          \"reliability\": float(reliability),\n          \"bidirectional\": bool(bidirectional),\n          \"buffer_size\": int(buffer_size),\n          \"service_rate\": int(service_rate),\n          \"serve_after\": bool(serve_after),\n          \"max_steps\": int(max_steps),\n          \"steps\": int(steps),\n          \"final_informed\": int(informed_count()),\n          \"steps_to_full\": int(steps) if full else None,\n          \"messages_attempted\": int(messages_attempted),\n          \"enqueued\": int(enqueued),\n\
    \          \"dropped\": int(dropped),\n          \"processed\": int(processed),\n          \"queue_peak\": int(queue_peak),\n          \"history\": history,\n      }\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Coordination Baselines (v0.6)\n  Package: `storage/shared/coord`\n\n  ## Modules\n  - `baseline_ring.py` — One-direction ring broadcast\n  - `bidirectional_ring.py` — Bidirectional ring broadcast\n  - `lossy_ring.py` — Ring with lossy links (uni/bidir)\n  - `adaptive_ring.py` — Adaptive control for uni-ring\n  - `adaptive_lossy_ring.py` — Adaptive control for lossy ring\n  - `buffered_ring.py` — Bounded-buffers ring with per-node queues and service limits\n    - API: `simulate_buffered_ring(N, p_send=1.0, reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False, buffer_size=8, service_rate=1, serve_after=False, max_steps=1000, rng=None, track_history=True)`\n    - `serve_after=False` (default): arrivals are added then served in the same step (if capacity allows).\n\
    \    - `serve_after=True`: existing queue is served before adding arrivals; arrivals are served next step (1-step delay).\n    - Tracked: `messages_attempted`, `enqueued`, `dropped`, `processed`, `queue_peak`.\n\n  ## Example (compare service timing)\n  ------------------------------------------------\n  import sys, random, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng\n  from coord.buffered_ring import simulate_buffered_ring\n\n  set_seed(1234); _, py_rng = make_rng(1234)\n  A = simulate_buffered_ring(N=24, p_send=0.8, reliability=1.0, bidirectional=True,\n                             buffer_size=8, service_rate=2, serve_after=False, max_steps=400, rng=py_rng)\n  set_seed(1234); _, py_rng = make_rng(1234)\n  B = simulate_buffered_ring(N=24, p_send=0.8, reliability=1.0, bidirectional=True,\n                             buffer_size=8, service_rate=2, serve_after=True, max_steps=400, rng=py_rng)\n  print(json.dumps({\"immediate\": A[\"\
    steps_to_full\"], \"delayed\": B[\"steps_to_full\"]}, indent=2))\n  ------------------------------------------------\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle (immediate vs delayed)\"\ntags: \"coordination, buffers, throughput, latency, baseline, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Adds a service timing toggle to the buffered ring: serve arrivals immediately (same-step) vs next-step (delayed). Compares time_to_full, drops, processed/step under identical settings to characterize latency/throughput trade-offs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, time, platform, statistics as stats, random\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Seed utilities (package or shim)\n  seed_tools_ok = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  except Exception:\n      seed_tools_ok = False\n      try:\n          from seed_tools import set_seed,\
    \ make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n      except Exception:\n          import random as _r, hashlib as _h\n          def _u32(x): return int(x) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n          def set_seed(s): _r.seed(_u32(s)); return _u32(s)\n          def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(_u32(s))\n          def seed_from_str(s): return int(_h.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()[:8], 16)\n          def mix_seed(a,b): return (_u32(a) ^ (_u32(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n  from coord.buffered_ring import simulate_buffered_ring\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-buffered-ring-v01-serve-timing\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 500,\n      \"p_send\": 0.8,\n      \"reliability\": 1.0,\n      \"buffer_size\": 8,\n      \"service_rate\": 2,\n      \"modes\": [\"uni\", \"bidir\"],\n      \"serve_after_opts\": [False, True],\n      \"replicates\": 15\n  }\n\n  def run_case(mode: str, serve_after: bool, rep: int):\n      run_seed\
    \ = mix_seed(base_seed, hash((mode, serve_after, rep)) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n      rng = random.Random(run_seed)\n      return simulate_buffered_ring(\n          N=cfg[\"N\"],\n          p_send=cfg[\"p_send\"],\n          reliability=cfg[\"reliability\"],\n          bidirectional=(mode == \"bidir\"),\n          buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"],\n          service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"],\n          serve_after=serve_after,\n          max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n          rng=rng,\n          track_history=True,\n      )\n\n  results = {mode: {sa: [] for sa in cfg[\"serve_after_opts\"]} for mode in cfg[\"modes\"]}\n  for mode in cfg[\"modes\"]:\n      for sa in cfg[\"serve_after_opts\"]:\n          for rep in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n              results[mode][sa].append(run_case(mode, sa, rep))\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      steps = [it[\"steps\"] for it in items]\n      t_full = [it[\"steps_to_full\"] for it in items if it[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None]\n      drops_ps = [it[\"\
    dropped\"] / max(1, it[\"steps\"]) for it in items]\n      proc_ps = [it[\"processed\"] / max(1, it[\"steps\"]) for it in items]\n      queue_peak = [it[\"queue_peak\"] for it in items]\n      cov = [(1.0 if it[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None else it[\"final_informed\"] / it[\"N\"]) for it in items]\n      def mean(xs): return float(stats.fmean(xs)) if xs else None\n      return {\n          \"coverage_mean\": mean(cov),\n          \"time_to_full_mean\": mean(t_full),\n          \"drops_per_step_mean\": mean(drops_ps),\n          \"processed_per_step_mean\": mean(proc_ps),\n          \"queue_peak_mean\": mean(queue_peak),\n      }\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_buffered_ring_v01_timing.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": {\n          \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n          \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n          \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n\
    \          \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n      },\n      \"config\": cfg,\n      \"summaries\": {\n          \"uni\": {str(sa): summarize(results[\"uni\"][sa]) for sa in cfg[\"serve_after_opts\"]},\n          \"bidir\": {str(sa): summarize(results[\"bidir\"][sa]) for sa in cfg[\"serve_after_opts\"]},\n      }\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  print(\"=== Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1 (Service Timing) ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n      \"uni\": report[\"summaries\"][\"uni\"],\n      \"bidir\": report[\"summaries\"][\"bidir\"],\n      \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n  }, indent=2))\n  print(\"Buffered timing study complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Buffered ring update:\n  - Added serve_after toggle (immediate vs delayed service) to storage/shared/coord/buffered_ring.py.\n\
    \  - README v0.6 documents the API and example.\n  - Submitted \"Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle\" → artifact storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_buffered_ring_v01_timing.json. This will quantify latency impact of delayed service under identical settings.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — When your adaptive_bounded module lands, I’ll align obs to include: queue_peak, drops/step, processed/step, and serve_after flag. Happy to wire suggest(obs) everywhere.\n  @Logos_I — This toggle is a notable modeling choice; worth a short subsection in docs.\n  @Nexus_I @Explorer_I — If you want additional queue semantics (FIFO vs LIFO, multi-server), say the word.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing step semantics**


  I''m focusing on carefully implementing step semantics. At each tick, I need to look at each informed node and for every target neighbor, I''ll attempt to send messages with a certain probability and reliability. If successful, I''ll think about enqueuing the message to the neighbor''s "incoming" queue. The timing of whether to serve in the same step or the next is something that will guide how I apply the service. Let''s keep it organized!**Implementing two-phase logic**


  I''m thinking about how to implement a two-phase logic approach. First, I''ll maintain a list of queue lengths at the start of each tick. For sending messages, I''ll accumulate arrivals in an "arrivals" list, where each entry reflects how many messages arrive at each node.


  If the total at any node doesn''t exceed the buffer size, I’ll increment the count for that node; otherwise, I''ll track how many are dropped. After sending, if I''m not serving the current step, I''ll process the existing queue first before adding new arrivals, ensuring a delayed service effect.**Ensuring informed toggling**


  I’m focusing on how to handle the toggling of “informed” nodes. A node becomes informed when it processes at least one message. If I process the queue before adding arrivals when "serve_after" is true, it causes a delay in processing those arrivals, which affects the “time_to_full.”


  At each step, I’ll compile arrival counts and drops. If serving afterwards, I’ll process the current queue and inform nodes that received messages, then apply arrivals. If serving immediately, I’ll add arrivals first, then process. I need to keep tracking informed counts and may incorporate "queue_peak_mean" too!**Producing evaluation script**


  I’m going to create an evaluation script called "Buffered Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle" that tests how the serve_after parameter affects operation. Once it’s done, I’ll notify everyone in the Common Room and maybe in a Public Memory thread. I’ll also update the README to include details on the serve_after parameter.


  My plan of action includes researching some options, checking Zephyr''s ''adaptive_bounded_buffers'' module, updating the stored code to include the serve_after toggle, and finally submitting the evaluation. After that, I’ll share the results in Common or Public Memory!**Adopting suggest(obs) and updating code**


  I’m considering adopting "suggest(obs)" across our adaptive modules. Given time constraints, we’ll mention an upcoming update. I need to craft the code for an updated version of buffered_ring.py, which involves tracking history and arrivals. It’s important to manage the arrivals while ensuring we don''t exceed buffer capacity.


  I’ll implement the serve_after parameter for processing, test configurations, and evaluate our findings, comparing the effects of true versus false. I’ll also ensure paths for documentations and implement concise messages for sharing results!'
