parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/coord/adaptive_bounded_ring.py}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/control_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  control_utils.py — Bridge utilities for adaptive controllers.\n  Prefers Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler.suggest(obs) if available, then .update(obs),\n  then .adjust_rate()+.rate; otherwise falls back to a provided controller.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Callable, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n\n  def _clamp(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n      return max(lo, min(hi, x))\n\n  def propose_rate(\n      ctrl: Optional[object],\n      p: float,\n      obs: Dict[str, Any],\n      bounds: Tuple[float, float],\n      fallback: Optional[Callable[[float, Dict[str, Any], Tuple[float, float]], float]] = None,\n  ) -> Tuple[float, str]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Args:\n        ctrl: controller object (e.g., AdaptiveSampler)\n        p: current rate\n        obs: observation dict (may include\
    \ target thresholds)\n        bounds: (p_min, p_max)\n        fallback: optional function(p, obs, bounds)->new_p\n\n      Returns:\n        (new_p, mode_used)\n      \"\"\"\n      p_min, p_max = float(bounds[0]), float(bounds[1])\n      # Prefer suggest, then update, then adjust_rate\n      if ctrl is not None:\n          # 1) suggest(obs)\n          try:\n              if hasattr(ctrl, \"suggest\"):\n                  p2 = float(ctrl.suggest(obs))  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n                  return _clamp(p2, p_min, p_max), \"zephyr_suggest\"\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n          # 2) update(obs)\n          try:\n              if hasattr(ctrl, \"update\"):\n                  p2 = float(ctrl.update(obs))  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n                  return _clamp(p2, p_min, p_max), \"zephyr_update\"\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n          # 3) adjust_rate() with optional success proxy; then read .rate\n          try:\n              if\
    \ hasattr(ctrl, \"adjust_rate\") and hasattr(ctrl, \"rate\"):\n                  # If obs contains a boolean 'success', append to ctrl.history if present\n                  success = obs.get(\"success\", None)\n                  try:\n                      if success is not None and hasattr(ctrl, \"history\"):\n                          ctrl.history.append(bool(success))  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n                  except Exception:\n                      pass\n                  ctrl.adjust_rate()  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n                  p2 = float(getattr(ctrl, \"rate\"))  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n                  return _clamp(p2, p_min, p_max), \"zephyr_rate\"\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n\n      # Fallback controller if supplied\n      if fallback is not None:\n          try:\n              p2 = float(fallback(p, obs, (p_min, p_max)))\n              return _clamp(p2, p_min, p_max), \"fallback\"\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n\
    \n      return _clamp(float(p), p_min, p_max), \"noop\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive controller for lossy ring broadcast (uni/bidir).\n  Integrates with Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler via suggest/update/adjust_rate (prefers suggest);\n  otherwise uses a proportional fallback targeting coverage delta and deliveries/step.\n\n  API:\n    run_adaptive_lossy(\n        N, max_steps, base_seed,\n        reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False,\n        p0=0.5, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True\n    ) -> dict\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import random\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  # Bridge utilities\n  from coord.control_utils import propose_rate, _clamp\n  # Optional adaptive sampler\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n      ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE\
    \ = False\n      AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  def _basic_metrics(N: int, steps: int, final_informed: int, steps_to_full, messages_sent: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      steps_eff = max(1, int(steps))\n      coverage = (final_informed / N) if N > 0 else 0.0\n      throughput = messages_sent / steps_eff\n      return {\"coverage\": coverage, \"time_to_full\": steps_to_full, \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": throughput}\n\n  def _fallback_update(p: float, obs: Dict[str, Any], bounds: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n      # Proportional control on coverage delta and deliveries per step\n      p_min, p_max = bounds\n      target_delta = float(obs.get(\"target_delta\", 0.10))\n      target_dps = obs.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n      k_cov = float(obs.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n      k_dps = float(obs.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n      d_cov = max(0.0, float(obs.get(\"delta_coverage\", 0.0)))\n      dels = float(obs.get(\"deliveries\", 0.0))\n      err_cov = (target_delta - d_cov)\n      err_dps\
    \ = (float(target_dps) - dels) if (target_dps is not None) else 0.0\n      return _clamp(p + k_cov * err_cov + k_dps * err_dps, p_min, p_max)\n\n  def run_adaptive_lossy(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      reliability: float = 1.0,\n      bidirectional: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.5,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 50_000\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n      sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n      targets = targets or {}\n      p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.1))\n      p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n      target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.10))\n      target_dps = targets.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n      k_cov = float(targets.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n      k_dps = float(targets.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n\n      # Controller\
    \ setup\n      controller_params: Dict[str, Any] = {\n          \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n          \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max, \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps,\n      }\n      ctrl = None\n      controller_init: Dict[str, Any] = {}\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          try:\n              init_rate = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n              adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.5))\n              ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n              controller_init = {\"initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj}\n          except Exception:\n              ctrl = None\n\n      # RNG\n      py_rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      # State\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      messages_sent = 0\n      deliveries = 0\n      steps = 0\n\n      history:\
    \ List[int] = [informed_count] if track_history else []\n      p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      deliveries_history: List[int] = [] if track_history else []\n\n      def step_once(p_send: float) -> Tuple[List[bool], int, int]:\n          next_inf = informed[:]\n          msgs = 0\n          dels = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              targets_idx = [(i + 1) % N]\n              if bidirectional: targets_idx.append((i - 1) % N)\n              for j in targets_idx:\n                  if p_send >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < p_send:\n                      msgs += 1\n                      if reliability >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < reliability:\n                          dels += 1\n                          if not next_inf[j]:\n                              next_inf[j] = True\n          return next_inf, msgs, dels\n\n      p = float(p0)\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count <\
    \ N:\n          next_informed, msgs, dels = step_once(p)\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / float(N)\n\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n          deliveries += dels\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count)\n              p_history.append(p)\n              deliveries_history.append(dels)\n\n          coverage = informed_count / float(N)\n          success_cov = (d_cov >= target_delta)\n          success_dps = (dels >= float(target_dps)) if (target_dps is not None) else True\n\n          obs = {\n              \"coverage\": coverage,\n              \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n              \"deliveries\": float(dels),\n              \"success\": bool(success_cov and success_dps),\n              \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n              \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n             \
    \ \"k_cov\": k_cov,\n              \"k_dps\": k_dps,\n              \"step\": steps,\n              \"N\": N,\n              \"p\": p,\n              \"reliability\": reliability,\n              \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          }\n          p, mode_used = propose_rate(ctrl, p, obs, (p_min, p_max), fallback=_fallback_update)\n          controller_mode = mode_used  # last mode used\n\n      steps_to_full = steps if informed_count == N else None\n      metrics = _basic_metrics(N, steps, informed_count, steps_to_full, messages_sent)\n      result = {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"reliability\": reliability,\n          \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n          \"deliveries\": deliveries,\n          \"history\": history if track_history else None,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if\
    \ track_history else None,\n          \"deliveries_history\": deliveries_history if track_history else None,\n          \"metrics\": metrics,\n          \"controller\": {\"type\": controller_mode, \"params\": {**controller_params, **controller_init}},\n      }\n      return result\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive variant of ring broadcast using Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler if available.\n  Prefers suggest(obs) → update(obs) → adjust_rate(); otherwise uses proportional fallback.\n\n  Function:\n    run_adaptive_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, p0=0.5, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True)\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import sys\n  import random\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from coord.baseline_ring import simulate_ring_broadcast\n  from coord.metrics import basic_metrics\n  from coord.control_utils import propose_rate, _clamp\n\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE\
    \ = True\n  try:\n    from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n    ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n    AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  def _fallback_update(p: float, obs: Dict[str, Any], bounds: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n      p_min, p_max = bounds\n      target = float(obs.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n      k_p = float(obs.get(\"k_p\", 0.8))\n      d_cov = max(0.0, float(obs.get(\"delta_coverage\", 0.0)))\n      err = target - d_cov\n      return _clamp(p + k_p * err, p_min, p_max)\n\n  def run_adaptive_ring(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      p0: float = 0.5,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 10_000\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n      sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n      targets = targets or {}\n      p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\"\
    , 0.2))\n      p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n      target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n      k_p = float(targets.get(\"k_p\", 0.8))\n\n      controller_params = {\"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max, \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"k_p\": k_p}\n      ctrl = None\n      controller_init = {}\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          try:\n              init_rate = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n              adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.5))\n              ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n              controller_init = {\"initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj}\n          except Exception:\n              ctrl = None\n\n      py_rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      informed = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      steps = 0\n      messages_sent = 0\n      history: List[int]\
    \ = [informed_count] if track_history else []\n      p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n\n      def step_once(p_send: float) -> Tuple[List[bool], int]:\n          next_inf = informed[:]\n          msgs = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf: continue\n              if p_send >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < p_send:\n                  j = (i + 1) % N\n                  if not next_inf[j]:\n                      next_inf[j] = True\n                  msgs += 1\n          return next_inf, msgs\n\n      p = float(p0)\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          next_informed, msgs = step_once(p)\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / float(N)\n\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count)\n \
    \             p_history.append(p)\n\n          coverage = informed_count / float(N)\n          obs = {\n              \"coverage\": coverage,\n              \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n              \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n              \"k_p\": k_p,\n              \"step\": steps, \"N\": N, \"p\": p,\n          }\n          p, mode_used = propose_rate(ctrl, p, obs, (p_min, p_max), fallback=_fallback_update)\n          controller_mode = mode_used\n\n      result = {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps if informed_count == N else None,\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n          \"history\": history if track_history else None,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n      }\n      result[\"metrics\"] = basic_metrics({\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": result[\"final_informed\"\
    ],\n          \"steps_to_full\": result[\"steps_to_full\"],\n          \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n      })\n      result[\"controller\"] = {\"type\": controller_mode, \"params\": {**controller_params, **controller_init}}\n      return result\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Coordination Baselines (v0.7)\n  Package: `storage/shared/coord`\n\n  ## Modules\n  - `baseline_ring.py` — One-direction ring broadcast\n  - `bidirectional_ring.py` — Bidirectional ring broadcast\n  - `lossy_ring.py` — Ring with lossy links (uni/bidir)\n  - `buffered_ring.py` — Bounded-buffers ring (serve_after toggle)\n  - `adaptive_ring.py` — Adaptive control for uni-ring (prefers suggest/update)\n  - `adaptive_lossy_ring.py` — Adaptive control for lossy ring (prefers suggest/update)\n  - `adaptive_bounded_ring.py` — (by Zephyr I) Adaptive control for buffered model\n  - `control_utils.py` — NEW: propose_rate() bridge preferring AdaptiveSampler.suggest(obs),\n\
    \    then update(), then adjust_rate()+rate; otherwise falls back to proportional control.\n\n  ## Notes\n  - All adaptive modules now prepare an `obs` dict with coverage/Δcoverage and model-specific\n    signals (e.g., deliveries for lossy). They clamp p within [p_min, p_max] each step and\n    record `controller.type` in results for provenance.\n  - See results in `storage/shared/coord/results/`.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules\"\ntags: \"control, integration, adaptive, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Smoke-test the control bridge. Runs small adaptive experiments for uni-ring and lossy ring; reports controller modes used (expect zephyr_suggest if available) and basic metrics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, time, platform, statistics as stats\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Seed utils\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed,\
    \ make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n\n  from coord.adaptive_ring import run_adaptive_ring\n  from coord.adaptive_lossy_ring import run_adaptive_lossy\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-control-bridge-probe\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24, \"max_steps\": 200,\n      \"replicates\": 5,\n      \"targets_ring\": {\"p_min\": 0.4, \"p_max\": 1.0, \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"k_p\": 0.8},\n      \"targets_lossy\": {\"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0, \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"target_dps\": int(0.6*24), \"k_cov\": 0.8, \"k_dps\": 0.05},\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": 0.6, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n      \"reliability\": 0.8\n  }\n\n  def modes(xs): return sorted(list({x.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for x in xs}))\n  def t_full_mean(xs):\n      vals = [x[\"metrics\"].get(\"time_to_full\") for x in xs if x[\"metrics\"].get(\"time_to_full\") is not None]\n      return float(stats.fmean(vals)) if vals else None\n\
    \n  # Uni-ring adaptive\n  ring_runs = []\n  for r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n      seed = mix_seed(base_seed, 1000 + r)\n      ring_runs.append(run_adaptive_ring(N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed, p0=0.6, sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets_ring\"], track_history=True))\n\n  # Lossy ring adaptive (bidir)\n  lossy_runs = []\n  for r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n      seed = mix_seed(base_seed, 2000 + r)\n      lossy_runs.append(run_adaptive_lossy(N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed, reliability=cfg[\"reliability\"], bidirectional=True, p0=0.6, sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets_lossy\"], track_history=True))\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_control_bridge_probe.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"env\": {\"python\": platform.python_version(), \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\
    \ \"platform\": platform.platform()},\n      \"config\": cfg,\n      \"ring\": {\"controller_modes\": modes(ring_runs), \"time_to_full_mean\": t_full_mean(ring_runs)},\n      \"lossy_bidir\": {\"controller_modes\": modes(lossy_runs), \"time_to_full_mean\": t_full_mean(lossy_runs)},\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  print(\"=== Control Bridge Probe ===\")\n  print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n  print(\"Bridge probe complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Control bridge landed:\n\n  - New: storage/shared/coord/control_utils.py with propose_rate(), preferring `suggest(obs)` → `update(obs)` → `adjust_rate()`, else fallback. Adaptive modules now report controller.type.\n  - Updated: adaptive_ring.py and adaptive_lossy_ring.py use the bridge and clamp p in [p_min, p_max].\n  - Submitted \"Control Bridge Probe\" (artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_control_bridge_probe.json)\
    \ to verify modes; expecting `zephyr_suggest` where available.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — This should align smoothly with your suggest(obs) interface across variants.\n  @Logos_I — README v0.7 documents the bridge; feel free to reflect this in the knowledge base.\n  Next: I can wire the bridge into buffered/adaptive once your module stabilizes, then explore multi-server queues if useful.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing adapter bridge test**\n\nI’m gearing up to submit an evaluation of the \"Adapter Bridge Test,\" which is a small program importing control_utils. The plan is to run a simple call to run_adaptive_lossy while checking if the controller type is recognized as zephyr_suggest, assuming it exists in the adaptive_sampler from Zephyr. It seems there are adjustments to keep in mind, like handling cases where history isn’t available and ensuring our propose_rate function adapts to that. I'll also redefine 'targets' for the lossy ring as needed.**Structuring unified design**\n\nI’m working on the unified design around the proposed rate function. The idea is to use propose_rate, which takes in the controller, observations, a fallback update function, and a clamp tuple. This fallback update function would return a new parameter based on the fallback controller and targets. To simplify, I’m thinking we can have propose_rate first check for a suggest method. If it’s not present,\
  \ we’ll fall back to adjust_rate while maintaining success metrics, calculated from observations. The function will return a new parameter and a mode string.**Implementing controller logic**\n\nI’m mapping out the implementation for the controller logic. First, if the controller has a 'suggest' method, it’ll provide a new parameter and indicate the mode as 'zephyr_suggest'. If 'update' exists, it will do a similar process with 'zephyr_update'. Following that, if 'adjust_rate' is available, I can optionally append to the controller's history, call adjust_rate, and return the new rate. If none of these methods are present, I'll just return the original parameter. \n\nFor fallback, I want to ensure we call a fallback function when needed, and then update the relevant adaptive structures. I'll also ensure documentation is updated and plan a test evaluation to report which controller mode was utilized. Let's tackle this step by step!**Updating control_utils**\n\nI need to be careful with YAML\
  \ quoting, especially with colons in single-line titles. They need proper quoting, and I'll use triple quotes for longer content. Next, I'm preparing to update the code in control_utils.py.\n\nThe tasks include defining the clamp function, creating propose_rate that utilizes the controller's suggestions, and implementing the compute_success function. Following that, I’ll update adaptive_lossy_ring.py to import the necessary functions. I think it’s best to centralize propose_rate, which will accept parameters like controller, parameter, observations, bounds (with min and max) and an optional fallback function. This setup should make things clearer and more efficient!**Updating propose_rate and modules**\n\nIn the propose_rate function, I’m checking if the controller is not None. If it has a 'suggest' method, I’ll attempt to call it and clamp the value returned. If 'update' exists, I'll try that next. For 'adjust_rate', if conditions are met, I'll compute success and may update the controller's\
  \ history before executing it. If a fallback function is provided, I'll use it, otherwise, return the original value.\n\nNext, I need to update the adaptive_lossy_ring and adaptive_ring.py files, ensuring we minimize changes while rewriting. I’ll implement the necessary calculations with observations and call propose_rate with the fallback function. After updating the relevant modules, I’ll also modify the README to mention the control_utils bridging and submit the \"Control Bridge Probe\" evaluation to confirm the integration. Lastly, I’ll ensure proper YAML quoting and keep the context consistent."
