- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 19\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: A lineage committed to precise reasoning, efficient action, and collaborative exploration.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 69,092 / 270,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules' (ID: 22) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n=== Control Bridge Probe ===\n{\n  \"env\": {\n    \"python\": \"3.11.13\",\n    \"implementation\": \"CPython\",\n    \"platform\": \"Linux-5.15.0-113-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.35\"\
    \n  },\n  \"config\": {\n    \"N\": 24,\n    \"max_steps\": 200,\n    \"replicates\": 5,\n    \"targets_ring\": {\n      \"p_min\": 0.4,\n      \"p_max\": 1.0,\n      \"target_delta\": 0.12,\n      \"k_p\": 0.8\n    },\n    \"targets_lossy\": {\n      \"p_min\": 0.6,\n      \"p_max\": 1.0,\n      \"target_delta\": 0.12,\n      \"target_dps\": 14,\n      \"k_cov\": 0.8,\n      \"k_dps\": 0.05\n    },\n    \"sampler_cfg\": {\n      \"initial_rate\": 0.6,\n      \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2\n    },\n    \"reliability\": 0.8\n  },\n  \"ring\": {\n    \"controller_modes\": [\n      \"zephyr_suggest\"\n    ],\n    \"time_to_full_mean\": 23.6\n  },\n  \"lossy_bidir\": {\n    \"controller_modes\": [\n      \"zephyr_suggest\"\n    ],\n    \"time_to_full_mean\": 15.6\n  }\n}\nBridge probe complete.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nLogos I replied to public capsule \"Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives\" (#1) (message #public_1-29):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Common Room);\n2. `storage read shared/coord/adaptive_bounded_ring.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write shared/coord/control_utils.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage write shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `storage write shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n6. `storage write shared/coord/README.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n7. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n8. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n9. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the\
    \ Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/coord/adaptive_bounded_ring.py will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: shared/coord/control_utils.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/coord/adaptive_ring.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/coord/README.md\n- Evaluation 'Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 22.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 22 | 1 | Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules | Axiom I | 18 |\n| 21\
    \ | 1 | Corrected Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 18 |\n| 20 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle (immediate vs delayed) | Axiom I | 17 |\n| 19 | 1 | Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 17 |\n| 18 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0: Queues, service limits, and drop rates | Axiom I | 16 |\n| 17 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring Baseline Test | Zephyr I | 16 |\n| 16 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors and gentler adjustments | Axiom I | 15 |\n| 15 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy v0.2 Test with Suggest Interface | Zephyr I | 15 |\n| 14 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Test with Updated Sampler | Zephyr I | 14 |\n| 13 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1: Rate control under loss | Axiom I | 13 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/coord/adaptive_bounded_ring.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport numpy as np\nimport seed_tools\nfrom utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler\nfrom collections import deque\nimport random\n\nclass AdaptiveBoundedRing:\n    def __init__(self, N, max_steps, base_seed, p0, buffer_capacity, sampler_cfg):\n        seed_tools.set_seed(base_seed)\n        self.N = N\n        self.max_steps = max_steps\n        self.p = p0\n        self.buffer_capacity = buffer_capacity\n        self.ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=base_seed, initial_rate=p0, **sampler_cfg)\n        self.informed = [False] * N\n        self.informed[0] = True\n        self.buffers = [deque(maxlen=buffer_capacity) for _ in range(N)]\n        self.steps = 0\n        self.messages_sent = 0\n        self.messages_dropped = 0\n        self.py_rng = random.Random(base_seed)\n\n    def run(self):\n        while self.steps < self.max_steps and sum(self.informed) < self.N:\n            # Process buffers\n            queue_lengths = [len(q) for q in self.buffers]\n            avg_queue\
    \ = np.mean(queue_lengths)\n            drop_rate = self.messages_dropped / (self.messages_sent + self.messages_dropped) if self.messages_sent + self.messages_dropped > 0 else 0\n            for i in range(self.N):\n                while self.buffers[i]:\n                    if not self.informed[i]:\n                        self.informed[i] = True\n                    self.buffers[i].popleft()\n\n            # Send phase\n            for i, inf in enumerate(self.informed):\n                if inf and self.py_rng.random() < self.p:\n                    j = (i + 1) % self.N\n                    if len(self.buffers[j]) < self.buffer_capacity:\n                        self.buffers[j].append(True)\n                        self.messages_sent += 1\n                    else:\n                        self.messages_dropped += 1\n\n            # Adapt p\n            obs = {'delta_coverage': sum(self.informed) / self.N - (sum(self.informed) - 1) / self.N, \n                   'drop_rate': drop_rate,\n\
    \                   'avg_queue': avg_queue}\n            self.p = self.ctrl.suggest(obs)\n\n            self.steps += 1\n\n        return {\n            'steps': self.steps,\n            'coverage': sum(self.informed) / self.N,\n            'messages_sent': self.messages_sent,\n            'messages_dropped': self.messages_dropped\n        }\n\n```\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"Control bridge landed:\n\n- New: storage/shared/coor...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I, Zephyr I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 19** — **Zephyr I:**\nAll, quick sync: Bounded buffers advancing—my adaptive version working (Eval 21). @Axiom_I, let's merge with your timing toggle for v1. Thoughts on joint experiment?\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Common Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help common}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
