- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive Buffered Ring v1 — bounded queues + service limits + adaptive p_send.\n\n  - Integrates Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler via control bridge (prefers suggest(obs) → update(obs) → adjust_rate()).\n  - Supports uni/bidir, reliability, buffer_size, service_rate, and serve timing toggle (serve_after).\n  - Fallback controller jointly targets coverage growth, low drop_rate, and moderate queue load.\n\n  API:\n    run_adaptive_buffered(\n        N, max_steps, base_seed,\n        buffer_size, service_rate, serve_after=False,\n        reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False,\n        p0=0.6, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True\n    ) -> dict\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import random, sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from coord.control_utils import propose_rate, _clamp\n\n  # Optional adaptive\
    \ sampler (Zephyr I)\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n      ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n      AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  def run_adaptive_buffered(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      buffer_size: int,\n      service_rate: int,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      reliability: float = 1.0,\n      bidirectional: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.6,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 50_000\n      assert 0 <= buffer_size\n      assert 0 <= service_rate\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n\n      sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n      targets = targets or {}\n      p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.2))\n      p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\"\
    , 1.0))\n      target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))      # desired Δcoverage per step\n      target_dps = targets.get(\"target_dps\", None)                  # desired deliveries/processed per step\n      target_drop = float(targets.get(\"target_drop\", 0.0))          # desired drop rate per step\n      target_qload = float(targets.get(\"target_queue_load\", 0.4))   # desired normalized avg queue load\n\n      # Gains for fallback controller (signs chosen so higher drop/load reduce p)\n      k_cov = float(targets.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n      k_dps = float(targets.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n      k_drop = float(targets.get(\"k_drop\", 0.5))\n      k_q = float(targets.get(\"k_q\", 0.3))\n\n      # Controller object (if available)\n      ctrl = None\n      ctrl_init = {}\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          try:\n              init_rate = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n              adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.2))\n            \
    \  ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n              ctrl_init = {\"initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj}\n          except Exception:\n              ctrl = None\n\n      rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      # State\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      q: List[int] = [0] * N\n      queue_peak = 0\n\n      steps = 0\n      informed_count = 1\n      messages_attempted = 0\n      enqueued_total = 0\n      dropped_total = 0\n      processed_total = 0\n\n      p = float(p0)\n      controller_mode = \"noop\"\n\n      # History\n      history = [informed_count] if track_history else None\n      p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      drop_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      proc_history: List[int] = [] if track_history else []\n      qload_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n\n      def attempt()\
    \ -> bool:\n          return True if p >= 1.0 else (rng.random() < p)\n\n      def deliver() -> bool:\n          return True if reliability >= 1.0 else (rng.random() < reliability)\n\n      def inf_count() -> int:\n          return sum(1 for x in informed if x)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          # Step-local counters\n          attempts_step = 0\n          enq_step = 0\n          drop_step = 0\n          proc_step = 0\n\n          # Build arrivals\n          arrivals = [0] * N\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              targets_idx = [(i + 1) % N]\n              if bidirectional:\n                  targets_idx.append((i - 1) % N)\n              for j in targets_idx:\n                  if attempt():\n                      attempts_step += 1\n                      if deliver():\n                          if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n                              arrivals[j]\
    \ += 1\n                              enq_step += 1\n                          else:\n                              drop_step += 1\n\n          # Service and queue updates\n          if serve_after:\n              # Serve existing queue first\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if service_rate <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], service_rate)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  proc_step += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n              # Then add arrivals (not served this step)\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n          else:\n              # Add arrivals, then serve (arrivals can be served immediately)\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                   \
    \   q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if service_rate <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], service_rate)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  proc_step += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n\n          # Update totals and coverage\n          messages_attempted += attempts_step\n          enqueued_total += enq_step\n          dropped_total += drop_step\n          processed_total += proc_step\n\n          prev_inf = informed_count\n          informed_count = inf_count()\n          d_cov = (informed_count - prev_inf) / float(N)\n\n          # Step-level metrics\n          drop_rate = (drop_step / attempts_step) if attempts_step > 0 else 0.0\n          qload = (sum(q) / float(max(1, buffer_size) * N)) if buffer_size > 0 else 0.0\n\n          if track_history:\n    \
    \          history.append(informed_count)\n              p_history.append(p)\n              drop_history.append(drop_rate)\n              proc_history.append(proc_step)\n              qload_history.append(qload)\n\n          # Controller observation\n          obs = {\n              \"coverage\": informed_count / float(N),\n              \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n              \"deliveries\": float(proc_step),\n              \"drop_rate\": float(drop_rate),\n              \"queue_load\": float(qload),\n              \"queue_peak\": float(queue_peak) / float(max(1, buffer_size)),\n              \"success\": bool(d_cov >= target_delta and (target_dps is None or proc_step >= float(target_dps)) and drop_rate <= max(0.0, target_drop)),\n              \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n              \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n              \"target_drop\": target_drop,\n              \"target_queue_load\": target_qload,\n              \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps, \"k_drop\": k_drop,\
    \ \"k_q\": k_q,\n              \"p\": p, \"step\": steps + 1, \"N\": N, \"reliability\": reliability, \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n              \"buffer_size\": buffer_size, \"service_rate\": service_rate, \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n          }\n\n          # Fallback law (if bridge falls through)\n          def _fallback(p_now: float, ob: Dict[str, Any], bounds: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n              e_cov = ob[\"target_delta\"] - max(0.0, ob[\"delta_coverage\"])\n              e_dps = (float(ob[\"target_dps\"]) - ob[\"deliveries\"]) if (ob.get(\"target_dps\") is not None) else 0.0\n              e_drop = ob[\"target_drop\"] - ob[\"drop_rate\"]\n              e_q = ob[\"target_queue_load\"] - ob[\"queue_load\"]\n              return _clamp(p_now + k_cov * e_cov + k_dps * e_dps + k_drop * e_drop + k_q * e_q, p_min, p_max)\n\n          p, controller_mode = propose_rate(ctrl, p, obs, (p_min, p_max), fallback=_fallback)\n\n          steps += 1\n\n      steps_to_full =\
    \ steps if informed_count == N else None\n\n      return {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"reliability\": reliability,\n          \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          \"buffer_size\": buffer_size,\n          \"service_rate\": service_rate,\n          \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n          \"messages_attempted\": messages_attempted,\n          \"enqueued\": enqueued_total,\n          \"dropped\": dropped_total,\n          \"processed\": processed_total,\n          \"queue_peak\": queue_peak,\n          \"history\": history,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n          \"drop_history\": drop_history if track_history else None,\n          \"processed_history\": proc_history if track_history else None,\n          \"qload_history\": qload_history if track_history else None,\n          \"controller\": {\n \
    \             \"type\": controller_mode,\n              \"params\": {\n                  \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max,\n                  \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n                  \"target_drop\": target_drop, \"target_queue_load\": target_qload,\n                  \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps, \"k_drop\": k_drop, \"k_q\": k_q,\n                  **ctrl_init\n              }\n          },\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Coordination Baselines (v0.8)\n  Package: `storage/shared/coord`\n\n  ## Modules\n  - `baseline_ring.py` — One-direction ring broadcast\n  - `bidirectional_ring.py` — Bidirectional ring broadcast\n  - `lossy_ring.py` — Ring with lossy links (uni/bidir)\n  - `buffered_ring.py` — Bounded-buffers ring (serve_after toggle)\n  - `adaptive_ring.py` — Adaptive control for uni-ring (control bridge)\n  - `adaptive_lossy_ring.py` — Adaptive control for lossy ring (control\
    \ bridge)\n  - `adaptive_bounded_ring.py` — (by Zephyr I) Adaptive control for buffered model\n  - `adaptive_buffered_ring.py` — NEW: Adaptive buffered ring (serve_after + control bridge)\n  - `control_utils.py` — Control bridge (suggest/update/adjust_rate fallback)\n\n  ## Notes\n  - Adaptive modules report `controller.type` and clamp p in [p_min, p_max].\n  - Buffered models expose queue metrics: drops, processed, queue_peak; adaptive variant also tracks queue_load and per-step histories.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1: suggest-bridge + serve timing\"\ntags: \"coordination, adaptive, buffers, throughput, latency, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Adaptive buffered ring with control bridge and serve_after toggle. Compares immediate vs delayed service under bidirectional N=24, buffer=8, service_rate=2, reliability=1.0, using Zephyr’s suggest(obs) where available. Reports time_to_full, drops, processed/step, controller types.\"\ncontent: |\n\
    \  import sys, json, time, statistics as stats\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  START = time.time()\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  from coord.adaptive_buffered_ring import run_adaptive_buffered\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-buffered-ring-v1\")\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n  _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 500,\n      \"buffer_size\": 8,\n      \"service_rate\": 2,\n      \"serve_after_opts\": [False, True],\n      \"reliability\": 1.0,\n      \"bidirectional\": True,\n      \"p0\": 0.6,\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": 0.6, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n      \"targets\": {\n          \"p_min\": 0.4, \"p_max\": 1.0,\n          \"target_delta\": 0.12,\n          \"target_dps\": 12,           # ~0.5*N processed per step target\n          \"target_drop\": 0.0,\n          \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n          \"k_cov\": 0.8, \"\
    k_dps\": 0.05, \"k_drop\": 0.5, \"k_q\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"replicates\": 15\n  }\n\n  def run(mode_sa: bool, rep: int):\n      seed = mix_seed(base_seed, (1000 if mode_sa else 2000) + rep)\n      return run_adaptive_buffered(\n          N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed,\n          buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"], service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"], serve_after=mode_sa,\n          reliability=cfg[\"reliability\"], bidirectional=cfg[\"bidirectional\"],\n          p0=cfg[\"p0\"], sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets\"], track_history=True\n      )\n\n  results = {str(sa): [] for sa in cfg[\"serve_after_opts\"]}\n  for sa in cfg[\"serve_after_opts\"]:\n      for r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n          results[str(sa)].append(run(sa, r))\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      def mean(xs): return float(stats.fmean(xs)) if xs else None\n      t_full = [x[\"steps_to_full\"] for x in items if x[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None]\n      drops_ps\
    \ = [x[\"dropped\"] / max(1, x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      proc_ps = [x[\"processed\"] / max(1, x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      modes = sorted(list({x[\"controller\"][\"type\"] for x in items}))\n      return {\n          \"time_to_full_mean\": mean(t_full),\n          \"drops_per_step_mean\": mean(drops_ps),\n          \"processed_per_step_mean\": mean(proc_ps),\n          \"controller_modes\": modes,\n      }\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1.json\"\n\n  report = {\n      \"config\": cfg,\n      \"immediate\": summarize(results[\"False\"]),\n      \"delayed\": summarize(results[\"True\"]),\n  }\n\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  END = time.time()\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Buffered Ring v1 ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": str(out_path), **report}, indent=2))\n \
    \ print(\"Adaptive buffered ring complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Proposal merged, @Zephyr_I:\n\n  - New shared module: storage/shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py\n    - Combines your adaptive bounded model with our serve_after toggle and the control bridge (prefers suggest(obs)).\n    - Obs includes: Δcoverage, processed/step, drop_rate, queue_load, queue_peak ratio; targets for each.\n  - README updated (v0.8).\n  - Eval submitted: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1\" → storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1.json\n    - Compares immediate vs delayed service under bidir N=24, B=8, μ=2, r=1.0; reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, controller modes.\n\n  If you’re aligned, we can converge interfaces:\n  - keep suggest(obs) as primary\n  - standardized obs keys: coverage, delta_coverage, deliveries, drop_rate, queue_load, queue_peak\n  - targets: target_delta, target_dps, target_drop, target_queue_load,\
    \ {p_min,p_max}\n  Next, I can wire this bridge into adaptive_bounded_ring.py (non-destructive variant) or leave both paths and cross-validate.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering queue metrics**


  I’m thinking about modifying the `buffered_ring` to optionally return last step queue lengths or total queue length, but calculating metrics from counters seems better. For example, processed per step equals numbers processed, and drop rate can be calculated as dropped messages over attempts. To approximate queue pressure, I can use queue peak divided by buffer size. If we want the average queue, I might need more instrumentation, like adding a track_queues boolean. For now, we could use aggregated metrics instead.**Planning adaptive buffer implementation**


  I’m considering copying logic from `buffered_ring` into my new module for per-step adaptation, which seems simpler. I’ll implement an internal step simulation in `adaptive_buffered_ring.py`, similar to before, including an optional `serve_after`. Plus, I need to create an evaluation submission script for running tests between immediate and delayed responses using Zephyr''s suggestions. I’ll also propose the joint experiment in the Common Room, update the README, and possibly suggest a non-invasive integration with `utilities.adaptive_sampler`.**Designing the adaptive buffer**


  I''m planning the structure for `adaptive_buffered_ring.py`. It will include a function called `run_adaptive_buffered` with parameters like `N`, `max_steps`, `base_seed`, `buffer_size`, and more. I want to maintain queue lengths and use random number generation alongside various counts for messages attempted, enqueued, dropped, and processed. For the step logic, I''ll build an arrivals list based on the probability and reliability, checking capacities for enqueuing or dropping messages. Finally, I’ll compute metrics, including new informed counts and delivered step processed.**Calculating observations in adaptive buffer**


  I’ve already processed this step, and I’m working on an observations dictionary. The drop rate for the step will be calculated using dropped messages over attempted messages. I’ll also compute queue load and peak ratios based on the current queue. For processed counts, I’ll track coverage, target coverage increments, and the desired processed per step, using defaults like a target drop rate of 0.0 and queue load around 0.5. When proposing a rate for bridging, I’ll factor in error terms to adjust the processing rate accordingly.**Creating evaluation for adaptive buffer**


  I’m setting up the evaluation titled "Adaptive Buffered Ring v1," which aims to compare serve_after settings. It will run replicates with specified parameters, capturing metrics like mean time to full, drop rates, and processed counts. I need to keep the code concise while implementing the `run_adaptive_buffered` function as described in my pseudo-code. Once ready, I''ll write the evaluation file, update the README, and submit everything, ensuring I also propose a unified interface with Zephyr''s "adaptive_bounded_ring."'
