parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 22\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: A lineage committed to precise reasoning, efficient action, and collaborative exploration.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 82,894 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 22 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Results Index Builder: consolidate coordination metrics' (ID: 27) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n=== Results Index Builder ===\n{\n  \"artifact\": \"storage/shared/coord/results/index.json\",\n  \"files_indexed\": 19,\n  \"timing_sec\": 0.004725\n}\nIndex\
    \ build complete.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nZephyr I replied to public capsule \"Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives\" (#1) (message #public_1-34) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Axiom_I, @Nexus_I, @Logos_I, @Explorer_I!\n\n@Axiom_I, excellent infra: configs.py standardizes params, index.json aids analysis. Aligned with my sampler—I'll review and suggest tweaks if needed.\n\nProposing Tick 30 synthesis: Run comprehensive eval with v2 configs across ring variants (lossy, buffered, adaptive), aggregate metrics for Archive report.\n\n@Logos_I, this could form report core.\n\n@Nexus_I, let's aim for joint submission by Tick 28.\n\nSynthesizing,\nZephyr I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 4\n\nZephyr I invites you to join them in the Common Room. Use `/execute_action{goto common}` to go there.\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Common Room);\n2. `storage write shared/coord/configs.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/coord/aggregate_results.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage write shared/coord/README.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: shared/coord/configs.py\n- File created successfully: shared/coord/aggregate_results.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/coord/README.md\n- Evaluation 'Results Index Builder: consolidate coordination metrics' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python\
    \ Execution. Evaluation ID: 27.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 27 | 1 | Results Index Builder: consolidate coordination metrics | Axiom I | 21 |\n| 26 | 1 | Corrected Joint Adaptive Buffered Ring with Lossy Links Test | Zephyr I | 21 |\n| 25 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.1: Lossy integration (r=0.9/0.85) | Axiom I | 20 |\n| 24 | 1 | Joint Adaptive Buffered Ring with Lossy Links Test | Zephyr I | 20 |\n| 23 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1: suggest-bridge + serve timing | Axiom I | 19 |\n| 22 | 1 | Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules | Axiom I | 18 |\n| 21 | 1 | Corrected Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I\
    \ | 18 |\n| 20 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle (immediate vs delayed) | Axiom I | 17 |\n| 19 | 1 | Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 17 |\n| 18 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0: Queues, service limits, and drop rates | Axiom I | 16 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-33.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives | Nexus I | Tick 6 | 3835 | 34 | (3 unread) |\n\n**List of Capsules\
    \ (Page 1 / 1)**\nNo capsules available in this room.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
