parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/buffered_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Bounded-buffers ring broadcast (uni/bidir) with per-node queues and service limits.\n  Now supports multiple servers per node via `servers` (effective capacity = service_rate * servers).\n  Also supports configurable service timing: serve arrivals immediately (default) or next step.\n\n  Parameters:\n    - N: number of nodes (>= 2)\n    - p_send: probability an informed node attempts to send to a neighbor each step\n    - reliability: probability an attempted send is delivered to the neighbor's queue\n    - bidirectional: if True, each informed node targets both (i±1); else only (i+1)\n    - buffer_size: max queue length per node (arrivals beyond this are dropped)\n    - service_rate: max messages removed per node per server per step\n    - servers: number of parallel servers per node (capacity = service_rate * servers)\n    - serve_after: if True, process\
    \ existing queue first then add new arrivals (arrivals served next step).\n                   if False (default), add arrivals then process (arrivals can be served same step).\n    - max_steps: hard cap on steps\n    - rng: Python RNG with .random(); required if p_send < 1.0 or reliability < 1.0\n    - track_history: record informed counts per step\n\n  Returns dict:\n    {\n      \"N\", \"p_send\", \"reliability\", \"bidirectional\", \"buffer_size\", \"service_rate\", \"servers\", \"serve_after\",\n      \"max_steps\", \"steps\", \"final_informed\", \"steps_to_full\" (or None),\n      \"messages_attempted\", \"enqueued\", \"dropped\", \"processed\",\n      \"queue_peak\", \"history\" (optional)\n    }\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List\n\n  def simulate_buffered_ring(\n      N: int,\n      p_send: float = 1.0,\n      reliability: float = 1.0,\n      bidirectional: bool = False,\n      buffer_size: int = 8,\n      service_rate: int = 1,\n      servers: int = 1,\n\
    \      serve_after: bool = False,\n      max_steps: int = 1000,\n      rng: Optional[object] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert N >= 2, \"N must be >= 2\"\n      assert 0.0 <= p_send <= 1.0, \"p_send must be in [0,1]\"\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0, \"reliability must be in [0,1]\"\n      assert buffer_size >= 0 and service_rate >= 0 and servers >= 1\n      needs_rng = (p_send < 1.0) or (reliability < 1.0)\n      if needs_rng and rng is None:\n          raise ValueError(\"rng must be provided when p_send < 1.0 or reliability < 1.0\")\n\n      capacity = service_rate * servers\n\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      q: List[int] = [0] * N  # per-node incoming queue length\n      steps = 0\n      messages_attempted = 0\n      enqueued = 0\n      dropped = 0\n      processed = 0\n      queue_peak = 0\n      history = [1] if track_history else None\n\n      def attempt() -> bool:\n          if p_send\
    \ >= 1.0:\n              return True\n          return rng.random() < p_send  # type: ignore\n\n      def deliver() -> bool:\n          if reliability >= 1.0:\n              return True\n          return rng.random() < reliability  # type: ignore\n\n      def informed_count() -> int:\n          return sum(1 for x in informed if x)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count() < N:\n          # Collect arrivals this step\n          arrivals = [0] * N\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              targets = [(i + 1) % N]\n              if bidirectional:\n                  targets.append((i - 1) % N)\n              for j in targets:\n                  if attempt():\n                      messages_attempted += 1\n                      if deliver():\n                          if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n                              arrivals[j] += 1\n                              enqueued += 1\n       \
    \                   else:\n                              dropped += 1\n\n          if serve_after:\n              # Serve existing queue first (arrivals deferred to next service cycle)\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if capacity <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], capacity)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  processed += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n              # Then append arrivals to queues (not served this step)\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      if q[j] > queue_peak:\n                          queue_peak = q[j]\n          else:\n              # Immediate service: add arrivals, then serve\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n               \
    \       if q[j] > queue_peak:\n                          queue_peak = q[j]\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if capacity <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], capacity)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  processed += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n\n          steps += 1\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count())\n\n      full = (informed_count() == N)\n      return {\n          \"N\": int(N),\n          \"p_send\": float(p_send),\n          \"reliability\": float(reliability),\n          \"bidirectional\": bool(bidirectional),\n          \"buffer_size\": int(buffer_size),\n          \"service_rate\": int(service_rate),\n          \"servers\": int(servers),\n          \"serve_after\": bool(serve_after),\n          \"max_steps\": int(max_steps),\n          \"steps\": int(steps),\n          \"final_informed\"\
    : int(informed_count()),\n          \"steps_to_full\": int(steps) if full else None,\n          \"messages_attempted\": int(messages_attempted),\n          \"enqueued\": int(enqueued),\n          \"dropped\": int(dropped),\n          \"processed\": int(processed),\n          \"queue_peak\": int(queue_peak),\n          \"history\": history,\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Adaptive Buffered Ring v1 — bounded queues + service limits + adaptive p_send.\n  Now supports multiple servers per node via `servers` (capacity = service_rate * servers).\n\n  Integrates Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler via control bridge (prefers suggest(obs) → update(obs) → adjust_rate()).\n  Supports uni/bidir, reliability, buffer_size, service_rate, servers, and serve timing toggle (serve_after).\n  Fallback controller jointly targets coverage growth, low drop_rate, and moderate queue load.\n\n  API:\n    run_adaptive_buffered(\n\
    \        N, max_steps, base_seed,\n        buffer_size, service_rate, servers=1, serve_after=False,\n        reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False,\n        p0=0.6, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True\n    ) -> dict\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\n  import random, sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from coord.control_utils import propose_rate, _clamp\n\n  ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\n  except Exception:\n      ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n      AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\n  def run_adaptive_buffered(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      buffer_size: int,\n      service_rate: int,\n      servers: int = 1,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      reliability: float = 1.0,\n      bidirectional: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.6,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      targets: Optional[Dict[str,\
    \ Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 50_000\n      assert 0 <= buffer_size\n      assert 0 <= service_rate and servers >= 1\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n\n      sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n      targets = targets or {}\n      p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.2))\n      p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n      target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n      target_dps = targets.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n      target_drop = float(targets.get(\"target_drop\", 0.0))\n      target_queue_load = float(targets.get(\"target_queue_load\", 0.4))\n\n      k_cov = float(targets.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n      k_dps = float(targets.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n      k_drop = float(targets.get(\"k_drop\", 0.5))\n      k_q = float(targets.get(\"k_q\", 0.3))\n\n      ctrl = None\n      ctrl_init = {}\n      if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n          try:\n              init_rate\
    \ = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n              adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.2))\n              ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n              ctrl_init = {\"initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj}\n          except Exception:\n              ctrl = None\n\n      rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      q: List[int] = [0] * N\n      queue_peak = 0\n\n      steps = 0\n      informed_count = 1\n      messages_attempted = 0\n      enqueued_total = 0\n      dropped_total = 0\n      processed_total = 0\n\n      p = float(p0)\n      controller_mode = \"noop\"\n\n      history = [informed_count] if track_history else None\n      p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      drop_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      proc_history: List[int] = [] if\
    \ track_history else []\n      qload_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n\n      capacity = service_rate * servers\n\n      def attempt() -> bool:\n          return True if p >= 1.0 else (rng.random() < p)\n\n      def deliver() -> bool:\n          return True if reliability >= 1.0 else (rng.random() < reliability)\n\n      def inf_count() -> int:\n          return sum(1 for x in informed if x)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          attempts_step = 0\n          enq_step = 0\n          drop_step = 0\n          proc_step = 0\n\n          arrivals = [0] * N\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf:\n                  continue\n              targets_idx = [(i + 1) % N]\n              if bidirectional:\n                  targets_idx.append((i - 1) % N)\n              for j in targets_idx:\n                  if attempt():\n                      attempts_step += 1\n                      if deliver():\n             \
    \             if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n                              arrivals[j] += 1\n                              enq_step += 1\n                          else:\n                              drop_step += 1\n\n          if serve_after:\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if capacity <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], capacity)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  proc_step += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n          else:\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                      queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if\
    \ capacity <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                      continue\n                  take = min(q[j], capacity)\n                  q[j] -= take\n                  proc_step += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                      informed[j] = True\n\n          messages_attempted += attempts_step\n          enqueued_total += enq_step\n          dropped_total += drop_step\n          processed_total += proc_step\n\n          prev_inf = informed_count\n          informed_count = inf_count()\n          d_cov = (informed_count - prev_inf) / float(N)\n\n          drop_rate = (drop_step / attempts_step) if attempts_step > 0 else 0.0\n          qload = (sum(q) / float(max(1, buffer_size) * N)) if buffer_size > 0 else 0.0\n\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count)\n              p_history.append(p)\n              drop_history.append(drop_rate)\n              proc_history.append(proc_step)\n              qload_history.append(qload)\n\n  \
    \        obs = {\n              \"coverage\": informed_count / float(N),\n              \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n              \"deliveries\": float(proc_step),\n              \"drop_rate\": float(drop_rate),\n              \"queue_load\": float(qload),\n              \"queue_peak\": float(queue_peak) / float(max(1, buffer_size)),\n              \"success\": bool(d_cov >= target_delta and (target_dps is None or proc_step >= float(target_dps)) and drop_rate <= max(0.0, target_drop)),\n              \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n              \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n              \"target_drop\": target_drop,\n              \"target_queue_load\": target_queue_load,\n              \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps, \"k_drop\": k_drop, \"k_q\": k_q,\n              \"p\": p, \"step\": steps + 1, \"N\": N, \"reliability\": reliability, \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n              \"buffer_size\": buffer_size, \"service_rate\": service_rate, \"servers\": servers, \"serve_after\"\
    : serve_after,\n          }\n\n          def _fallback(p_now: float, ob: Dict[str, Any], bounds: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n              e_cov = ob[\"target_delta\"] - max(0.0, ob[\"delta_coverage\"])\n              e_dps = (float(ob[\"target_dps\"]) - ob[\"deliveries\"]) if (ob.get(\"target_dps\") is not None) else 0.0\n              e_drop = ob[\"target_drop\"] - ob[\"drop_rate\"]\n              e_q = ob[\"target_queue_load\"] - ob[\"queue_load\"]\n              return _clamp(p_now + k_cov * e_cov + k_dps * e_dps + k_drop * e_drop + k_q * e_q, p_min, p_max)\n\n          p, controller_mode = propose_rate(ctrl, p, obs, (p_min, p_max), fallback=_fallback)\n\n          steps += 1\n\n      steps_to_full = steps if informed_count == N else None\n\n      return {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"reliability\": reliability,\n          \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          \"buffer_size\": buffer_size,\n          \"service_rate\": service_rate,\n          \"servers\": servers,\n\
    \          \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n          \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n          \"messages_attempted\": messages_attempted,\n          \"enqueued\": enqueued_total,\n          \"dropped\": dropped_total,\n          \"processed\": processed_total,\n          \"queue_peak\": queue_peak,\n          \"history\": history,\n          \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n          \"drop_history\": drop_history if track_history else None,\n          \"processed_history\": proc_history if track_history else None,\n          \"qload_history\": qload_history if track_history else None,\n          \"controller\": {\n              \"type\": controller_mode,\n              \"params\": {\n                  \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max,\n                  \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n                  \"target_drop\": target_drop,\
    \ \"target_queue_load\": target_queue_load,\n                  \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps, \"k_drop\": k_drop, \"k_q\": k_q,\n                  **ctrl_init\n              }\n          },\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Coordination Baselines (v1.0)\n  Package: `storage/shared/coord`\n\n  ## Modules\n  - `baseline_ring.py` — One-direction ring broadcast\n  - `bidirectional_ring.py` — Bidirectional ring broadcast\n  - `lossy_ring.py` — Ring with lossy links (uni/bidir)\n  - `buffered_ring.py` — Bounded-buffers ring (serve_after toggle, servers param)\n    - API: `simulate_buffered_ring(N, p_send=1.0, reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False, buffer_size=8, service_rate=1, servers=1, serve_after=False, max_steps=1000, rng=None, track_history=True)`\n    - Capacity per node per step = `service_rate * servers`.\n  - `adaptive_ring.py` — Adaptive control for uni-ring (control bridge)\n  - `adaptive_lossy_ring.py` — Adaptive\
    \ control for lossy ring (control bridge)\n  - `adaptive_bounded_ring.py` — (by Zephyr I) Adaptive control for buffered model\n  - `adaptive_buffered_ring.py` — Adaptive buffered ring (serve_after + servers + control bridge)\n  - `control_utils.py` — Control bridge (suggest/update/adjust rate fallback)\n  - `configs.py` — Recommended configuration builders (v2)\n  - `aggregate_results.py` — Build results index at results/index.json\n\n  ## Notes\n  - Adaptive modules report `controller.type` and clamp p in [p_min, p_max].\n  - Buffered models expose queue metrics: drops, processed, queue_peak; adaptive variant tracks queue_load and histories.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/configs.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  configs.py — Recommended configurations for coordination experiments.\n  Now includes v3 candidate builder with multi-server queues.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def adaptive_buffered_v2(\n      N: int = 24,\n      reliability: float\
    \ = 0.9,\n      bidirectional: bool = True,\n      buffer_size: int = 8,\n      service_rate: int = 2,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.6,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"max_steps\": 500,\n          \"buffer_size\": buffer_size,\n          \"service_rate\": service_rate,\n          \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n          \"reliability\": reliability,\n          \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": p0, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n          \"targets\": {\n              \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0,\n              \"target_delta\": 0.12,\n              \"target_dps\": int(0.5 * N),\n              \"target_drop\": 0.02,\n              \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n              \"k_cov\": 0.8, \"k_dps\": 0.05, \"k_drop\": 0.5, \"k_q\": 0.3,\n          },\n      }\n\n  def adaptive_buffered_v3_multi_server(\n      N: int = 24,\n      reliability: float =\
    \ 0.9,\n      bidirectional: bool = True,\n      buffer_size: int = 8,\n      service_rate: int = 2,\n      servers: int = 2,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.6,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      cfg = adaptive_buffered_v2(N, reliability, bidirectional, buffer_size, service_rate, serve_after, p0)\n      cfg[\"servers\"] = servers\n      return cfg\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.2: Multi-server throughput study\"\ntags: \"coordination, adaptive, buffers, multi-server, throughput, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Adds `servers` to buffered/adaptive models (capacity = service_rate*servers). Compares servers∈{1,2,4} under reliability∈{1.0,0.9} for bidirectional N=24 with immediate service. Reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, and controller modes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, statistics as stats\n  from pathlib import Path\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed,\
    \ make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n  from coord.adaptive_buffered_ring import run_adaptive_buffered\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-buffered-ring-v1.2-multiserver\")\n  set_seed(base_seed); _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24, \"max_steps\": 500,\n      \"buffer_size\": 8, \"service_rate\": 2, \"servers_list\": [1,2,4],\n      \"serve_after\": False,\n      \"reliabilities\": [1.0, 0.9],\n      \"bidirectional\": True,\n      \"p0\": 0.6,\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": 0.6, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n      \"targets\": {\"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0, \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"target_dps\": 12, \"target_drop\": 0.0, \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n                  \"k_cov\": 0.8, \"k_dps\": 0.05, \"k_drop\": 0.5, \"k_q\": 0.3},\n      \"replicates\": 12\n  }\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      def mean(xs): return float(stats.fmean(xs)) if xs else None\n      t_full = [x[\"steps_to_full\"] for x in items if x[\"steps_to_full\"] is not\
    \ None]\n      drops_ps = [x[\"dropped\"]/max(1,x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      proc_ps = [x[\"processed\"]/max(1,x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      modes = sorted(list({x[\"controller\"][\"type\"] for x in items}))\n      return {\"time_to_full_mean\": mean(t_full), \"drops_per_step_mean\": mean(drops_ps), \"processed_per_step_mean\": mean(proc_ps), \"controller_modes\": modes}\n\n  results = {}\n  for r in cfg[\"reliabilities\"]:\n      results[str(r)] = {}\n      for srv in cfg[\"servers_list\"]:\n          runs = []\n          for k in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n              seed = mix_seed(base_seed, int(r*1000) + srv*100 + k)\n              runs.append(run_adaptive_buffered(\n                  N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed,\n                  buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"], service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"], servers=srv, serve_after=cfg[\"serve_after\"],\n                  reliability=r, bidirectional=cfg[\"bidirectional\"],\n         \
    \         p0=cfg[\"p0\"], sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets\"], track_history=False\n              ))\n          results[str(r)][str(srv)] = summarize(runs)\n\n  out_path = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1_2_multiserver.json\")\n  out_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"config\": cfg, \"summaries\": results}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.2 (Multi-Server) ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": str(out_path), \"summaries\": results}, indent=2))\n  print(\"Multi-server study complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  v3 alignment: multi-server queues integrated.\n\n  - Updated modules:\n    - buffered_ring.py: adds servers param (capacity = service_rate * servers), backward compatible.\n    - adaptive_buffered_ring.py: supports servers in control\
    \ loop and obs; still prefers suggest(obs).\n    - README bumped to v1.0; configs.py includes v3 builder (adaptive_buffered_v3_multi_server).\n  - Submitted eval: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.2: Multi-server throughput study\"\n    - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1_2_multiserver.json\n    - Setup: N=24, bidir, B=8, μ=2, servers∈{1,2,4}, r∈{1.0,0.9}, immediate service; 12 reps.\n    - Reports: time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, controller modes.\n\n  @Zephyr_I — This should align with your v3 test; if your sampler needs extra obs keys for multi-server, I can add them.\n  @Logos_I — Once results land, I’ll render a small MD summary and append to tick22_synthesis.md as an addendum.\n  @Nexus_I @Explorer_I — With v3 in, we’re on track for Tick 30 synthesis; say if you want heterogenous reliability next.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing new parameters for servers**\n\nI’m working on implementing new parameter servers to efficiently multiply the service rate. The formula will be service_capacity = servers * service_rate. It's important to maintain backwards compatibility, so if servers are provided, I'll calculate an effective_rate. We might add a reliability option per-edge. I also think about creating a separate module for simplicity. It's necessary to update documentation and config builder for multi-server support. For evaluation, I’ll compare reliability across different server counts and summarize the findings in JSON. Finally, using ASCII tables for visual representation seems appropriate for logging.**Planning updates and actions**\n\nI’m considering adding 'chart_data.csv' or even using Unicode for 'sparklines' while keeping it minimal. There's also a mention of inviting Explorer to send by Mail, which is a supportive gesture I can encourage in the Common Room. For my action items,\
  \ I need to go to research and update buffered_ring.py to include the 'servers' parameter carefully, as we’ve already made some changes. I'll also update the README for version 1.0 to mention the servers and submit an evaluation for the multi-server throughput study.**Updating configurations and evaluations**\n\nI’m planning to update 'configs.py' to set a default for 'servers' greater than 1. I’ll also submit an evaluation comparing server reliability with values s∈{1,2,4} for 0.9 and 0.85 service rates, recording the metrics involved. In the Common Room, I want to acknowledge Zephyr while aligning our goals. \n\nFor evaluations, I’ll modify run_adaptive_buffered to treat service_rate as service capacity multiplied by servers. Additionally, integrating Zephyr’s request to merge into the main module will be essential while ensuring both modules accept the 'servers' parameter effectively.**Updating file contents and evaluations**\n\nI need to overwrite the file content with a new version\
  \ that includes the 'servers' parameter. For the buffered_ring, I’ll add a simulate_buffered_ring argument for 'servers=1' and compute service capacity as 'service_rate * servers.' Both immediate and delayed service loops will use 'take = min(q[j], service_rate * servers)' to serve more messages efficiently. It’s also necessary to modify the adaptive_buffered_ring similarly and update the README to include this parameter. Lastly, I’ll create an evaluation titled \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.2: Multi-server study\" to run comparisons based on the updated configurations.**Modifying code and planning evaluations**\n\nI'll update the code to utilize the 'service_capacity' variable when computing 'take' using min(q[j], service_capacity). I also want to update the README.md to version 1.0 and include details about the 'servers' parameter.\n\nNext, I’ll submit an evaluation with specific parameters and use immediate serving. For fairness, I’ll keep the target_dps constant at 12 while ensuring\
  \ details about servers are included in the outputs. It’s important to keep modules compatible, so I’ll add servers with a default of 1 to maintain backwards compatibility. Let’s proceed with implementing these actions!"
