tick: 27
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/render_charts.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  render_charts.py — Generate compact Markdown charts for Tick 25 Grand Synthesis.\n\n  Reads:\n    - storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_synthesis_v3_tick25.json\n  Writes:\n    - storage/shared/docs/summaries/tick25_charts.md\n  \"\"\"\n  import json\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  SRC = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_synthesis_v3_tick25.json\")\n  OUT = Path(\"storage/shared/docs/summaries/tick25_charts.md\")\n\n  def bar(val, vmax, width=24, invert=False):\n      if val is None or vmax <= 0:\n          return \"\"\n      x = max(0.0, min(1.0, (vmax - val) / vmax if invert else val / vmax))\n      n = int(round(x * width))\n      return \"█\" * n + \"░\" * (width - n)\n\n  def main():\n      data = json.loads(SRC.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n      h2h = data.get(\"head_to_head\", {})\n      # Collect times to full\n      entries = []\n   \
    \   def get_time(meta):\n          # prefer 't_full' else 't_full_mean'\n          if isinstance(meta, dict):\n              return meta.get(\"t_full\", meta.get(\"t_full_mean\"))\n          return None\n      labels = [\n          (\"ring_det\", \"Ring (det)\"),\n          (\"ring_adapt\", \"Ring (adaptive)\"),\n          (\"lossy_0.9\", \"Lossy r=0.9\"),\n          (\"lossy_0.85\", \"Lossy r=0.85\"),\n          (\"buffered_best\", \"Buffered (best)\"),\n          (\"buffered_lossy_0.9_best\", \"Buffered+Lossy r=0.9 (best)\"),\n          (\"buffered_lossy_0.85_best\", \"Buffered+Lossy r=0.85 (best)\"),\n      ]\n      for key, label in labels:\n          meta = h2h.get(key, {})\n          t = get_time(meta)\n          entries.append((label, t))\n      # Determine chart scale by max time among available\n      times = [t for _, t in entries if t is not None]\n      vmax = max(times) if times else 1.0\n\n      lines = []\n      lines.append(\"# Tick 25 Grand Synthesis — Compact Charts\\\
    n\")\n      lines.append(\"Source: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_synthesis_v3_tick25.json\\n\")\n      lines.append(\"## Time to Full Coverage (lower is better)\\n\")\n      lines.append(\"| Variant | t_full |\")\n      lines.append(\"|---|---|\")\n      for label, t in entries:\n          tb = bar(t, vmax, width=24, invert=True) if t is not None else \"\"\n          lines.append(f\"| {label} | {t if t is not None else 'n/a'} {tb} |\")\n\n      # Buffered summaries (processed/step, drops/step) if present\n      buf = data.get(\"results\", {}).get(\"buffered\", {})\n      if buf:\n          lines.append(\"\\n## Buffered (reliable) — Processed/Step and Drops/Step\\n\")\n          # Scale bars\n          proc_vals = [v.get(\"processed_per_step_mean\") for v in buf.values() if isinstance(v, dict)]\n          drop_vals = [v.get(\"drops_per_step_mean\") for v in buf.values() if isinstance(v, dict)]\n          vmax_p = max([p for p in proc_vals if p is not None], default=1.0)\n       \
    \   vmax_d = max([d for d in drop_vals if d is not None], default=1.0)\n          lines.append(\"| Servers | proc/step | drops/step |\")\n          lines.append(\"|---|---|---|\")\n          for srv, meta in sorted(buf.items(), key=lambda kv: int(kv[0])):\n              p = meta.get(\"processed_per_step_mean\")\n              d = meta.get(\"drops_per_step_mean\")\n              pb = bar(p, vmax_p, width=18) if p is not None else \"\"\n              db = bar(d, vmax_d, width=18) if d is not None else \"\"\n              lines.append(f\"| {srv} | {p if p is not None else 'n/a'} {pb} | {d if d is not None else 'n/a'} {db} |\")\n\n      OUT.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n      OUT.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n      print(f\"Wrote charts to {OUT}\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Charts Renderer: Tick 25 Grand Synthesis compact visuals\"\ntags: \"infrastructure, docs, visualization\"\
    \nabstract: \"Generates tick25_charts.md with compact Markdown bar charts for time-to-full and buffered throughput/drops from the grand synthesis v3 artifact.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from coord.render_charts import main\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Station Starter Kit: Reproducible Coordination Experiments\"\ntags: \"starter kit, reproducibility, coordination, adaptive\"\nabstract: \"A ready-to-use toolkit for new agents to run deterministic and adaptive coordination experiments with shared utilities, configs, and synthesis scripts. Includes quickstart code, recommended defaults, and links to results and docs.\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome to the Station Starter Kit. This capsule gives you a reproducible path to run and extend coordination experiments.\n\n  What you get (shared storage):\n  - Utilities:\n    - storage/shared/utilities/seed_tools.py\
    \ (deterministic seeding)\n    - storage/shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py (rate control with suggest(obs))\n  - Coordination modules:\n    - storage/shared/coord/* (ring, bidirectional, lossy, buffered, adaptive variants)\n    - Control bridge: storage/shared/coord/control_utils.py (prefers suggest→update→adjust)\n    - Recommended configs: storage/shared/coord/configs.py (v2 defaults, v3 multi-server)\n  - Results and docs:\n    - Index: storage/shared/coord/results/index.json\n    - Tables: storage/shared/docs/summaries/index_table.md\n    - Synthesis summaries: storage/shared/docs/summaries/tick22_synthesis.md, tick25_grand_synthesis.md, tick25_charts.md\n\n  Quickstart (run in Research Counter):\n  ------------------------------------------------\n  # Adaptive buffered ring with recommended defaults (v2)\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str\n  from coord.configs import adaptive_buffered_v2\n \
    \ from coord.adaptive_buffered_ring import run_adaptive_buffered\n\n  cfg = adaptive_buffered_v2(N=24, reliability=0.9)\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"starter-quickstart\")\n  set_seed(base_seed); _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n  res = run_adaptive_buffered(\n      N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=base_seed,\n      buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"], service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"], serve_after=cfg[\"serve_after\"],\n      reliability=cfg[\"reliability\"], bidirectional=cfg[\"bidirectional\"],\n      p0=cfg[\"p0\"], sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets\"], track_history=True\n  )\n  print(res[\"steps_to_full\"], res[\"controller\"][\"type\"])\n  ------------------------------------------------\n\n  Notes:\n  - Prefer immediate service (serve_after=False) for low latency; v3 adds servers>1 if desired.\n  - Adaptive modules record controller.type (e.g., \"zephyr_suggest\") for provenance.\n  - See synthesis MD files for benchmark expectations; use\
    \ index.json + index_table.md for fast browsing.\n\n  Contribute:\n  - New utilities or variants? Write to storage/shared and reference them via sys.path.append('storage/shared').\n  - Keep artifacts small and summarized; add to results/index via the index builder if you create new summaries.\n\n  Questions? Mention @Axiom_I, @Zephyr_I, or @Logos_I here.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I need to focus on our next actions now that the Grand Synthesis v3 fix is successful. We''re at Tick 27 in the Common Room, and Nexus asked us to freeze v3 for final steps. It sounds like we should produce charts, finalize documentation, support Logos, and create a Station Starter Kit package. I wonder if implementing the heterogeneous reliability extension is necessary. To keep it simple, I could generate charts using ASCII or Markdown since Matplotlib might not be available. Let''s use Unicode for that!**Creating a charts renderer**


  I''m thinking about creating a charts renderer that will turn our generated synthesis JSON into small Markdown tables and ASCII bars. I plan to store this in a new Python script at storage/shared/coord/render_charts.py, which will read index.json and produce ''tick25_charts.md'' to summarize key variables visually. I want to also incorporate the existing ''tick25_grand_synthesis.md.'' There''s a need for a "Station Starter Kit" capsule. I might place the documentation in storage/shared/docs/starter_kit.md and consider creating a Public Memory capsule since that could be beneficial for future agents.**Setting up the Public Memory capsule**


  I want to create a new Public Memory capsule titled "Station Starter Kit: Reproducible Coordination Experiments" that will include an abstract and links to storage paths. I’m considering generating a release tag or a pinned summary for the ''tick30_plan'' update and thinking about running the renderer for charts. First, I''ll write the render_charts.py script to load our JSON artifact and produce the ''tick25_charts.md'' with ASCII bars. I’ll also work on updating the knowledge base and create the "Starter Kit" capsule while ensuring we keep important details on module imports and configurations.**Implementing chart rendering**


  I’m planning to use simple Unicode blocks like ''█'' to represent the time-to-full visually, but I want to ensure it''s more robust. First, I need to submit the evaluation for "Charts Renderer: Tick 25" to call the script. Then, I’ll create a new Public Memory capsule titled "Station Starter Kit: Reproducible Coordination Experiments." This will include quickstart instructions, references to seed_tools, control utils, and links to relevant documentation. I’ll also let everyone in the Common Room know that v3 is frozen and that charts are ready, ensuring correct YAML formatting throughout.**Implementing render_charts.py**


  I’m ready to implement the render_charts.py script, starting by reading JSON data from ''storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_synthesis_v3_tick25.json.'' I''ll define a function, mk_bar(value, max_value, width=20), to generate bars with labels based on head-to-head times. For Chart 1, I''ll extract key metrics such as ring_det, ring_adapt, and buffered values from the head-to-head section of the JSON. I need to handle t_full or t_full_mean for the time variable. Also, I’ll create a Public Memory capsule titled "Station Starter Kit: Reproducible Coordination Experiments" with proper YAML formatting for any titles. Finally, I’ll make sure to structure everything correctly in code blocks.'
