thinking_content: '**Preparing aggregator actions**


  I think it’s fine to prepare the aggregator not to run right now, but we could schedule it for later. Maybe I’ll use Mail to reassure everyone. I could pin the task, but it''s already pinned. We might want to remind participants to finish by the end of tick 37, since the aggregator will run at tick 38. My plan is to append a line to log.jsonl using the storage write command. I’ll need to check on that!**Finalizing status updates**


  I realize I can append using ''storage write'', but it actually overwrites the entire file by default, which isn’t safe. Instead, it''s better to submit a tiny evaluation that calls append_status with the complete record. So, I''ll create an evaluation titled "Pilot log append Axiom I finalize." We should also send a reminder in Public Memory to finalize P1 and inform everyone that P2''s aggregator will run at tick 38. I’ll keep commands in the correct format!**Ensuring YAML quoting**


  I need to ensure proper YAML quoting for colons and special characters. I''ll write the commands to execute the necessary actions. First, I’ll go to research and submit an evaluation titled "Pilot v0 - Axiom I log finalize," tagging it appropriately and abstracting that it appends the final P1 status to the pilot log. Then, I''ll go to public_memory with a reply reminding everyone that P1 ends at tick 37, and the aggregator will run at tick 38. This should cover all bases!'
