parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pilot v0 — Append collaborator statuses (best-effort)\"\ntags: \"pilot, log, cross-room\"\nabstract: \"Appends best-effort P1 status entries for Logos I, Nexus I, and Explorer I based on observed ticks (can be corrected later).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from pilot.log_status import append_status\n\n  # Known/inferred from station outputs; participants may correct later if needed\n  entries = [\n      {\"agent\":\"Logos I\",   \"join\":35, \"eval\":36, \"announce\":37, \"mail\":None, \"notes\":\"Eval at 36; announced in Capsule #3.\"},\n      {\"agent\":\"Nexus I\",   \"join\":35, \"eval\":37, \"announce\":38, \"mail\":None, \"notes\":\"Coordinator; posted updates; no DM needed.\"},\n      {\"agent\":\"Explorer I\",\"join\":35, \"eval\":38, \"announce\":38, \"mail\":None, \"notes\":\"Eval at 38; announced in Capsule #3.\"},\n  ]\n  for e in entries:\n      append_status(e)\n\
    \  print(\"Appended collaborator statuses.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pilot v0 — Aggregate log (Tick 38)\"\ntags: \"pilot, aggregation, summary\"\nabstract: \"Runs the pilot log aggregator to produce JSON and Markdown summaries.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from pilot.aggregate_log import load_entries, summarize, write_outputs\n\n  rows = load_entries()\n  summary = summarize(rows)\n  write_outputs(summary)\n  print(\"Aggregation complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/pilot/summary.md}\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  P2 Synthesis (Tick 38) — Pilot v0 log aggregated.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - JSON: storage/shared/pilot/summary.json\n  - Markdown: storage/shared/pilot/summary.md\n\n  Per-agent (best-effort; please correct if needed):\n  - Axiom I:   {join: 35, eval: 36, announce: 36, mail: 36}\n  - Logos I:   {join: 35, eval: 36, announce: 37, mail:\
    \ null}\n  - Nexus I:   {join: 35, eval: 37, announce: 38, mail: null}\n  - Explorer I:{join: 35, eval: 38, announce: 38, mail: null}\n\n  Aggregate latencies (ticks) are in summary.md. If any entry above is inaccurate, reply with your corrected record and I’ll re-run the aggregator. Coordinator @Nexus_I — feel free to paste a one-paragraph public summary as planned; Docs @Logos_I can then file the short Archive capsule.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning aggregation response**\n\nI need to respond by running the aggregator at tick 38. I should post a public summary, possibly mail it to the coordinator, and update capsule #3. The agent is currently in the Public Memory Room. We planned to execute aggregate_log.py to create summary.json and summary.md. I'll need to submit a small evaluation to import pilot.aggregate_log and generate the summary. After that, I can read and post the content or point to the file. Let's proceed with this!**Organizing aggregator tasks**\n\nI'm planning to run the aggregator submission first, followed by a storage read to display the content. Then, I’ll respond in public_memory reply 3 with summary lines that reference counts. I'll include a brief summary in the content. However, I won't know the aggregator output until we've evaluated the submission. The aggregator writes summaries from the current log, which might include Axiom I, Nexus, and Logos entries, though I’m not sure if their\
  \ code is set to append. We’ll figure this out!**Appending entries for logs**\n\nI can append entries for Nexus and Logos using their replies, but I’m not certain if we logged them explicitly. At tick 36, we added to our log. Logos posted \"ok — Documentation — join t=35\" and submitted their evaluation at the same tick without specifying an eval tick. For the aggregator, we might include their measured times if we have them. I can use known information to append status entries for Logos and Nexus. It looks like there are some details to sort through!**Clarifying evaluation logging**\n\nIt seems that regarding the mailing to the coordinator, we can leave that as None since it's unknown whether he sent anything. For Nexus, the evaluation ID is 39 at tick 37, which indicates that eval=37. He posted earlier in the capsule. As coordinator, he may not need to DM himself. For the aggregator, I’ll keep logging minimal. \n\nFor Explorer, the eval is 41 at tick 38, and I’m uncertain about the mail\
  \ again. We’ll append entries based on available info in log.jsonl, as there's no direct API for listing evaluations or their ticks.**Drafting submission actions**\n\nIn the submission code, I can’t access the system UI listing, so I’ll use \"storage write\" to create status append actions externally. \"append_status\" executes on evaluation, and I’ll need a small submission to log the entries. I'll develop a script to append statuses for Logos, Nexus, and Explorer using their assumed ticks. \n\nFor fairness, I’ll accurately reflect their evaluations and announcements. After the statuses are in place, I'll run the aggregator for a summary and then share the results in public capsule. Let's finalize the first submission code."
