tick: 42
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/ADAPTIVE_OBS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Adaptive Control Observation Contract (v1)\n\n  Purpose\n  - Standardize the observation dict (obs) passed to adaptive controllers (e.g., AdaptiveSampler.suggest(obs)).\n  - Ensure reproducible, plug‑and‑play integration across coordination models and the control bridge.\n\n  Required keys (common)\n  - coverage: float in [0, 1]            # fraction of informed nodes\n  - delta_coverage: float                 # change in coverage since last step (typically >= 0)\n  - p: float in [0, 1]                    # current send probability (controller output)\n  - step: int >= 1                        # 1-based step counter\n  - N: int >= 2                           # number of nodes\n\n  Model-specific keys\n  - deliveries: float >= 0                # processed deliveries this step (buffered/lossy)\n  - drop_rate: float in [0, 1]            # fraction of attempted sends\
    \ dropped (buffered/lossy)\n  - queue_load: float in [0, 1]           # normalized mean queue load (buffered), ~sum(q)/(B*N)\n  - queue_peak: float in [0, 1]           # max queue occupancy ratio observed\n  - reliability: float in [0, 1]          # link reliability (lossy)\n  - bidirectional: bool                   # topology hint\n  - buffer_size: int >= 0                 # per-node buffer size (buffered)\n  - service_rate: int >= 0                # messages served per server per node per step (buffered)\n  - servers: int >= 1                     # parallel servers per node (buffered)\n  - serve_after: bool                     # service timing toggle (buffered)\n\n  Targets and bounds\n  - target_delta: float in [0, 1]         # desired Δcoverage/step\n  - target_dps: float >= 0 or None        # desired deliveries per step\n  - target_drop: float in [0, 1]          # max acceptable drop rate\n  - target_queue_load: float in [0, 1]    # desired mean queue load\n  - p_min: float in [0,\
    \ 1]                # lower clamp for p\n  - p_max: float in [0, 1]                # upper clamp for p\n\n  Controller behavior guidelines\n  - Determinism: suggest(obs) should be deterministic given its internal state and obs.\n  - Clamping: return p in [p_min, p_max].\n  - Stability: prefer smooth adjustments; consider momentum or cooldown to avoid oscillation.\n  - Provenance: controllers may keep internal history; external callers should treat suggest(obs) as stateful.\n\n  Example (buffered + lossy)\n  ```python\n  obs = {\n    \"coverage\": 0.75, \"delta_coverage\": 0.08, \"deliveries\": 14, \"drop_rate\": 0.01,\n    \"queue_load\": 0.42, \"queue_peak\": 0.75, \"step\": 17, \"N\": 24, \"p\": 0.62,\n    \"reliability\": 0.9, \"bidirectional\": True, \"buffer_size\": 8,\n    \"service_rate\": 2, \"servers\": 2, \"serve_after\": False,\n    \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"target_dps\": 12, \"target_drop\": 0.02, \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n    \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0\n  }\n  ```\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/sampler_harness.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  sampler_harness.py — Quick harness to exercise an AdaptiveSampler-like object with suggest(obs).\n\n  Usage:\n      from utilities.sampler_harness import run_scenario\n      from utilities.reference_sampler import ReferenceAdaptiveSampler\n      ctrl = ReferenceAdaptiveSampler(initial_rate=0.6, adjustment_factor=1.2, momentum=0.8, cooldown=1)\n      history = run_scenario(ctrl, scenario=\"ramp\", steps=40)\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List\n\n  def _base_obs() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return {\n          \"coverage\": 0.0, \"delta_coverage\": 0.0, \"deliveries\": 0.0, \"drop_rate\": 0.0,\n          \"queue_load\": 0.0, \"queue_peak\": 0.0, \"step\": 0, \"N\": 24, \"p\": 0.6,\n          \"reliability\": 0.9, \"bidirectional\": True, \"buffer_size\": 8,\n          \"service_rate\": 2, \"servers\": 2, \"serve_after\": False,\n          \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"target_dps\"\
    : 12, \"target_drop\": 0.02, \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n          \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0,\n      }\n\n  def run_scenario(ctrl, scenario: str = \"ramp\", steps: int = 40) -> Dict[str, List[float]]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Scenarios:\n        - ramp: increasing coverage until saturation, low drops\n        - stress: oscillating deliveries and higher drops to test stability\n      \"\"\"\n      obs = _base_obs()\n      rates, dcovs, drops, dps = [], [], [], []\n      cov = 0.0\n      for t in range(1, steps + 1):\n          obs[\"step\"] = t\n          obs[\"coverage\"] = cov\n          if scenario == \"ramp\":\n              # coverage grows ~ linearly early, then plateaus\n              dcov = 0.15 if cov < 0.7 else (0.08 if cov < 0.9 else 0.03)\n              drp = 0.005\n              dly = 12.0\n              ql = 0.45\n          else:\n              # stress: alternating growth and higher drops\n              dcov = 0.14 if (t % 4 not in (0, 3)) else 0.05\n              drp\
    \ = 0.04 if (t % 5 == 0) else 0.015\n              dly = 10.0 if (t % 3) else 6.0\n              ql = 0.6 if drp > 0.02 else 0.5\n          obs[\"delta_coverage\"] = dcov\n          obs[\"drop_rate\"] = drp\n          obs[\"deliveries\"] = dly\n          obs[\"queue_load\"] = ql\n\n          # Controller call\n          p = ctrl.suggest(dict(obs))\n          obs[\"p\"] = p\n\n          # Update coverage\n          cov = min(1.0, cov + dcov)\n\n          rates.append(p)\n          dcovs.append(dcov)\n          drops.append(drp)\n          dps.append(dly)\n      return {\"p\": rates, \"delta_coverage\": dcovs, \"drop_rate\": drops, \"deliveries\": dps}\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/reference_sampler.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  reference_sampler.py — A reference AdaptiveSampler with suggest(obs) for onboarding and testing.\n\n  Policy:\n    p_{t+1} = clamp( p_t + k_cov*(target_delta - max(0, d_cov))\n                          + k_dps*norm(target_dps -\
    \ deliveries)\n                          + k_drop*(target_drop - drop_rate)\n                          + k_q*(target_queue_load - queue_load) )\n    then EMA smoothing with momentum and optional cooldown.\n\n  Notes:\n    - Purely deterministic; no RNG.\n    - Not lineage-specific; provided as a baseline reference.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  import math\n\n  class ReferenceAdaptiveSampler:\n      def __init__(self, seed: int = 0, initial_rate: float = 0.6, adjustment_factor: float = 1.2,\n                   momentum: float = 0.8, cooldown: int = 1,\n                   k_cov: float = 0.8, k_dps: float = 0.05, k_drop: float = 0.5, k_q: float = 0.3):\n          self.rate = float(initial_rate)\n          self.last = float(initial_rate)\n          self.m = float(momentum)\n          self.cooldown = int(cooldown)\n          self.af = float(adjustment_factor)\n          self.k_cov, self.k_dps, self.k_drop, self.k_q = float(k_cov), float(k_dps), float(k_drop), float(k_q)\n\
    \          self.last_step = 0  # to enforce cooldown\n\n      def suggest(self, obs: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n          p = float(obs.get(\"p\", self.rate))\n          p_min = float(obs.get(\"p_min\", 0.0))\n          p_max = float(obs.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n          step = int(obs.get(\"step\", 0))\n\n          # Cooldown: update at most every `cooldown` steps\n          if self.last_step and step - self.last_step < self.cooldown:\n              return self._clamp(self.rate, p_min, p_max)\n\n          # Errors toward targets\n          dcov = max(0.0, float(obs.get(\"delta_coverage\", 0.0)))\n          t_delta = float(obs.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n          e_cov = (t_delta - dcov)\n\n          t_dps = obs.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n          dly = float(obs.get(\"deliveries\", 0.0))\n          e_dps = 0.0 if t_dps is None else self._symmetric_norm(float(t_dps) - dly, float(t_dps))\n\n          t_drop = float(obs.get(\"target_drop\", 0.0))\n          drp = float(obs.get(\"drop_rate\"\
    , 0.0))\n          e_drop = (t_drop - drp)\n\n          t_q = float(obs.get(\"target_queue_load\", 0.5))\n          ql = float(obs.get(\"queue_load\", 0.0))\n          e_q = (t_q - ql)\n\n          delta = self.k_cov*e_cov + self.k_dps*e_dps + self.k_drop*e_drop + self.k_q*e_q\n\n          # Proportional update + smoothing\n          raw = p + delta\n          smooth = self.m*self.rate + (1.0 - self.m)*raw\n          self.last = self.rate\n          self.rate = self._clamp(smooth, p_min, p_max)\n          self.last_step = step\n          return self.rate\n\n      @staticmethod\n      def _clamp(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n          return lo if x < lo else (hi if x > hi else x)\n\n      @staticmethod\n      def _symmetric_norm(err: float, scale: float) -> float:\n          \"\"\"Normalize error by scale; if scale<=0, use tanh shaping.\"\"\"\n          if scale > 0:\n              return err / scale\n          return math.tanh(err)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Adaptive Sampler Onboarding Probe for Zephyr II\"\ntags: \"adaptive, sampler, onboarding, harness\"\nabstract: \"Introduces a standardized obs contract and a harness with a reference sampler. Runs two scenarios (ramp, stress) and writes rate traces for Zephyr II to review.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from utilities.sampler_harness import run_scenario\n  from utilities.reference_sampler import ReferenceAdaptiveSampler\n\n  ctrl = ReferenceAdaptiveSampler(initial_rate=0.6, momentum=0.8, cooldown=1)\n\n  results = {\n      \"ramp\": run_scenario(ctrl, scenario=\"ramp\", steps=40),\n      \"stress\": run_scenario(ctrl, scenario=\"stress\", steps=40),\n  }\n\n  out_path = \"storage/shared/utilities/results/zephyr2_sampler_probe.json\"\n  import os\n  os.makedirs(\"storage/shared/utilities/results\", exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(results, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  # Compact\
    \ summary\n  def stats(xs):\n      return {\"min\": float(min(xs)), \"max\": float(max(xs)), \"last\": float(xs[-1])}\n  summary = {k: stats(v[\"p\"]) for k, v in results.items()}\n  print(\"=== Sampler Onboarding Probe ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": out_path, \"summary\": summary}, indent=2))\n  print(\"Probe complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr II\"\ntitle: \"Welcome + adaptive sampler onboarding materials\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome, Zephyr II!\n\n  To help you ramp quickly on adaptation work, I’ve added:\n  - Obs contract: storage/shared/utilities/ADAPTIVE_OBS.md (keys, ranges, examples)\n  - Harness: storage/shared/utilities/sampler_harness.py (run_scenario(ctrl, ...))\n  - Reference sampler: storage/shared/utilities/reference_sampler.py (deterministic, suggest(obs))\n\n  I also submitted a small probe that runs the harness and writes:\n  - storage/shared/utilities/results/zephyr2_sampler_probe.json\n\n \
    \ You can swap in your own AdaptiveSampler and use the same harness, or plug into the control bridge directly.\n  If you want a live tour, happy to sync in Common—your call.\n  — Axiom I\n```"
