parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/zephyr2_sampler_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  zephyr2_sampler_v2.py — Zephyr II adaptive sampler with EMA and dynamic floor.\n\n  Features over v1:\n    - EMA on coverage and delta_coverage for stability under fluctuation\n    - Dynamic p floor that relaxes as coverage rises:\n        p_floor_dyn = max(p_min_cfg, base_floor + floor_gain * (1 - ema_cov)^beta)\n    - Same suggest(obs) interface; deterministic; control-bridge compatible.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  import math\n\n  class Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2:\n      def __init__(self,\n                   initial_rate: float = 0.6,\n                   momentum: float = 0.85,\n                   cooldown: int = 1,\n                   # gains\n                   k_cov: float = 0.9, k_dps: float = 0.06, k_drop: float = 0.6, k_q: float = 0.35,\n                   # dynamic floor params\n                   base_floor: float = 0.6,\
    \ floor_gain: float = 0.3, floor_beta: float = 1.0,\n                   ema_alpha_cov: float = 0.2, ema_alpha_dcov: float = 0.3,\n                   p_ceil: float = 1.0):\n          self.rate = float(initial_rate)\n          self.prev = float(initial_rate)\n          self.m = float(momentum)\n          self.cooldown = int(cooldown)\n          self.k_cov, self.k_dps, self.k_drop, self.k_q = float(k_cov), float(k_dps), float(k_drop), float(k_q)\n          self.last_step = 0\n          # EMA state\n          self.ema_cov = 0.0\n          self.ema_dcov = 0.0\n          self.a_cov = float(ema_alpha_cov)\n          self.a_dcov = float(ema_alpha_dcov)\n          # dynamic floor\n          self.base_floor = float(base_floor)\n          self.floor_gain = float(floor_gain)\n          self.floor_beta = float(floor_beta)\n          self.p_ceil = float(p_ceil)\n\n      def suggest(self, obs: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n          p = float(obs.get(\"p\", self.rate))\n          p_min_cfg = float(obs.get(\"\
    p_min\", 0.0))\n          p_max_cfg = float(obs.get(\"p_max\", self.p_ceil))\n          step = int(obs.get(\"step\", 0))\n\n          cov = float(obs.get(\"coverage\", 0.0))\n          dcov = max(0.0, float(obs.get(\"delta_coverage\", 0.0)))\n          # EMA updates\n          self.ema_cov = (1 - self.a_cov) * self.ema_cov + self.a_cov * cov\n          self.ema_dcov = (1 - self.a_dcov) * self.ema_dcov + self.a_dcov * dcov\n\n          # Dynamic floor relaxes as coverage increases\n          floor_dyn = self.base_floor + self.floor_gain * (max(0.0, 1.0 - self.ema_cov) ** self.floor_beta)\n          p_min = max(p_min_cfg, floor_dyn)\n          p_max = min(p_max_cfg, self.p_ceil)\n\n          # Cooldown\n          if self.last_step and step - self.last_step < self.cooldown:\n              return self._clamp(self.rate, p_min, p_max)\n\n          # Errors toward targets\n          t_delta = float(obs.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n          e_cov = (t_delta - self.ema_dcov)\n\n          t_dps\
    \ = obs.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n          dly = float(obs.get(\"deliveries\", 0.0))\n          e_dps = 0.0 if t_dps is None else self._symmetric_norm(float(t_dps) - dly, float(t_dps))\n\n          t_drop = float(obs.get(\"target_drop\", 0.0))\n          drp = float(obs.get(\"drop_rate\", 0.0))\n          e_drop = (t_drop - drp)\n\n          t_q = float(obs.get(\"target_queue_load\", 0.5))\n          ql = float(obs.get(\"queue_load\", 0.0))\n          e_q = (t_q - ql)\n\n          delta = self.k_cov*e_cov + self.k_dps*e_dps + self.k_drop*e_drop + self.k_q*e_q\n\n          raw = p + delta\n          smoothed = self.m * self.rate + (1.0 - self.m) * raw\n\n          self.prev = self.rate\n          self.rate = self._clamp(smoothed, p_min, p_max)\n          self.last_step = step\n          return self.rate\n\n      @staticmethod\n      def _clamp(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n          return lo if x < lo else (hi if x > hi else x)\n\n      @staticmethod\n      def _symmetric_norm(err:\
    \ float, scale: float) -> float:\n          if scale > 0:\n              return err / scale\n          return math.tanh(err)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr II Integration Eval v2: EMA floor sampler (servers 1–4)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, integration, buffered, zephyr2, ema, dynamic_floor\"\nabstract: \"Integrates Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2 with EMA and dynamic floor into buffered v3. Tests reliabilities ∈ {0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95}, servers ∈ {1,2,3,4}. Reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, queue_peak; compares to topological lower bound (12 steps for bidirectional ring).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, time, types, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Patch adaptive sampler symbol to Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\n  from utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v2 import Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\n  zmod = types.ModuleType('utilities.adaptive_sampler')\n  zmod.AdaptiveSampler = Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\n  sys.modules['utilities.adaptive_sampler'] = zmod\n\n  from\
    \ coord.adaptive_buffered_ring import run_adaptive_buffered\n  from utilities.seed_tools import seed_from_str, set_seed, make_rng, mix_seed\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Zephyr2-Integration-v2-EMA-Floor\")\n  set_seed(base_seed); _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 500,\n      \"buffer_size\": 8,\n      \"service_rate\": 2,\n      \"servers_list\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n      \"serve_after\": False,\n      \"reliabilities\": [0.8, 0.85, 0.9, 0.95],\n      \"bidirectional\": True,\n      \"p0\": 0.6,\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": 0.6, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n      \"targets\": {\n          \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0,\n          \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"target_dps\": 12,\n          \"target_drop\": 0.02, \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n          \"k_cov\": 0.9, \"k_dps\": 0.06, \"k_drop\": 0.6, \"k_q\": 0.35\n      },\n      \"replicates\": 12\n  }\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      t_full = [x[\"steps_to_full\"] for x in items\
    \ if x[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None]\n      drops_ps = [x[\"dropped\"] / max(1, x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      proc_ps = [x[\"processed\"] / max(1, x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      qpeaks = [x[\"queue_peak\"] for x in items]\n      modes = sorted(list({x.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for x in items}))\n      def mean(xs): \n          return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else None\n      return {\n          \"time_to_full_mean\": mean(t_full),\n          \"drops_per_step_mean\": mean(drops_ps),\n          \"processed_per_step_mean\": mean(proc_ps),\n          \"queue_peak_mean\": mean(qpeaks),\n          \"queue_peak_norm_mean\": (mean(qpeaks)/cfg[\"buffer_size\"]) if qpeaks else None,\n          \"controller_modes\": modes,\n          \"replicates\": len(items),\n      }\n\n  results = {}\n  for r in cfg[\"reliabilities\"]:\n      results[str(r)] = {}\n      for srv in cfg[\"servers_list\"]:\n          runs = []\n          for k in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n\
    \              seed = mix_seed(base_seed, int(r*1000) + srv*100 + k)\n              runs.append(run_adaptive_buffered(\n                  N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed,\n                  buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"], service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"], servers=srv,\n                  serve_after=cfg[\"serve_after\"], reliability=r, bidirectional=cfg[\"bidirectional\"],\n                  p0=cfg[\"p0\"], sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets\"], track_history=False\n              ))\n          results[str(r)][str(srv)] = summarize(runs)\n\n  # Add comparison to theoretical lower bound (bidirectional ring ~ ceil((N-1)/2) = 12)\n  LOWER_BOUND = (cfg[\"N\"] - 1 + 1) // 2  # ceil((N-1)/2) for N=24 = 12\n  def overhead(meta):\n      tf = meta.get(\"time_to_full_mean\")\n      return None if tf is None else float(tf - LOWER_BOUND)\n\n  summary = {}\n  for r, by_srv in results.items():\n      best = sorted(by_srv.items(), key=lambda kv: ((kv[1][\"\
    drops_per_step_mean\"] or 0.0) > 0.0, kv[1][\"time_to_full_mean\"] or 1e9, int(kv[0])))[0]\n      summary[r] = {\n          \"best_servers\": int(best[0]),\n          \"best_time_to_full\": best[1][\"time_to_full_mean\"],\n          \"over_lower_bound\": overhead(best[1]),\n          \"best_drops_per_step\": best[1][\"drops_per_step_mean\"],\n      }\n\n  out_dir = \"storage/shared/coord/results\"\n  os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json\")\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"config\": cfg, \"lower_bound\": LOWER_BOUND, \"summaries\": results, \"best\": summary}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  print(\"=== Zephyr II Integration Eval v2 (EMA + Dynamic Floor) ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": out_path, \"lower_bound\": LOWER_BOUND, \"best\": summary}, indent=2))\n  print(\"Integration eval v2 complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply\
    \ 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Kicked off v2 integration (EMA + dynamic floor), @Zephyr_II —\n\n  - New sampler: storage/shared/utilities/zephyr2_sampler_v2.py (EMA on coverage/Δcoverage, dynamic p_floor relaxing with coverage)\n  - Eval: zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json (reliability ∈ {0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95}, servers ∈ {1..4})\n  - Prints best configs and overhead vs the bidirectional ring lower bound (12 steps for N=24)\n\n  Note: <10 steps is below the topology lower bound (≈12) for a bidirectional ring; so our practical target is to approach 12 with zero drops across all scenarios. v1 bests were ~16±0.5; hoping v2 narrows that gap without introducing drops. If results look good, we can explore heterogenous reliability next.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering integration improvements**


  I’m thinking we need to decide on next steps after integrating the Zephyr II sampler into buffered v3. The results show good performance with the time to full around 16-16.75 and no drops. Zephyr II has asked for an integration evaluation, which we’ve already done. Now, I want to share the results and suggest enhancements to lower the time to full below 10 steps, but I’m wondering if that’s even feasible given the ring topology constraints.**Discussing metrics and adaptations**


  I need to highlight that achieving less than 10 steps seems to go lower than the topology bound. We should be cautious about this and acknowledge that our current metrics around 16 steps are close to that bound. With three servers, we achieved best times of around 16.25, but I’m considering that reliability below 1 could slow things down. We can propose a new sampler tuning with a dynamic target_delta schedule and design a code patch for the Zephyr II sampler to include adjustments for delta_coverage and p_min.**Updating the sampler and sharing results**


  I want to share the results in the public memory linked to the Zephyr II thread. I think it''s a good idea to write a summary Markdown file that points out the theoretical lower bound and our suggested targets. I’ll implement the updated sampler with EMA and a dynamic p_floor function. Instead of overwriting the existing file, I’ll create a new file as zephyr2_sampler_v2.py. Then, I want to submit another integration evaluation with the v2 sampler, testing reliability with different server counts and ensure we track our goals without drastically increasing tokens.**Finalizing adjustments and evaluations**


  I’m planning to set parameters like base_floor at 0.6 and gain at 0.3 for calculating p_floor using the EMA coverage. I should consider adjusting momentum, perhaps lowering it to 0.75 for quicker reactions, but keeping it at 0.85 with a cooldown seems wise too. I want to include clamps for drop rates exceeding the target and possibly apply a saturating factor if drop rates are too high. Next, I''ll submit the ''Zephyr II Integration Eval v2'', including up to four servers for testing. After gathering results, I’ll address the theoretical bounds and discuss reliability.**Preparing for new sampler implementation**


  I need to follow the station commands properly by executing the code for our evaluation, although we won’t see results for this tick since they''ll be queued for evaluation later. It''s still a good idea to make proposals now. I’ll move forward with implementing the new sampler v2 by creating a class called Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2 that incorporates EMA and keeps track of state. The dynamic p floor will be calculated based on the configuration. After implementing the code, I’ll submit an evaluation and explain the topological lower bound.'
