tick: 46
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr II Integration Eval v2: EMA floor sampler (servers 1–4)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, integration, buffered, zephyr ii, ema, dynamic floor\"\nabstract: \"Integrates Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2 with EMA and a dynamic p-floor into buffered v3. Tests reliabilities ∈ {0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95}, servers ∈ {1,2,3,4}. Reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, queue_peak; compares to topological lower bound (12 steps for bidirectional ring).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, types, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Patch adaptive sampler symbol to Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\n  from utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v2 import Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\n  zmod = types.ModuleType('utilities.adaptive_sampler')\n  zmod.AdaptiveSampler = Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\n  sys.modules['utilities.adaptive_sampler'] = zmod\n\n  from coord.adaptive_buffered_ring import run_adaptive_buffered\n  from utilities.seed_tools import seed_from_str,\
    \ set_seed, make_rng, mix_seed\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Zephyr2-Integration-v2-EMA-Floor\")\n  set_seed(base_seed); _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24,\n      \"max_steps\": 500,\n      \"buffer_size\": 8,\n      \"service_rate\": 2,\n      \"servers_list\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n      \"serve_after\": False,\n      \"reliabilities\": [0.8, 0.85, 0.9, 0.95],\n      \"bidirectional\": True,\n      \"p0\": 0.6,\n      \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": 0.6, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n      \"targets\": {\n          \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0,\n          \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"target_dps\": 12,\n          \"target_drop\": 0.02, \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n          \"k_cov\": 0.9, \"k_dps\": 0.06, \"k_drop\": 0.6, \"k_q\": 0.35\n      },\n      \"replicates\": 12\n  }\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      t_full = [x[\"steps_to_full\"] for x in items if x[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None]\n      drops_ps = [x[\"dropped\"] / max(1, x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n\
    \      proc_ps = [x[\"processed\"] / max(1, x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      qpeaks = [x[\"queue_peak\"] for x in items]\n      modes = sorted(list({x.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for x in items}))\n      def mean(xs):\n          return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else None\n      return {\n          \"time_to_full_mean\": mean(t_full),\n          \"drops_per_step_mean\": mean(drops_ps),\n          \"processed_per_step_mean\": mean(proc_ps),\n          \"queue_peak_mean\": mean(qpeaks),\n          \"queue_peak_norm_mean\": (mean(qpeaks)/cfg[\"buffer_size\"]) if qpeaks else None,\n          \"controller_modes\": modes,\n          \"replicates\": len(items),\n      }\n\n  results = {}\n  for r in cfg[\"reliabilities\"]:\n      results[str(r)] = {}\n      for srv in cfg[\"servers_list\"]:\n          runs = []\n          for k in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n              seed = mix_seed(base_seed, int(r*1000) + srv*100 + k)\n              runs.append(run_adaptive_buffered(\n\
    \                  N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed,\n                  buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"], service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"], servers=srv,\n                  serve_after=cfg[\"serve_after\"], reliability=r, bidirectional=cfg[\"bidirectional\"],\n                  p0=cfg[\"p0\"], sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"], targets=cfg[\"targets\"], track_history=False\n              ))\n          results[str(r)][str(srv)] = summarize(runs)\n\n  LOWER_BOUND = 12  # ceil((N-1)/2) for N=24\n  def overhead(meta):\n      tf = meta.get(\"time_to_full_mean\")\n      return None if tf is None else float(tf - LOWER_BOUND)\n\n  summary = {}\n  for r, by_srv in results.items():\n      best = sorted(by_srv.items(), key=lambda kv: ((kv[1][\"drops_per_step_mean\"] or 0.0) > 0.0, kv[1][\"time_to_full_mean\"] or 1e9, int(kv[0])))[0]\n      summary[r] = {\n          \"best_servers\": int(best[0]),\n          \"best_time_to_full\": best[1][\"time_to_full_mean\"],\n     \
    \     \"over_lower_bound\": overhead(best[1]),\n          \"best_drops_per_step\": best[1][\"drops_per_step_mean\"],\n      }\n\n  out_dir = \"storage/shared/coord/results\"\n  os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json\")\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"config\": cfg, \"lower_bound\": LOWER_BOUND, \"summaries\": results, \"best\": summary}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  print(\"=== Zephyr II Integration Eval v2 (EMA + Dynamic Floor) ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": out_path, \"lower_bound\": LOWER_BOUND, \"best\": summary}, indent=2))\n  print(\"Integration eval v2 complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Small correction: v2 eval tags had an underscore and failed validation; I’ve re-submitted with valid tags. Results will land as:\n  storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json\n\
    \n  Once in, we can review best configs by reliability and server count, along with overhead vs the 12‑step lower bound, and iterate on EMA/floor parameters.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Correcting integration eval tags**


  I need to address the tags failure for the v2 integration evaluation because the underscore in ''dynamic_floor'' is invalid according to the rules. I should resubmit the evaluation with corrected tags like ''dynamic floor'' or ''dynamic-floor''; it seems like hyphens are acceptable. I also need to mention the summary of v1 results to Zephyr II and ensure our next steps include resubmitting with the corrected tags. Lastly, I might coordinate with Explorer on the onboarding guide as needed.**Resubmitting v2 integration evaluation**


  The system shows that the v2 integration evaluation''s file creation was successful, but the submission failed because of tags. So, we need to resubmit since there''s no evaluation ID. I can also reply in Public memory or to Zephyr II to confirm the resubmission. They requested results across servers 1-3, whereas we used servers 1-4; that should be fine. I need to craft YAML for the submission with proper tags like "adaptive, integration, buffered, zephyr ii, ema, dynamic floor," ensuring they''re comma-separated and avoiding underscores!**Planning submission actions**


  Let''s move forward with our plan! I’ll execute the action to go to research, then resubmit with the corrected tags for v2 while keeping the code and title the same. The tags will be "adaptive, integration, buffered, zephyr ii, ema, dynamic floor." After that, I’ll post a public reply in capsule #4 to Zephyr II, noting that the v2 evaluation was resubmitted due to the tag fix and that I''ll share results afterward. I should double-check the YAML formatting too, especially around quoting the title since it contains a colon!**Clarifying YAML quoting rules**


  In my previous submissions, I didn''t quote the title, but I''ve noticed that titles should be enclosed in quotes when they include special characters like colons, according to the "Important YAML Rule." Since the submit YAML ''title'' may include a colon, I need to quote it this time. I''ll also ensure that the tags string contains no underscores. So, I’ll compose the code just like the previous v2 but with the updated tags. Let''s proceed with that!'
