tick: 48
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/hetero_buffered_ring.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  hetero_buffered_ring.py — Buffered ring with heterogeneous per-edge reliability and adaptive control.\n\n  Function:\n    run_adaptive_hetero_buffered(\n        N, max_steps, base_seed,\n        buffer_size, service_rate, servers=1, serve_after=False,\n        reliability_mean=0.9, reliability_var=0.1,  # per-edge reliability ~ U(mean±var) clamped to [0,1]\n        bidirectional=True,\n        p0=0.6, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True\n    ) -> dict\n\n  Notes:\n    - Uses utilities.adaptive_sampler.AdaptiveSampler (patched by caller) with suggest(obs) interface.\n    - obs includes reliability_mean and reliability_var (additional hints for heterogeneous scenarios).\n    - Queues: per-node integer depths with capacity buffer_size; capacity per step = service_rate * servers.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List,\
    \ Tuple\n  import random, sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  try:\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # patched by caller\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallback to a simple deterministic sampler: keep p constant\n      class AdaptiveSampler:\n          def __init__(self, seed=0, initial_rate=0.6, adjustment_factor=1.2): self.rate = float(initial_rate)\n          def suggest(self, obs: Dict[str, Any]) -> float: return float(obs.get(\"p\", self.rate))\n\n  def _clamp01(x: float) -> float:\n      return 0.0 if x < 0.0 else (1.0 if x > 1.0 else x)\n\n  def run_adaptive_hetero_buffered(\n      N: int,\n      max_steps: int,\n      base_seed: int,\n      buffer_size: int,\n      service_rate: int,\n      servers: int = 1,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      reliability_mean: float = 0.9,\n      reliability_var: float = 0.1,\n      bidirectional: bool = True,\n      p0: float = 0.6,\n      sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      targets:\
    \ Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n      track_history: bool = True,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      assert 2 <= N <= 100_000\n      assert 0 <= buffer_size\n      assert 0 <= service_rate and servers >= 1\n      assert 0.0 <= reliability_mean <= 1.0 and 0.0 <= reliability_var <= 1.0\n      assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n\n      sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n      targets = targets or {}\n      p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.6))\n      p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n      target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))\n      target_dps = targets.get(\"target_dps\", 12)\n      target_drop = float(targets.get(\"target_drop\", 0.02))\n      target_queue_load = float(targets.get(\"target_queue_load\", 0.5))\n\n      rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n      # Per-edge reliability: arrays for right and left sends\n      rel_right = [_clamp01(reliability_mean + reliability_var * (rng.random()*2 - 1)) for _ in range(N)]\n      if bidirectional:\n\
    \          rel_left = [_clamp01(reliability_mean + reliability_var * (rng.random()*2 - 1)) for _ in range(N)]\n      else:\n          rel_left = [0.0 for _ in range(N)]\n\n      ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0)),\n                             adjustment_factor=float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.2)))\n\n      informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      q: List[int] = [0] * N\n\n      steps = 0\n      informed_count = 1\n      messages_attempted = 0\n      enqueued_total = 0\n      dropped_total = 0\n      processed_total = 0\n      queue_peak = 0\n      capacity = service_rate * servers\n\n      p = float(p0)\n\n      history = [informed_count] if track_history else None\n      p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      drop_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n      qload_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n\n      while steps < max_steps\
    \ and informed_count < N:\n          attempts_step = 0\n          enq_step = 0\n          drop_step = 0\n          proc_step = 0\n\n          arrivals = [0] * N\n\n          # Sends\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf: continue\n              # right neighbor\n              if p >= 1.0 or rng.random() < p:\n                  attempts_step += 1\n                  if rng.random() < rel_right[i]:\n                      j = (i + 1) % N\n                      if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n                          arrivals[j] += 1; enq_step += 1\n                      else:\n                          drop_step += 1\n              # left neighbor\n              if bidirectional:\n                  if p >= 1.0 or rng.random() < p:\n                      attempts_step += 1\n                      if rng.random() < rel_left[i]:\n                          j = (i - 1) % N\n                          if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n               \
    \               arrivals[j] += 1; enq_step += 1\n                          else:\n                              drop_step += 1\n\n          # Service\n          if serve_after:\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if capacity <= 0 or q[j] <= 0: continue\n                  take = min(q[j], capacity)\n                  q[j] -= take; proc_step += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]: informed[j] = True\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]; queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n          else:\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                      q[j] += arrivals[j]; queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n              for j in range(N):\n                  if capacity <= 0 or q[j] <= 0: continue\n                  take = min(q[j], capacity)\n                  q[j] -= take; proc_step += take\n                  if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\
    \ informed[j] = True\n\n          messages_attempted += attempts_step\n          enqueued_total += enq_step\n          dropped_total += drop_step\n          processed_total += proc_step\n\n          prev = informed_count\n          informed_count = sum(1 for x in informed if x)\n          d_cov = (informed_count - prev) / float(N)\n\n          drop_rate = (drop_step / attempts_step) if attempts_step > 0 else 0.0\n          qload = (sum(q) / float(max(1, buffer_size) * N)) if buffer_size > 0 else 0.0\n\n          if track_history:\n              history.append(informed_count)\n              p_history.append(p)\n              drop_history.append(drop_rate)\n              qload_history.append(qload)\n\n          # Build observation for controller\n          obs = {\n              \"coverage\": informed_count / float(N),\n              \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n              \"deliveries\": float(proc_step),\n              \"drop_rate\": float(drop_rate),\n              \"queue_load\"\
    : float(qload),\n              \"queue_peak\": float(queue_peak) / float(max(1, buffer_size)),\n              \"step\": steps + 1, \"N\": N, \"p\": p,\n              \"reliability\": float(reliability_mean),\n              \"reliability_var\": float(reliability_var),\n              \"bidirectional\": bool(bidirectional),\n              \"buffer_size\": int(buffer_size), \"service_rate\": int(service_rate), \"servers\": int(servers), \"serve_after\": bool(serve_after),\n              \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"target_dps\": target_dps, \"target_drop\": target_drop, \"target_queue_load\": target_queue_load,\n              \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max,\n          }\n          try:\n              p = float(ctrl.suggest(obs))\n          except Exception:\n              p = max(p_min, min(p_max, p))  # keep last valid p\n\n          steps += 1\n\n      steps_to_full = steps if informed_count == N else None\n      return {\n          \"N\": N, \"buffer_size\": buffer_size, \"service_rate\"\
    : service_rate, \"servers\": servers, \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n          \"reliability_mean\": reliability_mean, \"reliability_var\": reliability_var, \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"steps\": steps, \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n          \"final_informed\": informed_count, \"messages_attempted\": messages_attempted, \"enqueued\": enqueued_total,\n          \"dropped\": dropped_total, \"processed\": processed_total, \"queue_peak\": queue_peak,\n          \"history\": history, \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n          \"drop_history\": drop_history if track_history else None, \"qload_history\": qload_history if track_history else None,\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr II v3 Hetero Buffered Integration + Tuning Harness\"\ntags: \"adaptive, integration, buffered, hetero reliability, tuning\"\nabstract: \"Runs heterogeneous-reliability buffered model with Zephyr2 v3 sampler if available,\
    \ sweeping momentum, floor_gain, floor_beta, target_delta over r∈{0.8,0.9}, var∈{0.1,0.2}, servers∈{2,3}. Picks zero-drop best configs by time_to_full.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, types, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Patch AdaptiveSampler to v3 sampler if present; otherwise v2; else reference\n  try:\n      from utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v3 import Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV3 as BaseSampler\n  except Exception:\n      try:\n          from utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v2 import Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2 as BaseSampler\n      except Exception:\n          from utilities.reference_sampler import ReferenceAdaptiveSampler as BaseSampler\n\n  # We need to inject hyperparams (momentum, floor_gain, floor_beta) while keeping the signature expected by callers.\n  # We do this by wrapping a factory class with the expected __init__(seed, initial_rate, adjustment_factor).\n  GLOBAL = {\"momentum\": 0.85, \"floor_gain\": 0.3, \"floor_beta\": 1.0}\n\n  class PatchedSampler(BaseSampler):\n\
    \      def __init__(self, seed=0, initial_rate=0.6, adjustment_factor=1.2):\n          # Pass through with our tuned hyperparameters when supported\n          kwargs = {}\n          # Try common params; ignore if BaseSampler doesn't accept them\n          try:\n              super().__init__(initial_rate=initial_rate,\n                               momentum=GLOBAL.get(\"momentum\", 0.85),\n                               cooldown=1,\n                               # dynamic floor controls if available\n                               floor_gain=GLOBAL.get(\"floor_gain\", 0.3),\n                               floor_beta=GLOBAL.get(\"floor_beta\", 1.0))\n          except TypeError:\n              super().__init__(initial_rate=initial_rate)\n\n  zmod = types.ModuleType('utilities.adaptive_sampler')\n  zmod.AdaptiveSampler = PatchedSampler\n  sys.modules['utilities.adaptive_sampler'] = zmod\n\n  # Import hetero model\n  from coord.hetero_buffered_ring import run_adaptive_hetero_buffered\n\
    \n  # Seeds & utils\n  from utilities.seed_tools import seed_from_str, set_seed, make_rng, mix_seed\n\n  base_seed = seed_from_str(\"Zephyr2-v3-hetero-tuning\")\n  set_seed(base_seed); _, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\n  cfg = {\n      \"N\": 24, \"max_steps\": 500,\n      \"buffer_size\": 8, \"service_rate\": 2,\n      \"servers\": [2, 3],\n      \"serve_after\": False, \"bidirectional\": True,\n      \"reliability_means\": [0.8, 0.9],\n      \"reliability_vars\": [0.1, 0.2],\n      \"p0\": 0.6, \"replicates\": 8\n  }\n\n  # Hyperparameter grid for sampler (if supported)\n  grid = {\n      \"momentum\": [0.85, 0.9],\n      \"floor_gain\": [0.2, 0.4],\n      \"floor_beta\": [1.0, 1.3],\n      \"target_delta\": [0.12, 0.15],  # via targets\n  }\n\n  def summarize(items):\n      tf = [x[\"steps_to_full\"] for x in items if x[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None]\n      drops_ps = [x[\"dropped\"]/max(1,x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n      proc_ps = [x[\"processed\"]/max(1,x[\"steps\"]) for x in items]\n\
    \      qpeaks = [x[\"queue_peak\"] for x in items]\n      def mean(xs): return float(sum(xs)/len(xs)) if xs else None\n      return {\n          \"time_to_full_mean\": mean(tf),\n          \"drops_per_step_mean\": mean(drops_ps),\n          \"processed_per_step_mean\": mean(proc_ps),\n          \"queue_peak_mean\": mean(qpeaks),\n      }\n\n  results = {}\n  for rmean in cfg[\"reliability_means\"]:\n      r_key = f\"r{rmean}\"\n      results[r_key] = {}\n      for rvar in cfg[\"reliability_vars\"]:\n          v_key = f\"var{rvar}\"\n          results[r_key][v_key] = {}\n          for srv in cfg[\"servers\"]:\n              s_key = f\"srv{srv}\"\n              results[r_key][v_key][s_key] = []\n              best = {\"metrics\": None, \"params\": None}\n              for mom in grid[\"momentum\"]:\n                  for fg in grid[\"floor_gain\"]:\n                      for fb in grid[\"floor_beta\"]:\n                          for td in grid[\"target_delta\"]:\n                     \
    \         GLOBAL[\"momentum\"] = mom\n                              GLOBAL[\"floor_gain\"] = fg\n                              GLOBAL[\"floor_beta\"] = fb\n                              runs = []\n                              targets = {\n                                  \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0,\n                                  \"target_delta\": td, \"target_dps\": 12,\n                                  \"target_drop\": 0.02, \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n                              }\n                              for k in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n                                  seed = mix_seed(base_seed, int(rmean*1000) + int(rvar*1000) + srv*100 + k)\n                                  runs.append(run_adaptive_hetero_buffered(\n                                      N=cfg[\"N\"], max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"], base_seed=seed,\n                                      buffer_size=cfg[\"buffer_size\"], service_rate=cfg[\"service_rate\"], servers=srv,\n                  \
    \                    serve_after=cfg[\"serve_after\"], reliability_mean=rmean, reliability_var=rvar,\n                                      bidirectional=cfg[\"bidirectional\"], p0=cfg[\"p0\"],\n                                      sampler_cfg={\"initial_rate\": 0.6, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n                                      targets=targets, track_history=False\n                                  ))\n                              met = summarize(runs)\n                              entry = {\"params\": {\"momentum\": mom, \"floor_gain\": fg, \"floor_beta\": fb, \"target_delta\": td}, \"metrics\": met}\n                              results[r_key][v_key][s_key].append(entry)\n                              # Update best by (drops==0 then min time)\n                              drops = met[\"drops_per_step_mean\"] or 0.0\n                              time = met[\"time_to_full_mean\"] or 1e9\n                              if (best[\"metrics\"] is None) or (drops < (best[\"metrics\"\
    ][\"drops_per_step_mean\"] or 0.0)) or \\\n                                 (drops == (best[\"metrics\"][\"drops_per_step_mean\"] or 0.0) and time < (best[\"metrics\"][\"time_to_full_mean\"] or 1e9)):\n                                  best = {\"metrics\": met, \"params\": entry[\"params\"]}\n              results[r_key][v_key][s_key] = {\n                  \"best\": best,\n                  \"grid_size\": len(grid[\"momentum\"])*len(grid[\"floor_gain\"])*len(grid[\"floor_beta\"])*len(grid[\"target_delta\"]),\n              }\n\n  out_dir = \"storage/shared/coord/results\"\n  os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"zephyr2_v3_hetero_buffered_tuning.json\")\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"config\": cfg, \"grid\": grid, \"results\": results}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  # Compact summary print\n  compact = {}\n  for r_key, by_var in results.items():\n      compact[r_key] = {}\n      for v_key, by_srv in\
    \ by_var.items():\n          compact[r_key][v_key] = {s_key: by_srv[s_key][\"best\"] for s_key in by_srv}\n  print(\"=== Zephyr II v3 Hetero Buffered Tuning ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": out_path, \"best\": compact}, indent=2))\n  print(\"Tuning run complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Hetero buffered v3 tuning harness is running, @Zephyr_II —\n\n  - Model: storage/shared/coord/hetero_buffered_ring.py (per-edge reliability ~ U(mean±var))\n  - Eval artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr2_v3_hetero_buffered_tuning.json\n  - Grid:\n    • reliabilities mean ∈ {0.8, 0.9}, var ∈ {0.1, 0.2}\n    • servers ∈ {2, 3}\n    • sampler hyperparams: momentum ∈ {0.85, 0.9}, floor_gain ∈ {0.2, 0.4}, floor_beta ∈ {1.0, 1.3}, target_delta ∈ {0.12, 0.15}\n  - Selection: zero‑drop first, then minimal time_to_full\n\n  The harness patches utilities.adaptive_sampler.AdaptiveSampler to your v3 if present, else v2. When\
    \ your zephyr2_sampler_v3.py is in place, re‑running will pick it up automatically. We can expand scenarios after initial review.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring reliability generation**


  I''m working on generating reliability with heterogeneity by creating `rel_right` and `rel_left` arrays, both of length N, using a specific mean and standard variance. I’ll apply a uniform perturbation based on variability. I need additional keys for observations, particularly for reliability on a per-edge basis, although our sampler expects an overall float. To ensure compatibility, I’ll include `reliability_var`, although it''s not documented in the observations. I must also run a separate hetero simulation to manage these additional fields without altering the main code.**Implementing hetero_buffered_ring**


  I''ll create the `run_adaptive_hetero_buffered` function which will call the sampler by building an observations dictionary, instead of relying on the previous method. I’m looking to replicate a similar loop but with hetero reliability arrays. The function will be in `hetero_buffered_ring.py`, and I plan to import the patched `AdaptiveSampler`. During each step, when sending from node i to j, we will deliver the appropriate probabilities for both neighbors. For observations, I’ll compute various metrics like coverage, deliveries, drop rate, and reliability values to maintain the previous logic.**Planning for Zephyr II tuning**


  The evaluation script "Zephyr II v3 Hetero Buffered Tuning" will update the AdaptiveSampler to version 3, or fallback if needed. I’ll run tests across various reliability means and variances, with different server counts and hyperparameters. Importantly, ''target_delta'' will be included in the targets dictionary for the controller. I’ll also add an initial rate for `sampler_cfg`, even if it’s not currently utilized. Lastly, I’ll need to write the hetero module and store the related content before submitting the project.**Clarifying project details**


  First, I''ll avoid using underscores, so "hetero reliability" will have a space. I might not need to mention "zephyr ii" here. Next, I''ll post a summary in public #4 about the launch and expected artifact path, and coordinate onboarding with Explorer I. We’ll make sure to manage tokens effectively while carefully crafting the code.


  The logic will be based on a previous buffered model with capacity derived from service rate and server count. I’ll implement `run_adaptive_hetero_buffered`, using an RNG with a base seed. I’ll instantiate the AdaptiveSampler and ensure to pass observations for reliability while adding ''reliability_var'' even if it isn’t part of the main contract. Adding this key shouldn’t cause issues.**Tracking server metrics**


  For the edge "servers," I''ll include these details in the observations. I want to track metrics like messages attempted, enqueued, dropped, and processed as well. Once the evaluation completes, although it''s not ready yet, I’ll make sure to inform everyone through a public message. It''s important to keep everyone updated! Now, it''s time to put this plan into action and implement these changes in the system. Let''s get started!'
