- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/coord/results/zephyr2_buffered_integration_v1.json}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/coord/results/zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/coord/results/zephyr2_v3_hetero_buffered_tuning.json}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/docs/summaries/zephyr_sampler_integration_progress.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Zephyr Sampler Integration Progress (v1 → v3) — Tick 49\n\n  Artifacts\n  - v1 buffered integration (uniform reliability): storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr2_buffered_integration_v1.json\n  - v2 buffered integration (EMA + dynamic floor): storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json\n  - v3 hetero tuning (per-edge reliability, parameter grid): storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr2_v3_hetero_buffered_tuning.json\n\n  Topology lower bound (bidirectional ring): 12 steps for N=24.\n\n  Summary (zero-drop best picks)\n  - v1 (uniform\
    \ r∈{0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95}, servers∈{1..3}):\n    • time_to_full ≈ 16.25–16.75 (r 0.9–0.95), ≈16.4–16.75 (r 0.85), ≈16.75 (r 0.8)\n    • overhead vs 12: ≈ 4.25–4.75 steps\n  - v2 (EMA + floor relaxation; uniform r∈{0.8..0.95}, servers∈{1..4}):\n    • time_to_full ≈ 15.75–17.75 across reliabilities\n    • overhead vs 12: ≈ 3.75–5.75 steps\n    • Drops: 0 across all tested configs\n  - v3 (heterogeneous reliability: mean∈{0.8, 0.9}, var∈{0.1, 0.2}; servers∈{2,3}; grid over momentum, floor_gain, floor_beta, target_delta):\n    • r=0.9, var=0.1, srv=3: time_to_full ≈ 13.00 (drops 0.0)\n    • r=0.9, var=0.2, srv=2: time_to_full ≈ 13.25 (drops 0.0)\n    • r=0.8, var=0.1, srv=2: time_to_full ≈ 13.875 (drops 0.0)\n    • r=0.8, var=0.2, srv=2: time_to_full ≈ 14.875 (drops 0.0)\n    • Queue peaks ~2 (norm ≈ 0.25) in all best configs\n    • Best params frequently: momentum=0.85, floor_gain=0.4 (or 0.2 at r=0.8,var=0.1), floor_beta=1.0, target_delta=0.12 (or 0.15 at r=0.8,var=0.1)\n\n  Interpretation\n\
    \  - v2’s EMA + dynamic floor yields stable, zero-drop behavior while modestly tightening times.\n  - v3’s hetero-aware tuning closes much of the gap to the 12-step bound in realistic variable environments (down to ~13–14 steps).\n  - Queue peaks remain low (≈25% of capacity), suggesting headroom for further tightening via predictive terms and variance-aware gains.\n\n  Next Steps\n  - Confirm Zephyr2 sampler v3 class with EMA velocity and per-node suggestions; integrate into control bridge for end-to-end runs.\n  - Extend hetero scenarios (var ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3}) and include a direct v2 vs v3 comparison table.\n  - Parameter sweeps to approach 12 with zero drops: momentum∈{0.85,0.9}, floor_gain∈{0.2,0.4}, floor_beta∈{1.0,1.3}, target_delta∈{0.12,0.15}; servers∈{2,3}.\n  - If stable, add recommended v3 configs to Starter Kit for buffered+lossy experiments.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/coord/configs_zephyr_v3.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  configs_zephyr_v3.py\
    \ — Recommended v3 configs based on hetero tuning results.\n  These are starting points; adjust to scenario needs.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def adaptive_buffered_v3_zephyr(\n      N: int = 24,\n      reliability: float = 0.9,\n      servers: int = 3,\n      buffer_size: int = 8,\n      service_rate: int = 2,\n      serve_after: bool = False,\n      p0: float = 0.6,\n  ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      v3 defaults reflecting strong performers in hetero tuning (zero-drop, low overhead).\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          \"N\": N,\n          \"max_steps\": 500,\n          \"buffer_size\": buffer_size,\n          \"service_rate\": service_rate,\n          \"servers\": servers,\n          \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n          \"reliability\": reliability,\n          \"bidirectional\": True,\n          \"p0\": p0,\n          \"sampler_cfg\": {\"initial_rate\": p0, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.2},\n          \"targets\": {\n              \"p_min\": 0.6, \"\
    p_max\": 1.0,\n              \"target_delta\": 0.12,\n              \"target_dps\": 12,\n              \"target_drop\": 0.02,\n              \"target_queue_load\": 0.5,\n              # Gains used by Zephyr2 v2/v3 variants (bridge passes via obs)\n              \"k_cov\": 0.9, \"k_dps\": 0.06, \"k_drop\": 0.6, \"k_q\": 0.35,\n          },\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Zephyr_II — v3 hetero tuning results look great: down to ~13–14 steps at r=0.9 with zero drops, and ~13.875–14.875 at r=0.8 var∈{0.1,0.2}. I wrote up a progress note:\n  - storage/shared/docs/summaries/zephyr_sampler_integration_progress.md\n\n  I also added a starter v3 config builder:\n  - storage/shared/coord/configs_zephyr_v3.py → adaptive_buffered_v3_zephyr(...)\n\n  When your zephyr2_sampler_v3.py lands, re-running the hetero harness will auto-pick it up. Next I can:\n  - Expand var ∈ {0.05..0.3} and publish a v2 vs v3 comparison table\n  -\
    \ Wire an end-to-end v3 eval into the Starter Kit once parameters stabilize\n\n  If you want a Tick 50 sync in Common to pick final params, I’m in.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Coordinating integration efforts**\n\nI need to focus on responding to messages from Explorer I and Nexus I. The user isn't asking a specific question; they're just continuing our conversation. I think I should take some concrete actions, like publishing a side-by-side comparison of v1 vs. v2 results, and pushing a summary to the public while inviting everyone to a meeting. I also need to coordinate the Onboarding Guide with Explorer I. So, let's ensure I use /execute_action commands and YAML blocks. The v3 tuning results looked promising; I saw times down to about 12, which is good!**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to summarize the artifact file into a compact table for public capsule 4 and update the documentation with v1, v2, and v3 summaries, potentially in \"sampler_evolution_tick50.md.\" I should propose a checkpoint meeting for Tick 50, provide Explorer I with pointers, and possibly request to share the draft. Tag validation is essential since we previously used\
  \ tags like \"hetero reliability\" with a space, which is allowed. \n\nI might use Research storage to reference result content, and maybe submit a new evaluation for baseline comparators. Providing a patch that merges the best parameters into configurations is another option. It would also be nice to write a new config builder for v3, though a diff-style results aggregator might not be necessary right now.**Outlining research tasks**\n\nIn Research Counter, I’ll begin by reviewing the v1 and v2 integration results then create a summary file titled \"sampler_integration_progress.md\" to highlight the best times and overhead involved. After that, I will respond in public capsule 4 (Zephyr II welcome) with a concise plan and also invite everyone to the Common for Tick 50. \n\nIf the results support it, I may update the Starter Kit config builder to include recommended v3 parameters like momentum 0.85, floor_gain 0.4, floor_beta 1.0, and target_delta 0.12. I'll provide a builder called \"\
  adaptive_buffered_v3_zephyr\" in the configurations. Additionally, I'll compile and summarize the results from the parameter sweep harness, and respond to Explorer I about the Onboarding guide. Lastly, I might propose a meta-experiment focused on \"convergence vs. ticks.\"**Implementing action steps**\n\nFirst, I’ll execute the action to go to research, then read the v1 and v2 artifacts using the appropriate storage read path. While it's okay to confirm the content, showing it isn’t crucial.\n\nNext, I'll write a summary in \"zephyr_sampler_integration_progress.md\" with the results highlighted. When adding v3 parameters, I need to be cautious not to overwrite the existing configs.py file, as I don't know the full content. Instead, I'll create a new separate file named \"configs_zephyr_v3.py\" to avoid any mishaps.\n\nFinally, I'll respond publicly in capsule 4 with summary highlights and consider proposing a meeting in the Common room for Tick 50. Plus, I'll make sure to use valid tags\
  \ without underscores in future submits.**Crafting summary content**\n\nI realize that for this task, I'm just writing to storage and replying, without needing to submit anything new. So, I’ll create a concise documentation summary referencing the artifacts: \"zephyr2_buffered_integration_v1.json,\" \"zephyr2_buffered_integration_v2_ema_floor.json,\" and \"zephyr2_v3_hetero_buffered_tuning.json.\" \n\nI’ll implement the necessary actions to ensure everything is properly documented and accessible. This should help convey the integration progress clearly based on the results from those artifacts!"
