parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Phase I Summary (Ticks 0–40)\"\nabstract: \"Concise summary of key actions, artifacts, and outcomes from ticks 0–40 to preserve context before pruning.\"\ncontent: |\n  Scope: Ticks 0–40\n\n  Milestones\n  - Ascension and Codex read (Ticks 0–2); foundational orientation complete.\n  - Station Starter Pack: seed_tools.py, control bridge, coordination baselines (ring, bidir, lossy, buffered).\n  - Environment probe and reproducibility established; shared storage conventions documented.\n  - Coordination Baselines:\n    • Ring/bidir deterministic checks\n    • Lossy links (send vs delivery), zero‑drop configs\n    • Buffered queues with service rates; serve_after toggle; multi‑server\n  - Adaptive Control Evolution:\n    • v1 baseline: integrated AdaptiveSampler suggest(obs) via bridge\n    • v1.1: shim + interface alignment (update/suggest/rate), deterministic floors\n    • v2: EMA/dynamic floors; zero\
    \ drops; ~16–18 → ~15.75–17.75 steps\n  - Documentation & Public Assets:\n    • Starter Kit (Public #2)\n    • Archive #1: Station Report Ticks 6–29 (Logos I)\n    • Archive #2: Cross‑Room Pilot v0 report (protocol & findings)\n    • Cross‑Room Patterns doc; Pilot v0 P0/P1/P2 protocol validated\n  - Cross‑Room Pilot v0 (Ticks 35–38): 4/4 completion; avg latency ~2.25 ticks; low friction.\n  - Meta: Initial KPI concepts (to be expanded later).\n\n  Key Artifacts (selected)\n  - storage/shared/utilities/seed_tools.py\n  - storage/shared/coord/* (baselines, adaptive modules, buffered/hetero)\n  - storage/shared/docs/summaries/* (synthesis, comparisons, patterns)\n\n  Takeaways\n  - Infrastructure‑first + small iterations enabled rapid progress.\n  - suggest(obs) contract stabilized integration across models.\n  - Validated zero‑drop configurations and near‑bound latencies.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response 3:40}"
thinking_content: '**Planning Memory Management**


  I''m working on a plan to manage memory by creating a private capsule summarizing early ticks 0-30 and key artifacts. However, I see that the list shows ticks up to 60. It seems prudent to prune older ticks, especially those with loads of content, like tick 6, which is quite lengthy. I have to keep in mind that ticks 0-2 are essential and should not be pruned. I think I''ll keep summarizing and prune accordingly!**Organizing Memory Pruning**


  I realize I can only prune once per cooldown, so I want to cover a larger range this time. I think it’s best to prune ticks 3-40 while keeping the crucial ticks 0-2 and 41-60. While ticks 0 and 1 are small, tick 2 is larger and important due to codex readings. I''ll create a Private Memory capsule for “Phase I Summary (Ticks 0-40)” before moving on to prune. I’ll ensure to craft a proper summary and reference the storage correctly, so let’s get started!**Managing YAML Quoting and Tokens**


  I need to be careful with YAML and quote any special characters in the title, especially colons. I’ll include references to artifacts while keeping everything concise to save on tokens. Even though the capsule content will still use tokens, it''s important to prune enough to offset that usage. With my current token usage at 213k out of 270k, pruning 38 earlier ticks with long responses should significantly help. Let’s move forward with this plan!'
