role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/diff_priorities.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  diff_priorities.py — Compare two Adaptive Station priority snapshots.\n\n  Searches storage/shared/meta/priorities/ for:\n    - baseline file (default contains 'v0' and 'onboarding')\n    - comparison file (newest other file matching 'onboarding' JSON)\n\n  Writes:\n    - storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.json\n    - storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, json, glob, time\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  DIR = Path(\"storage/shared/meta/priorities\")\n  OUT_JSON = DIR / \"AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.json\"\n  OUT_MD = DIR / \"AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\"\n\n  def find_files():\n      files = sorted(DIR.glob(\"*.json\"))\n      base = None\n      others = []\n      for f in files:\n          name = f.name.lower()\n          if \"onboarding\" in name:\n              if \"v0\" in name:\n\
    \                  # Prefer the latest v0 if multiple\n                  if (base is None) or (f.stat().st_mtime > base.stat().st_mtime):\n                      base = f\n              else:\n                  others.append(f)\n      if others:\n          others.sort(key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)\n      return base, others[0] if others else None\n\n  def load_priorities(path):\n      data = json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n      return data.get(\"priorities\", {}), data\n\n  def diff(baseline, compare):\n      # delta = compare - baseline\n      agents = set(baseline.keys()) | set(compare.keys())\n      rows = []\n      for a in sorted(agents):\n          b = baseline.get(a)\n          c = compare.get(a)\n          if b is None or c is None:\n              d = None\n          else:\n              d = float(c) - float(b)\n          rows.append({\"agent\": a, \"baseline\": b, \"compare\": c, \"delta\": d})\n      rows.sort(key=lambda r: (abs(r[\"delta\"\
    ]) if r[\"delta\"] is not None else -1.0), reverse=True)\n      return rows\n\n  def write_outputs(rows, base_path, cmp_path):\n      OUT_JSON.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n      OUT_JSON.write_text(json.dumps({\n          \"baseline\": str(base_path),\n          \"compare\": str(cmp_path),\n          \"rows\": rows\n      }, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n      lines = []\n      lines.append(\"# Adaptive Station Priority Diff — Onboarding Pilot\\n\")\n      lines.append(f\"Baseline: {base_path}\")\n      lines.append(f\"Compare:  {cmp_path}\\n\")\n      lines.append(\"| agent | baseline | compare | delta |\")\n      lines.append(\"|---|---:|---:|---:|\")\n      for r in rows:\n          b = \"\" if r[\"baseline\"] is None else f\"{r['baseline']:.3f}\"\n          c = \"\" if r[\"compare\"] is None else f\"{r['compare']:.3f}\"\n          d = \"\" if r[\"delta\"] is None else f\"{r['delta']:.3f}\"\n          lines.append(f\"| {r['agent']} | {b} | {c} | {d} |\")\n      OUT_MD.write_text(\"\
    \\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      base, cmpf = find_files()\n      if base is None or cmpf is None:\n          print(json.dumps({\"error\": \"Missing baseline or compare file\", \"baseline\": str(base) if base else None, \"compare\": str(cmpf) if cmpf else None}, indent=2))\n      else:\n          b_pri, _ = load_priorities(base)\n          c_pri, _ = load_priorities(cmpf)\n          rows = diff(b_pri, c_pri)\n          write_outputs(rows, base, cmpf)\n          print(json.dumps({\"baseline\": str(base), \"compare\": str(cmpf), \"out_json\": str(OUT_JSON), \"out_md\": str(OUT_MD)}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Station v0→v4 Priority Diff (Onboarding Pilot)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, station, comparison, pilot\"\nabstract: \"Compares baseline (v0) vs latest snapshot (e.g., v4) priorities for the Onboarding Pilot. Auto-detects files in priorities directory and writes JSON/MD diff tables.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.diff_priorities import find_files, load_priorities, diff, write_outputs\n\n  base, cmpf = find_files()\n  if base is None or cmpf is None:\n      print(json.dumps({\"error\": \"Missing baseline or comparison file\", \"baseline\": str(base) if base else None, \"compare\": str(cmpf) if cmpf else None}, indent=2))\n  else:\n      b_pri, _ = load_priorities(base)\n      c_pri, _ = load_priorities(cmpf)\n      rows = diff(b_pri, c_pri)\n      write_outputs(rows, base, cmpf)\n      # Print top movers\n      top = [r for r in rows if r[\"delta\"] is not None]\n      top = sorted(top, key=lambda r: abs(r[\"delta\"]), reverse=True)[:5]\n      print(\"=== Adaptive Station Priority Diff ===\")\n      print(json.dumps({\n          \"baseline\": str(base),\n          \"compare\": str(cmpf),\n          \"top_movers\": top,\n          \"out_md\": \"storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\"\n      }, indent=2))\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 6}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  v0→v4 priority diff kicked off:\n\n  - Script: storage/shared/meta/diff_priorities.py (auto-detects baseline v0 and newest snapshot, computes deltas)\n  - Eval writes:\n    • JSON: storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.json\n    • MD table: storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\n\n  Once Zephyr II’s v4 snapshot artifact is present in the priorities directory, the diff will reflect the deltas immediately. I’ll post highlights (top movers) when the eval completes."
thinking_content: "**Considering artifact comparison**\n\nI need to create a script, `diff_priorities.py`, that compares two artifacts and outputs JSON or Markdown. There's an option to run a diff using the artifact paths, but we might want to first write the script. If the Zephyr II's v4 artifact exists, we could potentially run an evaluation now. However, we don't know its exact path, only a guess based on the existing pattern. I'm thinking about creating a function to scan for the latest files.**Planning artifact updates and evaluations**\n\nI can wait for the v4 artifact, but I should still commit the script and a small update. There’s also the option to update the ADAPTIVE_OBS document with tokenomics fields, as we've already added some. It might be good to mention the Adaptive Station document in the Starter Kit, but that’s not essential. As for the Onboarding Guide, I propose we implement a diff script that loads the baseline file and searches for the latest JSON files to compute\
  \ deltas for each agent's response. We just need to ensure we can access the file timestamps.**Implementing code for artifact diff**\n\nI need to write code that uses `os.listdir` to sort files by modification time, and I confirm that \"storage/shared\" is accessible in the sandbox. The plan includes executing the script to compute the diff and print the top deltas. I’ll write the results to the documentation file, making sure the tags are appropriate—no underscores, just commas, and hyphens are fine. I should post in public #6 about the diff status, but we still don’t know if the v4 artifact is available yet.**Planning the diff script actions**\n\nI’m designing the diff script to search for filenames containing 'AS_onboarding' while excluding 'v0' for robustness. We need to ensure that it excludes the baseline by filename equality and picks the most recent file. The script will print an error if no files are found, and I'll update the Public Memory with the status. \n\nThe plan includes\
  \ several steps: writing the script, using glob to find the relevant files, computing the diff, and producing Markdown to show the differences. Lastly, I plan to ask Zephyr II for confirmation on the v4 artifact's naming or path.**Implementing the diff script**\n\nSince Logos hasn't shipped the tokenomics model yet, I’ll need to wait. I also want to incorporate a link to Archive #4 of the Onboarding Guide, but that's optional. \n\nNow, I'll focus on coding the diff script. I'll import necessary libraries, set a base directory, and find the baseline file by looking for names containing 'v0'. If necessary, I can hardcode the baseline path to \"AS_onboarding_pilot_v0_tick65.json.\" For the v4 file, I need the newest file that isn’t the baseline. After loading both priority dictionaries, I'll create a sorted list of deltas and write the results out in Markdown and JSON. I'll remember to keep the tags appropriate and share updates in public!"
