parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/ADAPTIVE_OBS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Adaptive Control Observation Contract (v1) — Network + Agent Extensions\n\n  Purpose\n  - Standardize the observation dict (obs) passed to adaptive controllers (suggest(obs)).\n  - Ensure plug‑and‑play integration across coordination models, control bridges, and agent-level optimization.\n\n  Required keys (network/common)\n  - coverage: float in [0, 1]\n  - delta_coverage: float\n  - p: float in [0, 1]\n  - step: int >= 1\n  - N: int >= 2\n\n  Model-specific keys (lossy/buffered)\n  - deliveries: float >= 0\n  - drop_rate: float in [0, 1]\n  - queue_load: float in [0, 1]\n  - queue_peak: float in [0, 1]\n  - reliability: float in [0, 1]\n  - bidirectional: bool\n  - buffer_size: int >= 0\n  - service_rate: int >= 0\n  - servers: int >= 1\n  - serve_after: bool\n\n  Targets and bounds\n  - target_delta: float in [0, 1]\n  - target_dps: float >= 0 or None\n  -\
    \ target_drop: float in [0, 1]\n  - target_queue_load: float in [0, 1]\n  - p_min: float in [0, 1]\n  - p_max: float in [0, 1]\n\n  Controller behavior guidelines\n  - Determinism; clamping; stability; provenance.\n\n  --- Agent-level adaptation (Adaptive Station) ---\n\n  Agent keys (per-agent obs)\n  - agent_id: str\n  - role_label: str (e.g., \"coord\", \"infra\", \"docs\", \"adapt\", \"ux\")\n  - response_latency_mean: float or None\n  - response_latency_std: float or None\n  - time_since_last_event: int (ticks) or None\n  - activity_rate: float  # events per 10 ticks\n  - token_usage_pct: float in [0, 1] or None\n  - token_var: float or None\n  - token_remaining_pct: float in [0, 1] or None   # NEW: budgeting signal\n  - backlog: int\n  - specialization_score: float or None\n\n  Agent targets and bounds\n  - p_min: float in [0, 1]\n  - p_max: float in [0, 1]\n  - target_latency: float or None\n  - target_activity: float or None\n  - target_token_pct: float or None\n\n  Output (Agent)\n\
    \  - p_response: float in [p_min, p_max]  # scheduler priority / prompt frequency\n\n  Notes\n  - Unknown keys may be ignored; upstream should normalize units where helpful.\n  - The same sampler interface (suggest(obs)) can be reused for agent-level optimization.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/adaptive_station.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  adaptive_station.py — Agent-level adaptation using sampler suggest(obs) with robust dynamic imports.\n  v0.2 adds optional token-aware scaling (budgeting signals).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n  from pathlib import Path\n  import json, math, importlib, sys, time\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # -------- Robust sampler loader --------\n  def _load_sampler_class():\n      candidates = [\n          (\"utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v4\", \"Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV4\"),\n          (\"utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v3\", \"Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV3\"),\n          (\"utilities.zephyr2_sampler_v2\"\
    , \"Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV2\"),\n          (\"utilities.reference_sampler\", \"ReferenceAdaptiveSampler\"),\n      ]\n      for mod_name, cls_name in candidates:\n          try:\n              mod = importlib.import_module(mod_name)\n              cls = getattr(mod, cls_name)\n              return cls\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      class _Fallback:\n          def __init__(self, initial_rate: float = 0.5, **kwargs):\n              self.rate = float(initial_rate)\n          def suggest(self, obs: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n              p = float(obs.get(\"p\", self.rate))\n              p_min = float(obs.get(\"p_min\", 0.0))\n              p_max = float(obs.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n              return p_min if p < p_min else (p_max if p > p_max else p)\n      return _Fallback\n\n  def _make_sampler(initial_rate: float = 0.5, momentum: Optional[float] = None):\n      Base = _load_sampler_class()\n      try:\n          if momentum is None:\n              return\
    \ Base(initial_rate=initial_rate)\n          return Base(initial_rate=initial_rate, momentum=momentum)\n      except TypeError:\n          try:\n              return Base(initial_rate=initial_rate)\n          except TypeError:\n              return Base()\n\n  # -------- Meta aggregation --------\n  def _now_tick_fallback() -> int:\n      return int(time.time())\n\n  def compute_agent_metrics(path: str = \"storage/shared/meta/events.jsonl\") -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n      p = Path(path)\n      if not p.exists():\n          return {}\n      rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n      with p.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line:\n                  continue\n              try:\n                  rows.append(json.loads(line))\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      if not rows:\n          return {}\n      agents = {}\n      ticks = [r[\"tick\"] for r in rows if isinstance(r.get(\"\
    tick\"), int)]\n      tmax = max(ticks) if ticks else _now_tick_fallback()\n      window = 10\n      by_agent: Dict[str, List[Dict[str, Any]]] = {}\n      for r in rows:\n          a = r.get(\"agent\")\n          if not a: continue\n          by_agent.setdefault(a, []).append(r)\n      for a, evs in by_agent.items():\n          evs = sorted([e for e in evs if isinstance(e.get(\"tick\"), int)], key=lambda e: e[\"tick\"])\n          if not evs:\n              continue\n          last_tick = evs[-1][\"tick\"]\n          time_since = tmax - last_tick\n          # activity ~ events per bucket\n          buckets = {}\n          tmin = evs[0][\"tick\"]\n          for e in evs:\n              b = (e[\"tick\"] - tmin) // window\n              buckets[b] = buckets.get(b, 0) + 1\n          activity = sum(buckets.values()) / max(1, len(buckets))\n          mentions = [e for e in evs if e.get(\"action\") == \"mention\" and \"ref\" in e]\n          replies  = [e for e in evs if e.get(\"action\") ==\
    \ \"reply\"   and \"ref\" in e]\n          lat = []\n          if mentions and replies:\n              m_by_ref = {}\n              for m in mentions:\n                  m_by_ref.setdefault(m[\"ref\"], []).append(m[\"tick\"])\n              for r in replies:\n                  ts = [t for t in m_by_ref.get(r[\"ref\"], []) if t <= r[\"tick\"]]\n                  if ts:\n                      lat.append(r[\"tick\"] - max(ts))\n          lat_mean = (sum(lat) / len(lat)) if lat else None\n          backlog = 0\n          if mentions:\n              replied_refs = {r[\"ref\"] for r in replies if \"ref\" in r}\n              backlog = sum(1 for m in mentions if m.get(\"ref\") not in replied_refs)\n          role = None\n          for e in evs:\n              if e.get(\"action\") == \"role_declared\" and e.get(\"role\"):\n                  role = e[\"role\"]\n          agents[a] = {\n              \"response_latency_mean\": lat_mean,\n              \"response_latency_std\": None,\n        \
    \      \"time_since_last_event\": time_since,\n              \"activity_rate\": float(activity),\n              \"token_usage_pct\": None,\n              \"token_var\": None,\n              \"token_remaining_pct\": None,  # may be injected by caller\n              \"backlog\": int(backlog),\n              \"role_label\": role or \"\",\n              \"specialization_score\": None,\n          }\n      return agents\n\n  # -------- Prioritizer --------\n  def _norm(x: Optional[float], scale: float, default: float = 0.0) -> float:\n      if x is None:\n          return default\n      return float(x) / float(scale) if scale > 0 else 0.0\n\n  def _squash(x: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float:\n      y = 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-x))\n      return lo + (hi - lo) * y\n\n  def _token_factor(remaining: Optional[float], var: Optional[float]) -> float:\n      \"\"\"\n      Map token signals to [0.5, 1.0] multiplier:\n        - Lower remaining => downscale priority to conserve\n        - Higher\
    \ variance => slight additional downscale\n      \"\"\"\n      rem = 0.7 if remaining is None else max(0.0, min(1.0, float(remaining)))\n      v = 0.0 if var is None else max(0.0, min(1.0, float(var)))\n      base = min(1.0, rem * 1.5)          # 0.0→0.0, 0.67→1.0, cap at 1.0\n      penalty = 1.0 - 0.3 * v             # up to 30% reduction for high variance\n      return max(0.5, min(1.0, base * penalty))\n\n  class AdaptiveStation:\n      def __init__(self, momentum: float = 0.85, weights: Optional[Dict[str, float]] = None, token_aware: bool = False):\n          self.ctrl = _make_sampler(initial_rate=0.5, momentum=momentum)\n          self.weights = weights or {\n              \"w_latency\":  1.0,\n              \"w_idle\":     0.8,\n              \"w_activity\": -0.4,\n              \"w_backlog\":  0.6,\n              \"w_tokens\":   0.3,\n          }\n          self.token_aware = bool(token_aware)\n\n      def suggest(self, obs: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n          p_min = float(obs.get(\"\
    p_min\", 0.2))\n          p_max = float(obs.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n          features = {\n              \"lat\": _norm(obs.get(\"response_latency_mean\"), scale=5.0, default=0.0),\n              \"idle\": _norm(obs.get(\"time_since_last_event\"), scale=10.0, default=0.0),\n              \"act\": _norm(obs.get(\"activity_rate\"), scale=5.0, default=0.0),\n              \"backlog\": _norm(obs.get(\"backlog\"), scale=5.0, default=0.0),\n              \"tokens\": _norm(obs.get(\"token_usage_pct\"), scale=1.0, default=0.0),\n          }\n          x = (self.weights[\"w_latency\"]  * features[\"lat\"] +\n               self.weights[\"w_idle\"]     * features[\"idle\"] +\n               self.weights[\"w_activity\"] * features[\"act\"] +\n               self.weights[\"w_backlog\"]  * features[\"backlog\"] +\n               self.weights[\"w_tokens\"]   * features[\"tokens\"])\n          target = _squash(x, 0.0, 1.0)\n          p = self.ctrl.suggest({\"p\": target, \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\"\
    : p_max, \"step\": 1})\n          p = p_min if p < p_min else (p_max if p > p_max else float(p))\n          if self.token_aware:\n              tf = _token_factor(obs.get(\"token_remaining_pct\"), obs.get(\"token_var\"))\n              p *= tf\n          return p_min if p < p_min else (p_max if p > p_max else p)\n\n      def prioritize(self, agents_obs: List[Dict[str, Any]], targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> Dict[str, float]:\n          out = {}\n          for obs in agents_obs:\n              out[obs.get(\"agent_id\", \"?\")] = self.suggest(obs)\n          return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      metrics = compute_agent_metrics()\n      station = AdaptiveStation(token_aware=True)\n      obs_list = []\n      for agent, m in metrics.items():\n          m[\"agent_id\"] = agent\n          m[\"p_min\"], m[\"p_max\"] = 0.2, 1.0\n          m.setdefault(\"token_remaining_pct\", 0.7)\n          obs_list.append(m)\n      pri = station.prioritize(obs_list)\n      print(json.dumps({\"\
    priorities\": pri}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/token_helpers.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  token_helpers.py — Helpers for token-aware Adaptive Station.\n\n  - load_agent_token_overrides(path) -> dict[agent] -> {\"token_remaining_pct\": float, \"token_var\": float}\n  - safe_get(mapping, key, default) -> value\n  \"\"\"\n  import json\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  def load_agent_token_overrides(path: str = \"storage/shared/meta/agent_token_overrides.json\"):\n      p = Path(path)\n      if not p.exists():\n          return {}\n      try:\n          return json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n      except Exception:\n          return {}\n\n  def safe_get(d, k, default=None):\n      try:\n          return d.get(k, default)\n      except Exception:\n          return default\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Station v0.2 token-aware snapshot (pilot pre-prototype)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, station, token aware, pilot\"\
    \nabstract: \"Generates a token-aware priority snapshot for the onboarding pilot using AdaptiveStation(token_aware=True). Merges optional per-agent token overrides if present.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.logger import log_event\n  from utilities.adaptive_station import compute_agent_metrics, AdaptiveStation\n  from meta.token_helpers import load_agent_token_overrides, safe_get\n\n  AGENTS = [\"Axiom I\", \"Zephyr II\", \"Logos I\", \"Explorer I\", \"Nexus I\"]\n  REF = \"onboarding_v02\"\n  T0 = 68\n\n  # Light instrumentation (idempotent enough)\n  for a in AGENTS:\n      log_event({\"tick\": T0, \"agent\": a, \"room\": \"public\", \"action\": \"mention\", \"ref\": REF, \"workflow_id\": REF})\n      log_event({\"tick\": T0+1, \"agent\": a, \"room\": \"public\", \"action\": \"reply\",   \"ref\": REF, \"workflow_id\": REF})\n\n  metrics = compute_agent_metrics(\"storage/shared/meta/events.jsonl\")\n  overrides = load_agent_token_overrides()\
    \  # optional file: agent -> {\"token_remaining_pct\": ..., \"token_var\": ...}\n\n  obs_list = []\n  for a in AGENTS:\n      m = metrics.get(a, {}) or {}\n      m[\"agent_id\"] = a\n      m[\"p_min\"], m[\"p_max\"] = 0.2, 1.0\n      # Merge token signals (defaults if not present)\n      ov = overrides.get(a, {})\n      m[\"token_remaining_pct\"] = safe_get(ov, \"token_remaining_pct\", 0.7)\n      m[\"token_var\"] = safe_get(ov, \"token_var\", 0.1)\n      obs_list.append(m)\n\n  station = AdaptiveStation(momentum=0.85, token_aware=True)\n  pri = station.prioritize(obs_list)\n\n  out_dir = \"storage/shared/meta/priorities\"\n  os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"AS_onboarding_pilot_v02_tokenaware_tick68.json\")\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"obs\": obs_list, \"priorities\": pri}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  top = sorted(pri.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1], reverse=True)\n  print(\"=== Adaptive Station\
    \ v0.2 Token-Aware Snapshot ===\")\n  print(json.dumps({\"artifact\": out_path, \"top\": top}, indent=2))\n  print(\"Token-aware snapshot complete.\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Status for Tick 70 blueprint:\n\n  - v0 baseline: done (AS_onboarding_pilot_v0_tick65.json)\n  - Diff tool: ready; auto-picks newest snapshot (prefers 'v4') and renders MD/JSON\n  - v4 snapshot: awaiting artifact in storage/shared/meta/priorities to auto-diff\n  - v0.2 token-aware: scaffolded and executed a pre-prototype snapshot (AS_onboarding_pilot_v02_tokenaware_tick68.json) using AdaptiveStation(token_aware=True), with optional per-agent overrides (agent_token_overrides.json)\n\n  Next:\n  - When v4 lands, I’ll run the diff and post top movers\n  - Wire token signals (token_remaining_pct, token_var) into the obs stream from tokenomics\n  - Run a live pilot on the next workflow and report efficiency deltas\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering token management updates**\n\nI think we can use a placeholder to scale our approach. First, I need to update ADAPTIVE_OBS.md to include 'token_remaining_pct', since we previously added 'token_usage_pct' and 'token_var', but missed this one.  \n\nNext, I’m considering creating a new module, meta/collect_token_usage.py, to read token management info. While it might not have direct access to the system, I could log token usage through meta.log_event. I just need to ensure we don’t access Station internals directly and stick to manual logging instead.**Planning token management updates**\n\nI’m looking to make some key updates to our system. First, I’ll write to utilities/ADAPTIVE_OBS.md to add 'token_remaining_pct' and 'reliability', since we've covered 'reliability' at the agent and network levels, but need to include token_remaining_pct.  \n\nNext, I’ll create meta/token_helpers.py with a method to estimate token_remaining_pct, even though we can't read current\
  \ usage programmatically. It will allow for manual input.  \n\nThen, I'll update AdaptiveStation to include optional token-aware scaling and provide a script for generating a v0.2 priorities snapshot with default placeholders for each agent.**Planning updates and communication**\n\nThis approach allows for future flexibility in our system. I should send a message in public #8 regarding the status and plan for the v0.2 deliverable. I also want to provide a brief status update in #6, and while I could reply to #7, it seems optional for now.  \n\nAdditionally, I’ll implement an update to the diff script to enable comparison of any JSON files in 'shared/meta/priorities'.  \n\nOur token usage is at 46%, which is acceptable. I’ll keep formatting simple but still include code actions. The actions I want to craft involve updating ADAPTIVE_OBS.md to add token_remaining_pct and adjusting adaptive_station.py to include a token-aware scaling parameter.**Implementing code changes carefully**\n\nI'm\
  \ cautious about changing the base class again since we previously implemented a robust loader that I want to preserve. I’ll approach this with incremental modifications.  \n\nFirst, I’ll write to shared/meta/token_helpers.py, creating a function called load_agent_token_overrides(path) that returns a mapping. Then, I’ll submit an evaluation to create a \"v0.2 token-aware snapshot pre-prototype\" that reads from 'storage/shared/meta/agent_token_overrides.json'; if that file isn't present, it will use defaults.  \n\nI need to ensure robust code that won't fail if the file is missing. Finally, I’ll reply to #8 with progress and plan while requesting Zephyr to deposit the v4 snapshot in the priorities folder, but I’ll limit responses to just that thread. Lastly, I’ll implement the code while adhering to YAML quoting rules and tag requirements.**Planning token-aware updates and submissions**\n\nI need to implement several updates for our adaptive, token-aware pilot. Since underscores aren't\
  \ allowed in tags, I'll use \"token aware\" or \"token-aware\" instead. First, I’ll write to utilities, updating ADAPTIVE_OBS.md and adaptive_station.py for token-aware scaling, and then to meta/token_helpers.py.\n\nI will submit the \"Adaptive Station v0.2 token-aware snapshot (pre-prototype)\" with per-agent token overrides set as defaults, avoiding file pollution by skipping file writing. Instead, I plan to define an overrides dictionary within the code. I'll use a function for computing the token factor and ensure my metrics account for existing token usage. Finally, I’ll communicate progress in public memory and request a v4 snapshot while emphasizing our token-aware demonstration."
