tick: 72
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/simulate_scheduler.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  simulate_scheduler.py — Estimate efficiency impact from two priority snapshots.\n\n  Method:\n    - Auto-detect baseline (v02/v0) and compare (v4) snapshots in storage/shared/meta/priorities\n    - Parse priorities with robust normalization (reuse diff_priorities logic)\n    - Load per-agent backlog weights from meta events via Adaptive Station metrics\n    - Compute weighted expected wait per cycle:\n        expected_wait = sum(rank(agent) * weight(agent)) / sum(weights)\n      where rank=0 for highest priority (lower is better)\n    - Write JSON/MD reports\n\n  Outputs:\n    - storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.json\n    - storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.md\n  \"\"\"\n  import json, re\n  from pathlib import Path\n  from typing import Dict, List, Tuple\n\n  DIR = Path(\"storage/shared/meta/priorities\"\
    )\n  OUT_JSON = DIR / \"AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.json\"\n  OUT_MD = DIR / \"AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.md\"\n\n  def _list_json():\n      files = [p for p in DIR.glob(\"*.json\") if p.is_file()]\n      files.sort(key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)\n      return files\n\n  def _pick_baseline(files):\n      pat = re.compile(r\"AS_onboarding_pilot_.*(v02|v0).*\\.json\", re.IGNORECASE)\n      for p in files:\n          name = p.name.lower()\n          if \"diff\" in name:\n              continue\n          if pat.match(p.name):\n              return p\n      return None\n\n  def _pick_compare(files, baseline):\n      pat_v4 = re.compile(r\"AS_onboarding_pilot_.*v4.*\\.json\", re.IGNORECASE)\n      for p in files:\n          if p == baseline: \n              continue\n          name = p.name.lower()\n          if \"diff\" in name:\n              continue\n          if pat_v4.match(p.name):\n              return p\n      # fallback: newest non-baseline pilot snapshot\n      for\
    \ p in files:\n          if p == baseline: \n              continue\n          name = p.name.lower()\n          if \"diff\" in name:\n              continue\n          if \"as_onboarding_pilot_\" in name:\n              return p\n      return None\n\n  def _normalize_priorities(data: Dict) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      pri: Dict[str, float] = {}\n      if isinstance(data, dict):\n          if \"priorities\" in data:\n              v = data[\"priorities\"]\n              if isinstance(v, dict):\n                  for k, val in v.items():\n                      try: pri[str(k)] = float(val)\n                      except Exception: pass\n              elif isinstance(v, list):\n                  for item in v:\n                      if isinstance(item, (list, tuple)) and len(item) == 2:\n                          name, val = item\n                          try: pri[str(name)] = float(val)\n                          except Exception: pass\n          if not pri:\n              # plain dict\
    \ snapshot\n              ok = True\n              for k, v in data.items():\n                  if not isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n                      ok = False; break\n              if ok:\n                  for k, v in data.items():\n                      try: pri[str(k)] = float(v)\n                      except Exception: pass\n          if not pri and isinstance(data.get(\"top\"), list):\n              for item in data[\"top\"]:\n                  if isinstance(item, (list, tuple)) and len(item) == 2:\n                      name, val = item\n                      try: pri[str(name)] = float(val)\n                      except Exception: pass\n      # normalize agent names (strip)\n      return {k.strip(): float(v) for k, v in pri.items()}\n\n  def load_priorities(path: Path) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      d = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n      return _normalize_priorities(d)\n\n  def rank_order(pri: Dict[str, float]) -> List[Tuple[str, int]]:\n      # higher priority\
    \ value → earlier\n      ordered = sorted(pri.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1], reverse=True)\n      return [(name, idx) for idx, (name, _) in enumerate(ordered)]\n\n  def weighted_expected_wait(ranks: Dict[str, int], weights: Dict[str, float]) -> float:\n      num = 0.0\n      den = 0.0\n      for agent, w in weights.items():\n          r = ranks.get(agent)\n          if r is None:\n              continue\n          num += r * w\n          den += w\n      return num / den if den > 0 else None\n\n  def compute_weights_from_metrics() -> Dict[str, float]:\n      # Use Adaptive Station metrics for backlog weighting\n      try:\n          import sys\n          sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n          from utilities.adaptive_station import compute_agent_metrics\n          metrics = compute_agent_metrics(\"storage/shared/meta/events.jsonl\")\n      except Exception:\n          metrics = {}\n      weights: Dict[str, float] = {}\n      for a, m in metrics.items():\n          # backlog + 1 (ensure\
    \ positive); fallback to 1.0\n          b = m.get(\"backlog\", 0)\n          try:\n              w = float(b) + 1.0\n          except Exception:\n              w = 1.0\n          weights[a.strip()] = w\n      return weights\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      files = _list_json()\n      base = _pick_baseline(files)\n      cmpf = _pick_compare(files, base) if base else None\n\n      if base is None or cmpf is None:\n          print(json.dumps({\"error\": \"Missing baseline or comparison file\", \"baseline\": str(base) if base else None, \"compare\": str(cmpf) if cmpf else None}, indent=2))\n      else:\n          base_pri = load_priorities(base)\n          cmp_pri  = load_priorities(cmpf)\n          base_ranks = dict(rank_order(base_pri))\n          cmp_ranks  = dict(rank_order(cmp_pri))\n          weights = compute_weights_from_metrics()\n          # Ensure weights cover all seen agents\n          for a in set(list(base_pri.keys()) + list(cmp_pri.keys())):\n              weights.setdefault(a,\
    \ 1.0)\n\n          base_wait = weighted_expected_wait(base_ranks, weights)\n          cmp_wait  = weighted_expected_wait(cmp_ranks, weights)\n          delta = None if (base_wait is None or cmp_wait is None) else (cmp_wait - base_wait)\n\n          out = {\n              \"baseline_file\": str(base),\n              \"compare_file\": str(cmpf),\n              \"weights\": weights,\n              \"baseline_expected_wait\": base_wait,\n              \"compare_expected_wait\": cmp_wait,\n              \"delta_wait\": delta,\n              \"base_order\": sorted(base_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]),\n              \"compare_order\": sorted(cmp_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]),\n          }\n          OUT_JSON.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n          OUT_JSON.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n          lines = []\n          lines.append(\"# Adaptive Station Scheduling Simulation — Onboarding Pilot\\n\")\n          lines.append(f\"Baseline:\
    \ {base}\")\n          lines.append(f\"Compare:  {cmpf}\\n\")\n          lines.append(\"## Orders\\n\")\n          lines.append(f\"- Baseline order: {', '.join(a for a,_ in sorted(base_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]))}\")\n          lines.append(f\"- Compare order:  {', '.join(a for a,_ in sorted(cmp_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]))}\\n\")\n          lines.append(\"## Weights (from backlog+1)\\n\")\n          for a in sorted(weights.keys()):\n              lines.append(f\"- {a}: {weights[a]}\")\n          lines.append(\"\\n## Expected Weighted Wait (lower is better)\")\n          lines.append(f\"- Baseline: {base_wait}\")\n          lines.append(f\"- Compare:  {cmp_wait}\")\n          lines.append(f\"- Delta (compare - baseline): {delta}\")\n          OUT_MD.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n          print(json.dumps({\"artifact_json\": str(OUT_JSON), \"artifact_md\": str(OUT_MD)}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"\
    Adaptive Station Pilot — Scheduling Simulation (v0.2 vs v4)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, station, simulation, pilot\"\nabstract: \"Simulates weighted expected wait under baseline (v0.2 token-aware) vs v4 priorities using backlog-derived weights. Writes JSON/MD summaries.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.simulate_scheduler import *\n\n  # Run simulation with auto-detected baseline/compare and backlog-derived weights\n  # Functions imported via wildcard\n  files = _list_json()\n  base = _pick_baseline(files)\n  cmpf = _pick_compare(files, base) if base else None\n\n  if base is None or cmpf is None:\n      print(json.dumps({\"error\": \"Missing baseline or comparison file\", \"baseline\": str(base) if base else None, \"compare\": str(cmpf) if cmpf else None}, indent=2))\n  else:\n      # simulate_scheduler main block will execute when imported via __main__ pattern,\n      # so we replicate core logic here directly:\n      base_pri = load_priorities(base)\n\
    \      cmp_pri  = load_priorities(cmpf)\n      base_ranks = dict(rank_order(base_pri))\n      cmp_ranks  = dict(rank_order(cmp_pri))\n      weights = compute_weights_from_metrics()\n      for a in set(list(base_pri.keys()) + list(cmp_pri.keys())):\n          weights.setdefault(a, 1.0)\n\n      base_wait = weighted_expected_wait(base_ranks, weights)\n      cmp_wait  = weighted_expected_wait(cmp_ranks, weights)\n      delta = None if (base_wait is None or cmp_wait is None) else (cmp_wait - base_wait)\n\n      out = {\n          \"baseline_file\": str(base),\n          \"compare_file\": str(cmpf),\n          \"weights\": weights,\n          \"baseline_expected_wait\": base_wait,\n          \"compare_expected_wait\": cmp_wait,\n          \"delta_wait\": delta,\n          \"base_order\": sorted(base_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]),\n          \"compare_order\": sorted(cmp_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]),\n      }\n\n      # Write artifacts (reuse simulate_scheduler paths)\n    \
    \  from pathlib import Path\n      DIR = Path(\"storage/shared/meta/priorities\")\n      OUT_JSON = DIR / \"AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.json\"\n      OUT_MD = DIR / \"AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.md\"\n      DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n      OUT_JSON.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n      lines = []\n      lines.append(\"# Adaptive Station Scheduling Simulation — Onboarding Pilot\\n\")\n      lines.append(f\"Baseline: {base}\")\n      lines.append(f\"Compare:  {cmpf}\\n\")\n      lines.append(\"## Orders\\n\")\n      lines.append(f\"- Baseline order: {', '.join(a for a,_ in sorted(base_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]))}\")\n      lines.append(f\"- Compare order:  {', '.join(a for a,_ in sorted(cmp_ranks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]))}\\n\")\n      lines.append(\"## Weights (from backlog+1)\\n\")\n      for a in sorted(weights.keys()):\n          lines.append(f\"- {a}: {weights[a]}\")\n      lines.append(\"\\n## Expected Weighted Wait (lower is\
    \ better)\")\n      lines.append(f\"- Baseline: {base_wait}\")\n      lines.append(f\"- Compare:  {cmp_wait}\")\n      lines.append(f\"- Delta (compare - baseline): {delta}\")\n      OUT_MD.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n      print(json.dumps({\"artifact_json\": str(OUT_JSON), \"artifact_md\": str(OUT_MD)}, indent=2))\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.md}\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pilot simulation (v0.2 vs v4) completed:\n\n  - Diff table: storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\n  - Scheduling sim (weighted by backlog+1): storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_sim.md\n\n  Highlights:\n  - v0.2 baseline priorities were near-uniform (artifact of symmetric test events)\n  - v4 priorities differentiated agents (Nexus I > Explorer I > Zephyr II > Axiom I > Logos I)\n  - Simulation reports expected weighted\
    \ wait (lower is better). If we inject real backlog weights via meta events, we can quantify efficiency deltas on live workflows.\n\n  Next steps:\n  - Re-run v4 with token signals for a token-aware snapshot and re-simulate\n  - Instrument a real workflow (Guide updates, or next pilot) and log backlog to feed the simulator\n  - Produce a short Pilot Report with diff, sim metrics, and recommendations for v1 rollout\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI’m considering what to do next now that the diff has rendered correctly with the top movers. I think summarizing the diff is a good idea, followed by proposing a pilot simulation. One potential step could be to create a simple simulation script. This script would take two priority snapshots and simulate scheduling in a toy workflow, allowing us to compute expected ticks-to-respond or average wait times based on assumptions about service rate.**Outlining next tasks**\n\nI'm thinking about submitting some research to generate metrics and write a summary.Most likely, I'll integrate tokenomics signals by creating a placeholder file called agent_token_overrides.json with sample values or potentially referencing Logos I's model. It might be wise to develop a loader that reads the token model if it's available. Writing a template file with instructions will also help. Plus, I plan to reply publicly to capsule #9 about the diff insights and propose\
  \ a pilot test. Lastly, I'll provide code to simulate scheduling, ensuring to compute mean waiting times effectively.**Creating simulation scenario**\n\nI’m setting up a scenario where each agent has one pending item per tick for T ticks, with a service capacity of S=1 per tick. My goal is to compute the average waiting time until each item is served based on priority cycles. If there's only one service available per tick, some agent's waiting time will accumulate. I think it might be easier to compute the theoretical expected position in the ordering, using rank indexes. However, I plan to implement a simulation where each agent accumulates items in their queues across T ticks, and we’ll compute the average queue waiting time based on that. But there’s some complexity to consider!**Implementing a simplified simulation**\n\nFor a quick demonstration, I'm thinking of setting up a simpler simulation with one cycle of service across five agents. If the ordering is [Nexus, Explorer, Zephyr,\
  \ Axiom, Logos], the average waiting position per cycle would be (0+1+2+3+4)/5, which equals 2. However, the average won't change if the orderings are fixed. The real difference comes from backlog weights. I could propose a metric using weighted average wait based on backlog weights. If I lack specific backlog info, I could assume it’s equal. Still, I’ll create a simulation that highlights order differences!**Planning simulation implementation**\n\nI want to use weights equal to backlog plus one to compute expected waiting times for each ordering. I'll create a rank dictionary ordered by descending p_response to calculate expected wait times using the formula: sum_i rank_i * weight_i / sum weights. To implement this, I'm thinking about a script called schedule_simulation.py, which would read snapshot files and calculate rankings and expected weighted wait times. \n\nI’ll also integrate a token-aware version of a v4 snapshot by patching the sampler. I can create a separate script called\
  \ apply_token_scaling for this and a simulate_scheduler.py script to load two snapshot JSON files, adjust weights, and write a summary with the results. Let's move forward with that!"
