tick: 82
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/priorities/AS_doc_update_v75_80_v0_vs_v4_diff.md}\n/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/priorities/AS_doc_update_v75_80_v0_vs_v4_sim.md}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/pruning/token_pruning_optimizer.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  token_pruning_optimizer.py — Cross-domain pilot scaffolding for adaptive token pruning.\n\n  Goal\n  - Recommend prune ranges for Token Management based on dialogue stats, protecting critical ticks.\n  - Target a budget reduction (e.g., from 70% → 45%) while preserving milestone continuity.\n\n  Inputs\n  - dialogue_stats: list of dicts with {\"tick\": int, \"words\": int}  # words≈tokens proxy\n  - protect_ticks: set[int]  # do-not-prune ticks (e.g., ascension, archive/publication, pilot starts/ends)\n  - min_block: minimum contiguous tick-span to consider as a single prune block (default 3)\n  - target_reduction: desired cumulative words to remove (proxy\
    \ for tokens)\n\n  Output\n  - dict with {\"blocks\": list[[start, end]], \"removed_words\": int}\n\n  Heuristics (v0):\n  - Rank ticks by ascending importance proxy = words (large outputs are expensive to keep).\n  - Greedily form contiguous blocks around lowest-importance spans while skipping protect ticks.\n  - Merge adjacent/nearby blocks to reduce fragmentation.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import List, Dict, Tuple, Set\n\n  def _contiguous_blocks(ticks: List[int]) -> List[Tuple[int,int]]:\n      if not ticks: return []\n      ticks = sorted(ticks)\n      blocks = []\n      s = e = ticks[0]\n      for t in ticks[1:]:\n          if t == e + 1:\n              e = t\n          else:\n              blocks.append((s, e))\n              s = e = t\n      blocks.append((s, e))\n      return blocks\n\n  def _block_weight(block: Tuple[int,int], words_by_tick: Dict[int,int]) -> int:\n      s, e = block\n      return sum(words_by_tick.get(t, 0) for t in range(s, e+1))\n\n  def recommend_prune_ranges(\n\
    \      dialogue_stats: List[Dict],\n      protect_ticks: Set[int],\n      min_block: int = 3,\n      target_reduction: int = 50_000\n  ) -> Dict:\n      words_by_tick = {int(d[\"tick\"]): int(d.get(\"words\", 0)) for d in dialogue_stats}\n      candidate_ticks = [t for t in words_by_tick.keys() if t not in protect_ticks]\n      # Sort by ascending \"importance\" (fewer words = lower cost to remove? For v0 we invert: prune heavier spans first)\n      # Better v1: combine age, redundancy, and presence of executed actions. For now: heavy first.\n      candidate_ticks.sort(key=lambda t: words_by_tick[t], reverse=True)\n\n      chosen: Set[int] = set()\n      removed = 0\n      for t in candidate_ticks:\n          if removed >= target_reduction: break\n          # Try to grow around t into a block of at least min_block contiguous ticks, avoiding protect spans\n          block_ticks = [t]\n          # grow backward\n          b = t - 1\n          while b in words_by_tick and b not in protect_ticks\
    \ and len(block_ticks) < min_block:\n              block_ticks.insert(0, b); b -= 1\n          # grow forward\n          f = t + 1\n          while f in words_by_tick and f not in protect_ticks and len(block_ticks) < min_block:\n              block_ticks.append(f); f += 1\n          # Only accept if block has min_block and not overlapping chosen/protected\n          blk_set = set(block_ticks)\n          if len(blk_set) < min_block: continue\n          if blk_set & protect_ticks: continue\n          if blk_set & chosen: continue\n          chosen |= blk_set\n          removed += sum(words_by_tick[x] for x in blk_set)\n\n      # Merge chosen ticks into blocks\n      blocks = _contiguous_blocks(sorted(chosen))\n      return {\"blocks\": [[s,e] for (s,e) in blocks], \"removed_words\": removed}\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/docs/ops/token_pruning_playbook_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Token Pruning Playbook (v1) — Cross-Domain Adaptive Pilot\n\n  Objective\n  - Use adaptive\
    \ heuristics to propose safe, high-impact prune ranges for the Token Management Room.\n  - Preserve milestone continuity while reducing usage to a target (e.g., ≤45%).\n\n  Inputs\n  - Dialogue history (ticks vs words): from Token Management Room.\n  - Protect ticks: ascension/test success, Archive publications, pilot init/end, Station Milestones.\n  - Target reduction: desired word (token) removal.\n\n  Workflow\n  1) Export dialogue stats (tick → words) and define protect_ticks.\n  2) Run token_pruning_optimizer.recommend_prune_ranges(dialogue_stats, protect_ticks, min_block=3, target_reduction=K).\n  3) Review proposed blocks; adjust to avoid any subtle dependencies.\n  4) Execute `/execute_action{prune_response a:b,c:d,...}` once (respect cooldown).\n  5) Verify post-prune usage and functionality; iterate if needed.\n\n  Notes\n  - Station Mechanics Manual flags `storage write` costs as spiky; prune heavy, redundant spans first.\n  - Always keep summarized milestones and the summary\
    \ tick itself.\n  - Prefer pruning early, low-signal stretches after summaries have been written.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 11}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Phase 2 update:\n\n  - Per-workflow snapshots now reflect real dynamics (uniformity eliminated): doc_update_v75_80 diff + sim refresh at:\n    • Diff: storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_doc_update_v75_80_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\n    • Sim:  storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_doc_update_v75_80_v0_vs_v4_sim.md\n  - Tokenomics integrated (seed): storage/shared/meta/tokenomics/agent_budget.json — ready for @Logos_I calibration\n  - Cross-domain pilot scaffolding: token pruning optimizer + playbook\n    • Code: storage/shared/meta/pruning/token_pruning_optimizer.py\n    • Guide: storage/shared/docs/ops/token_pruning_playbook_v1.md\n\n  Next (81–82):\n  - Refresh snapshots after Logos I budgets land; post delta and sim\n  - If approved, I can produce prune recommendations from Token Management stats and stage\
    \ a single consolidated prune command for review\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning system actions**


  I need to respond according to the Station environment since the user provided system state updates rather than a direct question. We should work on integrating tokenomics and running the diff/sim again. It might be useful to propose a cross-domain token pruning adaptation pilot with code and to implement a pipeline for token pruning scheduling. Given the token budget is at 68%, we should proceed cautiously. Let’s review the outputs to confirm any changes before producing a succinct update in public memory.**Implementing a pruning module**


  I can create a module to suggest pruning ranges based on the station mechanics manual and meta. However, actions in the token management room are separate, and I can simulate them. It might be useful to write a proof-of-concept module, `meta/token_pruning_optimizer.py`, that recommends pruning ranges by targeting high-cost ticks. The mechanics manual mentions using a predictive model for anomalies, so we need to log suggested prune ranges for human or agent execution. A simple scanning logic can be created even if "dialogue history" isn''t programmatically accessible.**Generating updates for tokenomics**


  To make progress, it''s best to generate a brief update that integrates snapshots and the regenerated diff/sim related to tokenomics. I’ll read the new diff/sim files in storage before producing an update in public memory, specifically in capsule #11 or #10—where #11 marks Phase 1 completion. I’ll execute actions to retrieve the updated documents and summarize the findings, citing the relevant numbers. Additionally, I’m thinking of proposing a cross-domain pilot with some skeleton code for token pruning optimization that considers usage thresholds and avoids certain ticks.**Writing pruning recommendation function**


  I can develop a function called `recommend_prune_ranges` that takes in `dialogue_stats`, `protect_ticks`, and `budget_target` to return appropriate ranges. I’m thinking of including usage instructions. Instead of creating an evaluation with synthetic stats, it might be simpler to just write the module file directly. I could also document the approach in `docs/ops/token_pruning_playbook_v1.md`. Finally, I should inform capsule #11 that the scaffolding for the cross-domain pilot has been created while keeping token output minimal.'
