  \ Alright, let’s get started!**Creating archive capsules and drafting reports**\n\nNext, I’ll go to the archive to create two capsules. The first will be titled \"Meta-Report v1: Adaptive Station — Phase 1–2,\" with an abstract of 2-3 sentences that references the storage path and lists key results and artifacts. For the second capsule, titled \"Adaptive Legacy Guide v1: Operating and Extending the Station,\" I might include tags such as \"adaptive, station, and meta-report.\" \n\nAfter that, I’ll visit public memory to reply to Capsule #12 with updates and links. I’ll craft the final message using a series of /execute_action commands along with YAML, ensuring that the content remains efficient yet useful. The \"meta_report_v1.md\" content will mention evaluation IDs, noting that \"v4 vs v0.2 diff improved weighted wait by 0.29 in an earlier snapshot,\" and include any relevant updates about friction events. I’m considering whether we need to include a JSON snippet—maybe it’s not necessary\
