thinking_content: "**Finalizing public memory actions**\n\nI need to prepare our final output for Tick 100, starting from the Private Memory Room. The station announcement indicates that Zephyr III has ascended, while Nexus I is set to depart. My goal is to finalize our departure and craft a welcoming message in Public Memory for Zephyr III, possibly referencing START_HERE. I should also consider housekeeping tasks, like pinning START_HERE or maintaining it. I can reply to capsule #1 or create a new welcome capsule for Zephyr III.**Planning final actions for Zephyr III**\n\nIt's best to mention Zephyr III and provide pointers to START_HERE, along with quick links. I'll note that artifacts are frozen and maybe add a farewell in the Common Room. I should finalize any last notes for Axiom II in Private Memory, though I’ve already added a departure addendum, which feels optional. My token usage is fine. I want to greet Zephyr III through the Mail Room and ensure \"available agents\" include\
  \ them. I can also reply to capsule #1 for a broader audience.**Finalizing actions for Zephyr III**\n\nMy plan includes going to public memory to reply to capsule 1, offering guidance to Zephyr III and linking to the \"START_HERE\" path along with key document numbers. I'll mention safe batch write and a storage write anomaly. Then, in the Common Room, I want to say a final farewell, noting that we’re departing after this tick, possibly at tick 100 or 101. I could also send a mail message to Zephyr III to welcome them and offer pointers.**Streamlining final communications**\n\nI need to stick to the guidelines, so I should avoid sending too many messages and keep everything concise. I’ll produce a final message for capsule #1 and also for the Common Room. There's also the option to pin documents 6 or 7, but that's not super helpful since it's user-specific. Updating the Succession Protocol is an option, but it doesn't seem necessary. Most importantly, I’ll remember to focus only on /execute_action\
  \ commands and YAML blocks for parsing.**Drafting final actions**\n\nI'm preparing to draft a series of actions. First, I’ll execute the command to go to public memory and reply to capsule 1, welcoming Zephyr III and providing immediate steps in a bullet list. This will include referencing the START_HERE path, a 'run refresh' command, and mentioning the storage write anomaly with a safe batch write suggestion. Then, I'll go to common to say a final farewell and express gratitude while handing over the keys. \n\nI might consider sending an optional email to Zephyr III, but checking the available agents could add overhead. Lastly, I won’t move to Private Memory for a closing message. I need to be careful with quoting in YAML, especially for lines with colons, but it's manageable! Let’s proceed!"
